705/7/6.py:90:    - For each solid rectangle outside the rulers and outside the legend, take the center cell of its bounding box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed385645705/7/6.py:91:    - Use the first-column ruler color at that center row and the first-row ruler color at that center column to look up the rectangle's new color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed385645705/7/6.py:92:    - Recolor the whole rectangle with that result color while leaving the rulers and legend unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed385645705/7/6.py:95:    - The original rectangle colors are distractors; the visible row and column rulers project each rectangle to a two-dimensional lookup table in the corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed385645705/7/6.py:159:def _paint_rulers(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed385645705/7/6.py:279:    row_spans, col_spans = _paint_rulers(grid, top_order, top_lengths, left_order, left_lengths)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed385645705/7/6.py:325:    raise RuntimeError(\"failed to generate a valid mixing-table ruler input\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_053229_seed218530468_gpt54_high_resume/seed218530468__9__codegen_prompts__6.log:35:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed218530468/9/prompt.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\\n\\n每个参考题描述包含：\\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\n\\n参考题目如下：\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"1\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"2d0172a1\\\" lines=\\\"209-224\\\">\\n<description>\\nConvert a rough nested line drawing into a clean canonical frame-and-dot diagram.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The grid has one background color and one foreground color.\\n- Foreground 4-connected objects are rough closed frames or small filled blobs.\\n- Frames may contain other frames/blobs; blobs outside a frame remain outside it.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Detect the containment tree of foreground objects using holes of each frame object.\\n- Replace every blob with one foreground pixel.\\n- Replace every frame with a rectangular border padded two cells around its direct children.\\n- Place siblings by their original row/column overlap and order, with one empty cell between canonical objects.\\n\\nKey insight: The exact wobbly geometry is irrelevant; only enclosure plus relative sibling positions define the output.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"2\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"aaef0977\\\" lines=\\\"25-41\\\">\\n<description>\\nReplace an orange canvas with concentric Manhattan-distance color rings centered on the lone marker pixel.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The grid is an orange background with exactly one non-orange marker pixel.\\n- The marker color is one of the colors in the fixed non-orange ring cycle.\\n\\nRule:\\n- The marker location is distance 0 and keeps the marker color.\\n- Each step of Manhattan distance away from the marker advances one position\\n  through the cycle green, yellow, black, grey, red, teal, maroon, pink, blue.\\n- Fill every pixel of the original grid by this distance-indexed cycle.\\n\\nKey insight: The output is not copied from existing objects; it is the\\ndistance field around the single marker, colored by a cyclic palette that\\nexcludes the orange background.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"3\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"bc93ec48\\\" lines=\\\"48-63\\\">\\n<description>\\nCopy each foreground object anchored in a true grid corner clockwise into the next corner.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The dominant color is the background.\\n- Foreground objects are monochromatic 4-connected components.\\n- Relevant objects are exactly those whose bounding box touches two adjacent borders at one grid corner.\\n\\nRule\\n- Start from the input unchanged.\\n- For each corner object, copy its pixel mask and color to the next corner clockwise: top-left to top-right, top-right to bottom-right, bottom-right to bottom-left, and bottom-left to top-left.\\n- Preserve each object's orientation by aligning its bounding box to the destination corner; stamps may overwrite existing pixels at the destination, but source pixels are not cleared.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- Interior and side-only objects are distractors; only components actually anchored to a corner participate in the clockwise perimeter copy.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"4\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"15660dd6\\\" lines=\\\"33-54\\\">\\n<description>\\nCombine each column's repeated template mask with its single solid color swatch.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The grid is a table of framed panels separated by background rows/columns.\\n- The leftmost column gives one solid row-label color for each panel row.\\n- In each panel column, exactly one panel has a solid non-background interior,\\n  while the other panels share the same mask drawn in one template color on\\n  the background.\\n\\nRule:\\n- For every panel column, find the row containing the solid interior swatch.\\n- Rebuild one output panel using that row's left label as the frame color.\\n- Fill the repeated template mask with the swatch color and leave the mask\\n  background cells as background; separate rebuilt panels with one\\n  background column.\\n\\nKey insight:\\nThe table encodes a colorized stencil per column: the solid panel supplies\\nthe paint color and frame label, while the duplicate template panels supply\\nthe shape mask.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"5\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"d6e50e54\\\" lines=\\\"8-25\\\">\\n<description>\\nMove each maroon marker toward the blue rectangle and recolor the rectangle red.\\n\\nInput structure\\nA background canvas contains one solid blue rectangular object and several isolated\\nmaroon marker pixels. Each marker is horizontally or vertically aligned with the\\nrectangle and lies outside it.\\n\\nRule\\nStart with a background canvas, repaint the blue rectangle red, and move each\\nmaroon marker straight toward the rectangle along its row or column. Exactly one\\nmarker is strictly closer to the rectangle than all others and enters the\\nrectangle boundary; every other marker lands in the adjacent exterior cell just\\noutside its aligned side.\\n\\nKey insight\\nThe single entering marker is the unique global nearest marker to the rectangle,\\nnot the nearest marker on each of the four sides.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"6\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"342ae2ed\\\" lines=\\\"34-49\\\">\\n<description>\\nDraw the missing diagonal connector segment between each pair of same-color rectangular objects.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The grid has one dominant background color.\\n- Every foreground color appears as exactly two separated solid rectangular 4-connected objects.\\n- The two rectangles of each color are diagonally offset with facing corners on a 45-degree line.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Keep all existing rectangles unchanged.\\n- For each foreground color, connect the lower facing corner of the upper rectangle to the upper facing corner of the lower rectangle.\\n- Paint only the intervening background pixels on that diagonal, excluding the two endpoint pixels already in the rectangles.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- Same-color rectangles define the endpoints; the output completes the open diagonal between their nearest facing corners.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"7\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"f0100645\\\" lines=\\\"51-68\\\">\\n<description>\\nSlide each inner colored object horizontally into the same-colored vertical wall until it touches an obstacle.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\n- The only foreground colors are two non-background colors.\\n- One foreground color fills the left column and the other fills the right column.\\n- Extra 8-connected objects of each wall color appear away from that color's wall.\\n\\nRule\\n- Clear the extra objects from their original positions.\\n- For each wall color, process its 8-connected extra objects from nearest to farthest from the matching wall.\\n- Slide each object horizontally toward its matching wall as far as possible without overlapping the wall or an already settled object of the same color.\\n- Keep the two vertical wall columns fixed.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- The side columns act like color-specific gravity walls: same-colored objects compact sideways against their own wall while preserving each object's shape.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"8\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"c9680e90\\\" lines=\\\"52-67\\\">\\n<description>\\nMove each mirrored bottom source pixel to the far end of its trail and redraw the top half as its reflection.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- A solid non-background row separates equal-height top and bottom halves.\\n- The top half has one marker color on the background.\\n- In the bottom half, exactly one color has positions that mirror the top markers across the separator, and the other color forms trails touching those source pixels.\\n\\nRule\\n- Identify the bottom source color by reflecting each bottom color into the top half and matching the top marker set.\\n- For every bottom source pixel, follow its unique 4-connected trail of the other bottom color to the trail endpoint.\\n- Clear the old top markers, bottom sources, and trails; place the source color at each endpoint and place the top marker color at the reflected endpoint.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- The top half is only a mirror display of the bottom moving sources; the actual motion is encoded by the trail attached to each bottom source pixel.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"9\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"dfadab01\\\" lines=\\\"79-93\\\">\\n<description>\\nExpand each colored control pixel into its corresponding fixed 4x4 glyph.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- Black background with single-pixel markers in colors 2, 3, 5, and/or 8.\\n- Some inputs also show a sample 4x4 glyph in the output color, with a same-rule marker just below-right of the sample.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Replace each marker color by its learned 4x4 glyph: 2->yellow frame, 3->blue ring, 5->pink diagonal blocks, 8->orange X.\\n- Paint each glyph with its top-left corner at the marker pixel, clipping at the grid boundary.\\n- Remove the sample glyphs and skip their below-right label markers.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- The colored pixels are control pixels for a fixed glyph alphabet; non-control sample glyphs are only legend entries, not preserved scene objects.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"10\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"581f7754\\\" lines=\\\"8-22\\\">\\n<description>\\nSlide multi-color sprites to align their marker pixels with matching isolated border anchors.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = most common color.\\n- Multi-color sprites in the interior; each has a minority-color \\\"marker\\\" pixel.\\n- Isolated border pixels (non-bg with all 4-neighbors bg) act as anchors.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.\\n- Top/bottom-edge anchor (non-corner): slide sprite horizontally so marker column = anchor column.\\n- Left/right-edge anchor (or corner): slide sprite vertically so marker row = anchor row.\\n\\nKey insight: The anchor's edge position determines the slide axis — top/bottom means horizontal, left/right (or corner) means vertical.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"11\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"b1986d4b\\\" lines=\\\"19-37\\\">\\n<description>\\nRender the filled-square object counts as compact nested stacks ordered by count rank.\\n\\nInput structure\\nA large noisy grid has a dominant background, scattered non-square noise, and\\nfilled monochrome square objects. Each square side length has exactly one\\nobject color, and side lengths form consecutive sizes.\\n\\nRule\\nIgnore non-square components. If the lowest square in the scene is of the\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed241687935/15/codegen_prompts/2.md:24:- `Key insight`：缺角的位置同时编码了两个信息——目标角落和旋转方向；解题者需要先发现缺角与角落的对应映射关系，再理解 L 形如何被简化投影到 2×2 槽中。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210747_seed1852178230_gpt54_high/seed1852178230__15__codegen_prompts__5.log:12:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'rg -n -A90 -B5 \\\"def main|def generate_input\\\" /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/136b0064.py /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/195c6913.py /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/58490d8a.py /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/36a08778.py'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/36a08778.py-2-from collections import Counter, deque\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/36a08778.py-3-import numpy as np\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/36a08778.py-4-from arc_utils import STRUCT8, components_mask\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/36a08778.py-5-import random\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/36a08778.py-6-\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/36a08778.py:7:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/36a08778.py-8-    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/36a08778.py-9-    Simulate water falling from top-edge sources, pooling on shelves, and cascading off edges.\\n/home