h each grey rectangle's single border gap, with ray length equal to the rectangle's interior area.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/1.py:190:    - One or more grey 1-pixel-thick rectangular borders appear on the grid.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/1.py:191:    - Each grey rectangle has exactly one centered 1-pixel gap on one side.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/1.py:192:    - Each rectangle interior contains exactly one non-black, non-grey seed pixel.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/1.py:195:    - For each grey rectangle, identify its bounding box, its unique border gap, and the unique seed color inside.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/1.py:198:    - The ray length equals the cavity area, truncated if it reaches the grid boundary; keep the original grey borders, seed pixels, and all unrelated cells unchanged.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/1.py:379:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/6/4.py:158:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/6/4.py:160:    Push each framed pattern outward using the seed's missing side, then add a mirrored copy on the opposite side.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/6/4.py:171:    - Also place a mirrored copy one full frame length away on the opposite side, reflecting across the axis parallel to the push direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/6/4.py:175:    - The yellow seed is a directional code: its lone exposed side selects the push direction, and that same axis determines how the opposite-side mirror is produced.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/6/4.py:448:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/5/4.py:145:def main(grid: np.ndarray) ->