ontaining some non-background single pixels.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/1.py:104:    - For each grey frame, count how many non-background, non-grey pixels lie strictly inside it.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/1.py:106:    - Repaint the entire grey border of that frame with the looked-up legend color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/1.py:277:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210747_seed1852178230_gpt54_high/seed1852178230__13__codegen_prompts__4.log:35:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_18\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1852178230/13/prompt.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\\n\\n每个参考题描述包含：\\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\n\\n参考题目如下：\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"1\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"bae5c565\\\" lines=\\\"10-28\\\">\\n<description>\\nErase the top palette row and redraw it below as a widening wedge centered on its missing cell.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The top row is a palette row with exactly one background gap.\\n- Below it, the only foreground is one vertical marker bar of a single color.\\n- The marker bar is either in the gap column or immediately beside it.\\n\\nRule\\n- Clear the grid to background.\\n- Starting at the top of the marker bar, each next row copies one more\\n  column of the top-row palette on both sides of the gap.\\n- Fill the gap column with the marker color, and keep the vertical marker bar.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- The lone background cell in the top row is the center of the expanding\\n  copy; the lower vertical bar provides the center color and the row where\\n  the expansion begins.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"2\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"470c91de\\\" lines=\\\"48-65\\\">\\n<description>\\nMove each teal-cornered filled rectangle one cell diagonally toward its teal corner.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- Dominant background surrounds several filled rectangular colored objects.\\n- Each object has exactly one teal control pixel replacing one corner cell of\\n  its rectangle.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Treat the teal pixel as the missing corner of its colored rectangle.\\n- Erase each original rectangle footprint, including the teal pixel.\\n- Repaint the completed rectangle shifted one cell diagonally in the direction\\n  of that teal corner.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- The control pixel's corner position gives both the missing cell to restore\\n  and the diagonal motion vector.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"3\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"3d6c6e23\\\" lines=\\\"10-27\\\">\\n<description>\\nMove each vertical stream of pixels into a bottom-aligned centered pile.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- A mostly background grid contains one or more vertical source columns of\\n  foreground pixels.\\n- Each source column has n^2 foreground pixels, and the top-to-bottom color\\n  sequence splits into monochrome groups of lengths 1, 3, 5, ...\\n\\nRule\\n- Clear the canvas to background.\\n- For each source column, read the foreground colors from top to bottom and\\n  rebuild them at the bottom below the same column as odd-width centered\\n  rows of lengths 1, 3, 5, ...\\n\\nKey insight\\n- The scattered vertical pixels are falling grains; a square number of\\n  grains decomposes into the odd row widths of a centered pyramid.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"4\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"13f06aa5\\\" lines=\\\"36-51\\\">\\n<description>\\nExtend each colored marker from its directional sprite to a grid edge, painting a dotted ray and the whole edge side.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\n- One repeated body color forms small 8-connected directional sprites.\\n- Each marker is a singleton non-background, non-body color embedded in one sprite.\\n\\nRule:\\n- The body pixels around a marker lie mostly behind it; the opposite direction is the marker's ray direction.\\n- Paint every second pixel from the marker along that ray, then paint the entire boundary side reached by the ray.\\n- If two painted boundary sides meet at a corner, make that shared corner black.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- The same seven-pixel body sprite rotates to encode the direction; its local center-of-mass bias points away from the ray.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"5\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"2c181942\\\" lines=\\\"7-21\\\">\\n<description>\\nAttach monochrome sprites to the matching sides of a central hollow square.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = background. A hollow NxN square (hub) with bg corners/interior and four differently-colored edges (top, bottom, left, right).\\n- 2-4 monochrome sprites scattered on the grid, each matching one hub edge color.\\n\\nRule:\\n- For each hub edge color, find the matching sprite outside the hub.\\n- Rotate the sprite (0/90/180/270°) so its contact edge has exactly N-2 contiguous cells aligned with the hub side, and the rotated sprite is mirror-symmetric along the contact-edge axis (UD for left/right, LR for top/bottom).\\n- Translate it to adjoin that hub side. \\n- Clear everything else to bg; output is hub + attached sprites only.\\n\\nKey insight: Each edge color uniquely pairs a sprite to a side; symmetry along the contact-edge axis disambiguates the correct rotation.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"6\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"79cce52d\\\" lines=\\\"29-44\\\">\\n<description>\\nCrop off the control row and column, then cyclically roll the payload by the two marker offsets.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The grid is square, with a control row on top and a control column on the left.\\n- The control row and column share one filler color and one single-pixel marker color.\\n- The lower-right square is the payload and contains none of the control colors.\\n\\nRule\\n- Remove the top control row and left control column.\\n- Roll the remaining payload down by the marker's zero-based position in the left control column.\\n- Roll the payload right by the marker's zero-based position in the top control row.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- The two border markers are cyclic shift amounts for the payload, not colors to preserve.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"7\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"30f42897\\\" lines=\\\"51-66\\\">\\n<description>\\nRepeat the single colored border segment around the rectangular border, leaving one segment-length gap between copies.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\n- There is exactly one foreground color.\\n- All foreground pixels form one contiguous segment on the rectangular border, possibly crossing the cycle start.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Unwrap the grid border clockwise into a cyclic path.\\n- Let n be the length of the foreground segment.\\n- Copy the segment with the same color every 2*n border positions around the cycle.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- The foreground segment is not extended by rows or columns directly; it is a motif on the perimeter cycle, repeated with an equal-sized gap.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"8\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"52364a65\\\" lines=\\\"10-24\\\">\\n<description>\\nErase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- A grid has one dominant background color and several monochromatic 4-connected foreground objects.\\n- Each foreground object spans at least two columns in its bounding box.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Find each same-color 4-connected foreground object.\\n- Within each object's own bounding box, set foreground pixels in the two leftmost columns to the background color.\\n- Leave all other pixels unchanged.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- The deletion is measured from each object's local left edge, not from the grid edge or from a shared global column.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"9\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"ad38a9d0\\\" lines=\\\"23-36\\\">\\n<description>\\nRecolor each placeholder object according to its normalized shape while leaving the background fixed.\\n\\nInput structure\\nA same-size grid with one dominant background color and one foreground\\nplaceholder color forming separated 4-connected objects.\\n\\nRule\\nReplace every placeholder object by the color assigned to its exact\\ntranslation-normalized mask; all background pixels remain unchanged.\\n\\nKey insight\\nThe input objects are a shape legend with repeated instances: identical\\nmasks always receive identical colors, independent of their position.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"10\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"5034a0b5\\\" lines=\\\"16-32\\\">\\n<description>\\nShift each interior pixel whose color matches a frame side one cell toward that matching side.\\n\\nInput structure\\nThe grid has a one-cell-thick rectangular frame: the four corners are the\\nbackground color, and each side between corners is a solid, distinct side\\ncolor. The interior is mostly background with sparse foreground pixels.\\n\\nRule\\nInterior pixels with the top-side color move one row up, bottom-side color\\nmove one row down, left-side color move one column left, and right-side color\\nmove one column right. A pixel already adjacent to its matching side stays in\\nplace; colors that do not match a frame side and the frame itself are unchanged.\\n\\nKey insight\\nThe colored frame sides act as direction labels for matching interior pixels.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"11\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"42f83767\\\" lines=\\\"23-39\\\">\\n<description>\\nExpand the lower color grid by replacing each pixel with its matching top stencil.\\n\\nInput structure\\nThe input has a top legend and a lower dense color grid, separated by blank rows.\\nThe legend contains left-to-right 2x2 color swatches and, to their right,\\nthe same number of square neutral-color stencil masks.\\n\\nRule\\nPair the swatches and stencil masks by left-to-right order. For every pixel in\\nthe lower color grid, paste the paired stencil mask as one output block,\\nrecoloring the mask pixels with that pixel's color and leaving mask holes as bg.\\n\\nKey insight\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/9_1.log:12:代码已写入 [1.py](/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1155420539/9/1.py:1)。`main()` 按顶边/左边刻度读取窗口、裁剪同色矩形并按 ruler 顺序重排；`generate_input()` 会随机化颜色集合、两条 ruler 的排列、窗口尺寸、块尺寸和块内偏移，并用构造出的期望输出反校验 `main()`。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/9_1.log:43:用网格边缘的彩色刻度尺确定每个内部色块的裁剪窗口，再按刻度尺颜色顺序拼接裁剪结果。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/9_1.log:57:- 边缘刻度尺同时充当了色块的寻址索引和输出排列的顺序指令；解题者必须先发现边缘颜色与内部色块颜色的对应关系，再意识到刻度顺序决定了拼接顺序。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/9_1.log:1357:1. `main()` 直接把顶边和左边的彩色刻度读成两条有序 ruler，按位置而不是颜色 id 排序。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/9_1.log:1359:3. 输出按左 ruler 的顺序决定行高、按上 ruler 的顺序决定列宽，把每个裁剪块放回其同色行列交叉单元，其余位置保持黑色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/9_1.log:1360:4. `gen