_new/codegen_logs_20260619_053142_seed287049989_resume_gpt54_xhigh/12_4.log:2570:+        ruler = rulers[int(rng.integers(len(rulers)))]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260619_053142_seed287049989_resume_gpt54_xhigh/12_4.log:2574:+        for local_r, local_c in ruler:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260619_053142_seed287049989_resume_gpt54_xhigh/12attempt()\\n        if result is not None:\\n            return result\\n    raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Failed to generate input after {GENERATION_RETRIES} attempts\\\")\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210621_gpt54_high_missing/9__codegen_prompts__6.log:30:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_15\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed56627177/9/prompt.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\\n\\n每个参考题描述包含：\\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\n\\n参考题目如下：\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"1\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"1d61978c\\\" lines=\\\"8-22\\\">\\n<description>\\nRecolor the two diagonal foreground-bar orientations, assigning teal to the larger orientation and red to the smaller one.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The grid has one dominant background color and one foreground color.\\n- Foreground pixels form one-cell-thick diagonal bars.\\n- Every foreground pixel belongs to exactly one diagonal orientation.\\n\\nRule\\n- Keep the background unchanged.\\n- Classify each foreground pixel by whether it has a diagonal neighbor on the NW/SE axis or the NE/SW axis.\\n- Recolor the orientation with more foreground pixels teal and the other orientation red.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- The output colors depend on the relative population of the two diagonal orientations, not on a fixed slash direction or position.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"2\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"2ba387bc\\\" lines=\\\"6-21\\\">\\n<description>\\nSort scattered 4×4 squares into two columns by type: frames left, solids right.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = most common color. Multiple 4×4 objects on bg.\\n- Frames: colored 1px border, bg-filled 2×2 interior.\\n- Solids: entirely filled with one non-bg color.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Classify each 4×4 object as frame or solid by its interior.\\n- Sort each group top-to-bottom by input row.\\n- Stack frames in left column (cols 0–3), solids in right (cols 4–7).\\n- Output is 8 wide; height = 4 × max(#frames, #solids), bg-padded.\\n\\nKey insight: Frame vs solid is determined solely by whether the 2×2 interior matches bg.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"3\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"52364a65\\\" lines=\\\"10-24\\\">\\n<description>\\nErase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- A grid has one dominant background color and several monochromatic 4-connected foreground objects.\\n- Each foreground object spans at least two columns in its bounding box.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Find each same-color 4-connected foreground object.\\n- Within each object's own bounding box, set foreground pixels in the two leftmost columns to the background color.\\n- Leave all other pixels unchanged.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- The deletion is measured from each object's local left edge, not from the grid edge or from a shared global column.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"4\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"8e5c0c38\\\" lines=\\\"9-21\\\">\\n<description>\\nClean each color layer by enforcing vertical mirror symmetry.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = background. Several non-bg colors, each forming a nearly-symmetric pattern about some vertical axis.\\n- Some pixels in each color are \\\"noise\\\" that breaks the symmetry.\\n\\nRule:\\n- For each non-bg color, find the vertical axis that best explains its pixel layout.\\n- Remove any pixel that lacks a same-color mirror counterpart across that axis.\\n\\nKey insight: Each color has its own independent symmetry axis; the task is per-color denoising, not whole-grid symmetry.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"5\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"e729b7be\\\" lines=\\\"8-20\\\">\\n<description>\\nComplete the scene by adding the point-reflected copy of the colored object across the central marker.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The grid has odd dimensions, a dominant background, and a center-row marker color appearing only at the left edge, center, and right edge.\\n- A single divider color fills the center column except for the center marker.\\n- All remaining foreground pixels form the object to copy, entirely on the left side of the divider.\\nRule\\n- Keep the input unchanged.\\n- For every object pixel, paint the pixel rotated 180 degrees around the center marker with the same color.\\nKey insight\\n- The center marker is the rotation center; the yellow-looking divider is not mirrored, it only separates the source from the empty target side.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"6\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"fc10701f\\\" lines=\\\"20-35\\\">\\n<description>\\nMove the orange rectangle onto the maroon rectangle and mark gated corridor crossings in red.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The dominant background contains black obstacle segments.\\n- There is one solid orange rectangle and one solid maroon rectangle of the same size.\\n- The two rectangles share either their row span or their column span, so the move is straight and axis-aligned.\\n\\nRule\\n- Erase the original orange rectangle to the background.\\n- Replace the maroon rectangle with the orange rectangle.\\n- Between the two rectangles, paint red across the moving rectangle's width or height only at corridor cells flanked by black obstacle segments perpendicular to the movement.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- The black segments define gates in the straight corridor; only those gated openings, not every swept background cell, become red.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"7\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"6165ea8f\\\" lines=\\\"74-90\\\">\\n<description>\\nBuild a color-labeled shape-equivalence table from the objects listed on the right edge.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The background contains one main 4-connected object for each foreground color.\\n- The rightmost column has one singleton pixel of each foreground color, listed top-to-bottom.\\n- Those singleton pixels define the row and column order of the output table.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Normalize each main object to its tight mask and compare masks up to rotation or reflection.\\n- Draw 2x2 color labels across the top and down the left, separated by one background row/column.\\n- For each off-diagonal table cell, paint a 2x2 red block when the two labeled objects have the same shape under rotation/reflection, otherwise paint a 2x2 grey block.\\n- Leave diagonal cells and all separators as background.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- Object positions and original orientations are distractors; the relation is dihedral shape equivalence, while the right-edge legend fixes the table order.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"8\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"97d7923e\\\" lines=\\\"81-94\\\">\\n<description>\\nRecolor vertical bars by legend-driven rank selection.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = background. Top-left: monochrome blocks touching row 0; each has color K and height k.\\n- Main grid: vertical bars capped top and bottom by a single color, with solid-color interiors.\\n\\nRule:\\n- For each legend entry (K, k), find vertical bars capped by K.\\n- Rank bars by interior length (longest = rank 1).\\n- Recolor the rank-k bar's interior to K.\\n\\nKey insight: Legend height is a rank index into length-sorted bars, not a literal size.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"9\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"4c416de3\\\" lines=\\\"99-118\\\">\\n<description>\\nReplicate a pre-drawn corner pattern to every other marker-bearing corner.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = most frequent color. Hollow 0-frames (possibly partial L-shapes); each\\n  frame-corner cell is either 0 or a painted (non-bg, non-0) color.\\n- >= 1 'source' corner: the pattern is already drawn (one color, both outward\\n  cells and an inward-diagonal trail).\\n- Other corners: a single colored pixel on the inward diagonal at the pattern's\\n  deepest (k,k) offset; the pixel's color is that corner's target color.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Extract the canonical (TL-oriented) pattern from any source.\\n- For each non-source corner whose marker cell is colored, paint the same\\n  pattern rotated to that corner's orientation, using the marker's color.\\n\\nKey insight: the pattern is symmetric about the corner's inward-diagonal axis\\n(canonical dr == dc), so it reflects cleanly across all four corner orientations.\\nPainting uses each target's OWN marker color, not the source color.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"10\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"7e4d4f7c\\\" lines=\\\"9-24\\\">\\n<description>\\nCompress the L-shaped cue to three rows and add a pink copy of the top-row foreground mask.\\n\\nInput structure\\nThe grid has a dominant background color, a two-color top row, and all\\nforeground pixels below the top row lie in the first column as vertical markers.\\n\\nRule\\nKeep the input top row as output row 0 and the first marker row as output row 1.\\nOutput row 2 is background except at the top-row foreground columns, which are\\nrecolored pink.\\n\\nKey insight\\nThe lower repeated marker rows only identify the vertical cue; the generated\\nrow is a recolored mask of the horizontal cue in the top row.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"11\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"3e6067c3\\\" lines=\\\"7-20\\\">\\n<description>\\nConnect framed squares via colored bridges following a control-pixel sequence.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = background. Border color forms equal-sized framed squares with unique inner fill colors.\\n- Control row below squares: colored pixels read left-to-right encode visitation order.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Start at the square matching first control color c0.\\n- For each consecutive pair (ci, ci+1), find the ci+1-colored square aligned in the same row or column band, preferring nearest.\\n- Draw a bridge colored ci between the pair, spanning the gap with inner-square thickness.\\n\\nKey insight: Row/column-band alignment plus proximity resolves ambiguity when inner colors repeat.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"12\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"2d0172a1\\\" lines=\\\"209-224\\\">\\n<description>\\nConvert a rough nested line drawing into a clean canonical frame-and-dot diagram.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The grid has one background color and one foreground color.\\n- Foreground 4-connected objects are rough closed frames or small filled blobs.\\n- Frames may contain other frames/blobs; blobs outside a frame remain outside it.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Detect the containment tree of foreground objects using holes of each frame object.\\n- Replace every blob with one foreground pixel.\\n- Replace every frame with a rectangular border padded two cells around its direct children.\\n- Place siblings by their original row/column overlap and order, with one empty cell between canonical objects.\\n\\nKey insight: The exact wobbly geometry is irrelevant; only enclosure plus relative sibling positions define the output.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"13\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"898e7135\\\" lines=\\\"7-20\\\">\\n<description>\\nInflate a frame's hole-layout and fill each hole with its matching piece.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = most common color. Largest component is a monochrome frame enclosing bg holes.\\n- Outside pieces composed of k×k blocks; k = side of smallest solid square piece.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Extract connected hole regions inside the frame as slots.\\n- Match each piece to a slot by comparing block-level shapes under rotation/flip.\\n- Output the layout scaled by k, with pieces placed in slots; frame color as background.\\n\\nKey insight: Pieces are k×k-block-scaled versions of holes; downsampling reveals shape matches under all 8 orientations.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"14\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"edb79dae\\\" lines=\\\"39-53\\\">\\n<description>\\nStamp recolored sprites into a framed region using placeholder positions and a color legend.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg background, a rectangular single-color frame, colored placeholder cells inside the frame.\\n- Outside the frame: sprite shapes (one per placeholder color) and a small legend mapping each placeholder color to an output color.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Find the frame and its interior placeholders.\\n- For each placeholder color, locate the matching-color sprite outside the frame.\\n- Stamp each sprite at the placeholder's position inside the frame.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210621_gpt54_high_missing/9__codegen_prompts__6.log:32:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_16\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/9/codegen_prompts/6.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\\n\\n## 新题位置\\n\\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed56627177/9`\\n- 题号：`6`\\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/9/6.py`\\n\\n## 新题描述\\n\\n<new_puzzle index=\\\"6\\\">\\n- `description`：根据网格边缘色带的颜色顺序，对网格内部的同心矩形嵌套图案进行颜色层级重排。\\n\\n- `Input structure`：\\n  - 背景为一种主色（如 black）。\\n  - 网格中央有一个由多种颜色组成的同心矩形嵌套图案：最外层是一种颜色的单像素宽矩形框，内部是另一种颜色的矩形框，依此类推，最内层可能是一个实心小矩形。每层颜色各不相同。\\n  - 网格的最上方一行（或最左方一列）有一排单像素色带，从左到右（或从上到下）依次排列若干颜色，这些颜色恰好是同心矩形中出现的所有颜色，但顺序与同心矩形中从外到内的顺序不同。\\n\\n- `Rule`：\\n  - 读取边缘色带中颜色的排列顺序，从左到右记为 C1, C2, C3, ...\\n  - 在原始同心矩形中，识别每层矩形框的颜色及其层级（从外到内）。\\n  - 重新构建同心矩形：最外层使用 C1 的颜色，第二层使用 C2 的颜色，依此类推。每层保持单像素宽矩形框的形状，嵌套结构与原始图案的层数和几何比例完全相同，仅颜色重新分配。\\n  - 边缘色带本身在输出中保持不变。\\n\\n- `Key insight`：同心矩形的层级结构是\\\"骨架\\\"，色带是\\\"重排指令\\\"。解题者需要先识别出同心矩形的层级顺序，再发现色带编码了新的颜色分配映射——色带的第 k 个颜色映射到第 k 层，而不是映射到某个特定颜色。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n## 机制相似参考题\\n\\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\\n\\n已选参考：train/34cfa167, train/22208ba4, train/db118e2a, train/52364a65, eval/581f7754, train/a834deea, train/d749d46f, eval/8f215267\\n\\n<reference_puzzle rank=\\\"1\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"34cfa167\\\">\\n<similarity>\\nscore=0.3731\\nmechanism=0.4564\\nlexical=0.0135\\ncode_feature=0.5000\\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:rectangle, operation:sort_order, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:row_col\\n</similarity>\\n<paths>\\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/34cfa167.py\\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/34cfa167.json\\n</paths>\\n<description>\\nComplete a four-corner framed rectangle from one decorated anchor rectangle and its diagonal mate.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\n- Two same-color solid rectangular anchors of the same size sit on opposite\\n  diagonal corners, with the first anchor above-left of the second.\\n- The upper-left anchor has two one-cell-thick vertical control bars to its\\n  right and two one-cell-thick horizontal control bars below it.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Copy the anchor rectangle into the two missing corners of the implied\\n  larger rectangle.\\n- Repeat the right-side control bars horizontally between the left and right\\n  anchors, using their spacing as the period, and draw the outer top and\\n  bottom borders in the first right-control color.\\n- Repeat the below-side control bars vertically between the top and bottom\\n  anchors, using the same period, and draw the outer left and right borders\\n  in the first below-control color.\\n\\nKey insight: The small control bars are the first two ticks of two periodic\\nframe patterns; the diagonal anchor supplies the opposite corner and the\\nmissing two anchor copies.\\n</description>\\n<annotation>\\n{\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"symmetry/pattern\\\",\\n  \\\"src\\\": \\\"two same-color solid rectangular anchors, with two right control bars and two below control bars beside the upper-left anchor\\\",\\n  \\\"dst\\\": \\\"the missing two anchor corners and periodic frame segments between all four anchors\\\",\\n  \\\"transform\\\": \\\"copy the anchor rectangle into the missing corners; repeat the right-control colors across the top and bottom anchor rows and outer borders, and repeat the below-control colors down the left and right side bars using the same spacing\\\"\\n}\\n</annotation>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle rank=\\\"2\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"22208ba4\\\">\\n<similarity>\\nscore=0.3660\\nmechanism=0.4460\\nlexical=0.0136\\ncode_feature=0.5000\\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:sort_order, output:same_size, relation:row_col\\n</similarity>\\n<paths>\\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/22208ba4.py\\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/22208ba4.json\\n</paths>\\n<description>\\nMove the repeated boundary color's rectangles one block inward while leaving singleton boundary rectangles in place.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The background is the most common color.\\n- Foreground objects are solid monochrome rectangles touching a grid corner.\\n- Exactly one foreground color appears as multiple separate 4-connected objects; other colors appear once.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Clear the multiple objects of the repeated color from their original positions.\\n- For each cleared rectangle, translate it away from the row and column border it touches by exactly its height and width.\\n- Keep singleton-color objects unchanged; overlapping translated rectangles of the same color merge.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- Multiplicity selects the moving color, and each boundary rectangle's touched edges determine its inward diagonal translation.\\n</description>\\n<annotation>\\n{\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"move_along_path\\\",\\n  \\\"src\\\": \\\"the foreground color with multiple 4-connected solid rectangles on grid corners\\\",\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"from each rectangle's corner, move inward away from the touched row and column borders by one rectangle height/width\\\",\\n  \\\"trajectory\\\": \\\"translate each selected rectangle once; same-color overlaps merge\\\",\\n  \\\"transform\\\": \\\"clear selected rectangles at their original positions; leave singleton-color rectangles unchanged\\\"\\n}\\n</annotation>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle rank=\\\"3\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"db118e2a\\\">\\n<similarity>\\nscore=0.3556\\nmechanism=0.4746\\nlexical=0.0140\\ncode_feature=0.2500\\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, object:frame, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:inside\\n</similarity>\\n<paths>\\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/db118e2a.py\\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/db118e2a.json\\n</paths>\\n<description>\\nNormalize the framed input motif into a 5x5 icon and stamp two copies on a 15x15 canvas.\\n\\nInput structure\\nThe input is a rounded rectangular frame: the four corners are the background\\ncolor, and every other outer-border pixel has one frame color. Non-background\\npixels inside that frame are the motif to preserve.\\n\\nRule\\nMake a 5x5 version of the rounded frame with a 3x3 interior. Crop the input\\ninterior motif to its bounding box, center that crop in the 3x3 interior, and\\npaste the resulting 5x5 icon at upper-left positions (2, 2) and (8, 8) in a\\n15x15 background canvas.\\n\\nKey insight\\nThe variable-size frame is only a carrier; the meaningful object is the\\ncompact interior motif, which is normalized to the fixed 3x3 icon interior.\\n</description>\\n<annotation>\\n{\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"transform_in_place\\\",\\n  \\\"src\\\": \\\"rounded rectangular outer frame with a non-background interior motif\\\",\\n  \\\"transform\\\": \\\"build a 5x5 rounded-frame icon from the frame color, center the interior motif bbox in its 3x3 interior, and paste two copies at fixed diagonal positions on a background canvas\\\",\\n  \\\"grid_shape\\\": \\\"15x15\\\"\\n}\\n</annotation>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle rank=\\\"4\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"52364a65\\\">\\n<similarity>\\nscore=0.3427\\nmechanism=0.4291\\nlexical=0.0145\\ncode_feature=0.4000\\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\\n</similarity>\\n<paths>\\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/52364a65.py\\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/52364a65.json\\n</paths>\\n<description>\\nErase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- A grid has one dominant background color and several monochromatic 4-connected foreground objects.\\n- Each foreground object spans at least two columns in its bounding box.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Find each same-color 4-connected foreground object.\\n- Within each object's own bounding box, set foreground pixels in the two leftmost columns to the background color.\\n- Leave all other pixels unchanged.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- The deletion is measured from each object's local left edge, not from the grid edge or from a shared global column.\\n</description>\\n<annotation>\\n{\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"transform_in_place\\\",\\n  \\\"src\\\": \\\"monochromatic 4-connected foreground objects on a background\\\",\\n  \\\"transform\\\": \\\"for each object, set foreground pixels in its two leftmost bbox columns to bg\\\"\\n}\\n</annotation>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle rank=\\\"5\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"581f7754\\\">\\n<similarity>\\nscore=0.3532\\nmechanism=0.4565\\nlexical=0.0142\\ncode_feature=0.3333\\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\\n</similarity>\\n<paths>\\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/581f7754.py\\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/581f7754.json\\n</paths>\\n<description>\\nSlide multi-color sprites to align their marker pixels with matching isolated border anchors.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = most common color.\\n- Multi-color sprites in the interior; each has a minority-color \\\"marker\\\" pixel.\\n- Isolated border pixels (non-bg with all 4-neighbors bg) act as anchors.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.\\n- Top/bottom-edge anchor (non-corner): slide sprite horizontally so marker column = anchor column.\\n- Left/right-edge anchor (or corner): slide sprite vertically so marker row = anchor row.\\n\\nKey insight: The anchor's edge position determines the slide axis — top/bottom means horizontal, left/right (or corner) means vertical.\\n</description>\\n<annotation>\\n{\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"move_to_match\\\",\\n  \\\"src\\\": \\\"multi-color sprite s with a unique marker color (minority color inside s)\\\",\\n  \\\"dst\\\": \\\"align to isolated border pixel d (same marker color)\\\",\\n  \\\"match_cond\\\": \\\"s.marker.color == d.color\\\",\\n  \\\"transform\\\": \\\"translate s: if d on top/bottom edge → align col(s.marker) to col(d); else → align row(s.marker) to row(d); clip out-of-bounds pixels\\\"\\n}\\n</annotation>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle rank=\\\"6\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"a834deea\\\">\\n<similarity>\\nscore=0.3349\\nmechanism=0.3993\\nlexical=0.0169\\ncode_feature=0.5000\\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:sprite, operation:sort_order, output:same_size, relation:inside\\n</similarity>\\n<paths>\\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/a834deea.py\\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/a834deea.json\\n</paths>\\n<description>\\nFill each black 5x5 region's missing interior positions with a fixed 3x3 positional color legend.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The grid uses teal as the dominant background and black for one or more\\n  5x5 regions.\\n- Each black region has a black one-pixel border and a 3x3 interior that\\n  may already contain teal pixels.\\n\\nRule\\n- Overlay the legend 1 7 6 / 4 8 5 / 2 9 3 on the 3x3 interior of every\\n  5x5 black region.\\n- Wherever an interior non-center legend position is still black, recolor it\\n  to the corresponding legend color; leave existing teal pixels, the center,\\n  and the black border unchanged.\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/16/1.py:15:    assert rows.size >= 2, \"expected at least two legend colors in the leftmost column\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/16/1.py:28:    - The leftmost column contains a vertical legend of distinct non-black colors, read from top to bottom.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_021006_seed1583749884/seed1583749884__16__codegen_prompts__4.log:19:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/16/prompt.md && printf '\\\\\\\\n--- DES ---\\\\\\\\n' && sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/16/des.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\\n\\n每个参考题描述包含：\\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\n\\n参考题目如下：\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"1\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"42f83767\\\" lines=\\\"23-39\\\">\\n<description>\\nExpand the lower color grid by replacing each pixel with its matching top stencil.\\n\\nInput structure\\nThe input has a top legend and a lower dense color grid, separated by blank rows.\\nThe legend contains left-to-right 2x2 color swatches and, to their right,\\nthe same number of square neutral-color stencil masks.\\n\\nRule\\nPair the swatches and stencil masks by left-to-right order. For every pixel in\\nthe lower color grid, paste the paired stencil mask as one output block,\\nrecoloring the mask pixels with that pixel's color and leaving mask holes as bg.\\n\\nKey insight\\nThe lower grid is not copied directly; it is an index grid whose colors select\\nthe stencil shape from the legend, so each input pixel becomes one square block.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"2\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"98c475bf\\\" lines=\\\"62-76\\\">\\n<description>\\nErase the complete interior glyph and expand each endpoint marker pair into its color's full glyph.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The grid is 20x20 with background inside two same-color full-height vertical frame bars.\\n- Inside the frame there is one complete color glyph and one or more other colors appearing only as two endpoint markers in the same row.\\n- Marker endpoints are always in the first and last interior columns.\\n\\nRule\\n- Keep the vertical frame unchanged.\\n- Erase any complete interior glyph.\\n- For each endpoint marker pair, use that marker color's learned glyph template and anchor its horizontal bar on the marker row.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- Color identifies which glyph shape to draw; the two endpoint pixels are not copied objects, they are anchors for reconstructing that color's full symbol.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"3\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"d753a70b\\\" lines=\\\"81-93\\\">\\n<description>\\nRed diamond outlines contract by one layer and gray diamond outlines expand by one layer while other objects stay fixed.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- A 16x16 orange-background grid contains one-cell-thick Manhattan-diamond outlines.\\n- Red and gray outlines are the changing objects; other colored diamond outlines are static.\\n- Some outlines may be clipped by the grid boundary, but their visible pixels still fit a clipped Manhattan-distance contour.\\nRule\\n- Clear all red and gray pixels.\\n- Red objects are redrawn with the same diamond center and radius minus one.\\n- Gray objects are redrawn with radius plus one; an ambiguous edge-clipped growing arc continues away from the nearest perpendicular edge.\\nKey insight\\n- The task is not about moving whole objects: each changing object is a contour of a diamond, and the visible operation is one step of contour contraction or expansion.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"4\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"87ab05b8\\\" lines=\\\"9-24\\\">\\n<description>\\nErase all distractor pixels and expand the single red control pixel into the grid quadrant that contains it.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The grid has one dominant background color.\\n- Exactly one red pixel is the control pixel.\\n- Other non-background pixels are distractors.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Clear the canvas to the background color.\\n- Split the grid into equal top/bottom and left/right halves.\\n- Fill the quadrant containing the red control pixel with red.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- The red control pixel selects a whole half-grid quadrant by its row half and column half; all other foreground pixels are noise.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"5\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"df978a02\\\" lines=\\\"57-72\\\">\\n<description>\\nLet the largest center-pointing object grow outward while every other object loses its inward tip.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The grid has a single dominant background color and four 8-connected monochromatic foreground objects.\\n- The objects surround a central background gap and point toward it from cardinal directions.\\n- Exactly one object has the largest area.\\n\\nRule\\n- Find the central background gap by minimizing aggregate distance to the four objects.\\n- Recolor the nearest-to-center pixel of each non-largest object to background.\\n- Add a three-pixel cap in the largest object's color on the side away from the center, centered on the shared row or column.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- The edit is a transfer of prominence around a common center: losers retract at their tips, and the unique largest object extends outward from the center.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"6\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"981571dc\\\" lines=\\\"6-19\\\">\\n<description>\\nReconstruct a 4-way symmetric mosaic by filling missing (black) pixels.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- A colored grid exhibiting bilateral symmetry along both a vertical and a horizontal axis.\\n- Some pixels are erased to color 0 (black), creating gaps in the pattern.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Infer the vertical and horizontal reflection axes from the visible (non-zero) pixels.\\n- For each black pixel, recover its color from the mirrored position across either axis or both.\\n- When multiple mirrors yield candidates, use the majority color.\\n\\nKey insight: The reflection axes are not given — they must be deduced from the surviving pixels by finding the axes that best preserve the existing symmetry.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"7\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"20270e3b\\\" lines=\\\"7-21\\\">\\n<description>\\nConnect two sprites using matching connector pixels, then tight-crop.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- Background color `bg`, sprite color `obj`, connector color `ctrl` (small, 2 components).\\n- Two main foreground sprites, plus possibly tiny detached pixels belonging to one sprite.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Identify the **base** sprite (closest to grid top-left).\\n- Translate the other sprite so its connector sits one cell above the base's connector.\\n- Stamp the plug onto the base; remove connectors (recolor `ctrl` to `obj`).\\n- Output is the tight crop around all non-background pixels.\\n\\nKey insight: The connector pixels define the unique docking point and direction.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"8\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"305b1341\\\" lines=\\\"22-37\\\">\\n<description>\\nExpand each sparse color object into a filled rectangular region using its legend-paired fill color.\\n\\nInput structure\\nA background-color grid has a two-column legend in columns 0 and 1, starting at row 0: each row gives\\na source color in the left column and that source color's fill color in the right column.  Outside the\\nlegend, the foreground pixels are sparse dot objects whose colors are exactly the legend source colors.\\n\\nRule\\nClear the legend.  For each source color, take the bbox of all of its non-legend dots, expand that bbox\\nby one pixel in every direction, and fill background cells inside the expanded rectangle with the paired\\nlegend fill color while preserving every original non-legend dot.\\n\\nKey insight\\nThe legend order is also the layer order: earlier legend rows are in front, so fill rectangles are painted\\nfrom the last legend row back to the first and higher-priority fills overwrite lower-priority fills.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"9\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"1d61978c\\\" lines=\\\"8-22\\\">\\n<description>\\nRecolor the two diagonal foreground-bar orientations, assigning teal to the larger orientation and red to the smaller one.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The grid has one dominant background color and one foreground color.\\n- Foreground pixels form one-cell-thick diagonal bars.\\n- Every foreground pixel belongs to exactly one diagonal orientation.\\n\\nRule\\n- Keep the background unchanged.\\n- Classify each foreground pixel by whether it has a diagonal neighbor on the NW/SE axis or the NE/SW axis.\\n- Recolor the orientation with more foreground pixels teal and the other orientation red.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- The output colors depend on the relative population of the two diagonal orientations, not on a fixed slash direction or position.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"10\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"ecb67b6d\\\" lines=\\\"138-155\\\">\\n<description>\\nRecolor the grey diagonal-chain regions in an orange field to teal.\\n\\nInput structure\\nThe input contains only grey pixels and orange pixels.  Grey pixels form\\nseveral 8-connected regions embedded in the orange field.\\n\\nRule\\nDecompose each grey 8-connected region into 4-connected lobes.  Recolor the\\nwhole region teal only when it contains a straight diagonal run of at least\\nthree pixels and those lobes meet only by diagonal corner contacts in a\\nnon-branching diagonal chain or cycle; a single 4-connected region is\\nrecolored only when it is a square diagonal staircase.\\n\\nKey insight\\nThe teal regions are not selected by size or position; they are the grey\\nregions whose internal connectivity depends on diagonal corner joins, while\\nsame-edge cracks, rectangles, bars, and branching/noisy regions remain grey.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"11\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"a1aa0c1e\\\" lines=\\\"74-97\\\">\\n<description>\\nCompress the stacked colored bars into a compact ordered table with the control pixel on the selected row.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- A background grid contains several full-width colored bars from top to\\n  bottom; the last bar is the base/separator color.\\n- Each non-base bar may have an aligned three-column comb motif below it,\\n  alternating side-pair rows with solid rows.\\n- A singleton control pixel sits away from the colored motifs.\\n\\nRule\\n- Make one output row per non-base bar, preserving top-to-bottom order.\\n- In that row, paint the bar color once for each solid three-pixel row in\\n  its motif, then paint the base-bar color in the separator column.\\n- The singleton control pixel sits immediately above the base bar. Among\\n  motifs whose open side-pair parity is compatible with that bottom row,\\n  put the control pixel in the output row with the fewest solid rows; use\\n  horizontal distance to the motif center only to break count ties.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- The vertical comb height is a count, while the control pixel is read by\\n  projecting it onto the center gap of compatible comb rows rather than by\\n  its vertical band alone.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"12\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"b10624e5\\\" lines=\\\"24-39\\\">\\n<description>\\nReplicate a motif across quadrants with scaling and reflection keyed to red anchor blocks.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- Grid divided into four quadrants by a full-row and full-column divider of a single non-bg color.\\n- Each quadrant contains a red (2) square anchor block of varying size.\\n- The top-left quadrant also has a colored motif attached to its red anchor.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Use the top-left quadrant's motif as the source pattern.\\n- For each other quadrant, scale the motif by the ratio of that quadrant's red block size to the source red block size.\\n- Reflect horizontally for right-side quadrants, vertically for bottom quadrants (both for bottom-right).\\n- Align the scaled/reflected motif so its red region overlaps the target anchor, then stamp non-bg pixels.\\n\\nKey insight: Red block size encodes the scale factor; quadrant position encodes the reflection axes.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"13\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"15660dd6\\\" lines=\\\"33-54\\\">\\n<description>\\nCombine each column's repeated template mask with its single solid color swatch.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The grid is a table of framed panels separated by background rows/columns.\\n- The leftmost column gives one solid row-label color for each panel row.\\n- In each panel column, exactly one panel has a solid non-background interior,\\n  while the other panels share the same mask drawn in one template color on\\n  the background.\\n\\nRule:\\n- For every panel column, find the row containing the solid interior swatch.\\n- Rebuild one output panel using that row's left label as the frame color.\\n- Fill the repeated template mask with the swatch color and leave the mask\\n\\n--- DES ---\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：将网格中每个前景对象的像素按行扫描顺序重新排列为底部对齐的垂直条，条的列位置由对象颜色在图例中的排名决定。\\n\\n- `Input structure`：\\n  - 背景为 Black。\\n  - 网格最左列有一个垂直颜色图例：从上到下排列不同颜色的像素（如 Red、Blue、Green、Yellow），代表列位置 0、1、2、3。\\n  - 网格中散布着若干个 4-连通单色前景对象（颜色与图例中的颜色匹配），面积各不相同。\\n\\n- `Rule`：\\n  - 创建与输入同大的背景色画布。\\n  - 对每种图例颜色，计算该颜色在网格中的总像素数 N。\\n  - 在图例中找到该颜色的排名 K（从上到下第 K 个）。\\n  - 在输出画布的第 K 列中，从底部向上绘制 N 个该颜色的像素。\\n  - 保持图例列不变。\\n\\n- `Key insight`：对象的形状和位置被完全丢弃，仅保留像素总数作为条的高度；图例既定义了颜色到列位置的映射，又隐含了多种颜色共存时的排列规则。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：在两个半面板中，找到能够完美\\\"拼合\\\"为矩形的对象对，将它们移动到彼此相邻的位置并合并。\\n\\n- `Input structure`：\\n  - 背景为 Azure。\\n  - 网格被一条完整的 Maroon 水平分隔线分为上下两个面板。\\n  - 上面板有 2-3 个 4-连通单色前景对象，下面板也有 2-3 个 4-连通单色前景对象。\\n  - 上面板中的每个对象与下面板中的恰好一个对象可以拼合为一个完整的矩形（两者的形状互补：将一个翻转后放在另一个旁边恰好填满一个矩形）。\\n\\n- `Rule`：\\n  - 对每对上下面板的对象，测试是否存在一种拼合方式使两者形成完整矩形（允许垂直翻转下面板对象）。\\n  - 找到所有匹配的对象对。\\n  - 在输出中，将每对匹配对象拼合为矩形绘制，矩形之间间隔一列背景色，从左到右按上面板对象的原始列位置排列。\\n  - 上面板对象保持原色在上方，下面板对象保持原色在下方。\\n  - 丢弃分隔线。\\n\\n- `Key insight`：配对基于形状互补性（拼合为矩形），而非颜色或大小匹配——解题者需要在心理上\\\"翻转拼合\\\"来验证每对候选对象。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：根据每个对象边界上 Yellow 标记像素的数量和位置，在对象的对应方向上绘制等长的射线。\\n\\n- `Input structure`：\\n  - 背景为 Black。\\n  - 网格中有若干个 4-连通的 Grey 实心前景对象。\\n  - 每个对象的边界上有 1-4 个 Yellow 标记像素（替换了该位置的 Grey 像素），分布在对象的不同边上。\\n\\n- `Rule`：\\n  - 对每个 Yellow 标记像素，确定它所在的对象边（上/下/左/右边界）。\\n  - 从标记位置沿着远离对象的方向（即标记所在边的法线外方向）绘制一条 Yellow 射线。\\n  - 射线长度等于该对象的 Yellow 标记总数。\\n  - 射线不覆盖已有的前景像素。\\n  - 保持对象的 Grey 像素不变。\\n\\n- `Key insight`：每个标记的方向由其所在的边决定，而所有标记的射线长度相同（等于标记总数）——标记总数同时编码了射线长度，形成了一种\\\"自计数\\\"机制。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：将网格中每一行的前景像素按颜色分组后向两侧推离，颜色在图例中的排名决定了推离的优先级。\\n\\n- `Input structure`：\\n  - 背景为 Black。\\n  - 网格最上行有一个颜色优先级图例：从左到右排列不同颜色像素（如 Red、Blue、Green），越靠左优先级越高。\\n  - 网格下方各行中包含不同颜色的前景像素，混合在同一行中。\\n\\n- `Rule`：\\n  - 对每行（图例行除外），收集所有前景像素。\\n  - 按颜色在图例中的优先级排序：最高优先级的颜色像素放在行的中心，次高优先级的像素向两侧扩展，最低优先级的像素被推到行的两端。\\n  - 具体地：最高优先级的像素保持在原行的中心区域（居中放置），次优先级的像素紧贴在其两侧，以此类推。\\n  - 每种颜色的像素保持原有数量，在其分配的区域内居中排列。\\n\\n- `Key insight`：优先级不是决定\\\"去留\\\"而是决定\\\"位置\\\"——高优先级的颜色占据中心，低优先级的被推到边缘；这是一种基于排名的空间重分配。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：在包含\\\"时钟面板\\\"序列的网格中，每个面板的指针位置相对于前一个面板顺时针旋转了固定角度；补全最后一个缺失指针的面板。\\n\\n- `Input structure`：\\n  - 背景为 Black。\\n  - 网格被 Grey 分隔列分为 4 个等大的正方形面板。\\n  - 每个面板中心有一个 Red 像素（圆心），周围有一个由 Grey 像素构成的 5x5 正方形边框（表盘）。\\n  - 前 3 个面板中，各有一个 Yellow 的 2 像素长指针从中心向边框延伸，指向 8 个方向之一（上、右上、右、右下、下、左下、左、左上）。\\n  - 第 4 个面板只有表盘和圆心，没有指针。\\n\\n- `Rule`：\\n  - 观察前 3 个面板的指针方向序列，推断相邻面板间的固定旋转步长（每步 = 45 度顺时针旋转 K 步，K 为常数）。\\n  - 将第 3 个面板的指针方向再顺时针旋转 K 步，得到第 4 个面板的指针方向。\\n  - 在第 4 个面板中绘制该方向的 Yellow 指针。\\n\\n- `Key insight`：面板序列是一个旋转动画的帧；旋转步长需要从前三帧中归纳——这是一种序列外推任务，核心推理在于发现恒定的旋转增量。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210621_gpt54_high_missing/12__codegen_prompts__7.log:65:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_33\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/29/code.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Combo variant of b9e38dc0 (index 29)\\n# combo_spec: D12/0+D13/1\\n# Name: 统一开口方向+颜色编码方向\\n\\n# Design analysis\\n# ---------------\\n# spec:\\n#   fused_variant:\\n#     summary: |\\n#       以 D13/1 的“闭合门面颜色编码开口”作为基础，再叠加 D12/0 的“同图多个精灵且方向统一”。\\n#       每个精灵仍是原题家族里的漏斗/半包围墙，但原本的几何缺口被一条直线门面补上；\\n#       门面颜色不再只是“这是门”，而是从固定色表里编码全局辐射方向。\\n#       同一张图至少有两个精灵，所有精灵的门面颜色相同，因此它们共享同一 outward direction。\\n#   concrete_geometry:\\n#     sprite:\\n#       - 保留原题的两条锯齿臂 + 闭合端 + 1:1 / 1:2 两种臂角模式。\\n#       - 在原开口处补一条整齐的水平/垂直门面，长度仍为 gap+1。\\n#       - 非门面的墙统一使用 closed_color；门面使用 direction_color。\\n#     multiplicity:\\n#       - 每张图放置 2 个精灵，彼此独立、互不重叠，并沿与辐射垂直的轴分开摆放。\\n#       - 因为两个精灵共享相同门面色，所以会重复支撑“这个颜色代表这个方向”。\\n#     palette:\\n#       - 方向编码色固定为 4 个显眼颜色：1/2/3/4 分别对应 上/右/下/左。\\n#       - 背景、闭合墙、填充种子、障碍全部避开这 4 个方向色，避免视觉混淆。\\n#   behavior_trace:\\n#     example: |\\n#       例：若门面颜色为 2（红），则两只闭合漏斗都朝右辐射。\\n#       原题流程：从真实缺口的两个端点推出开口方向，再向外放射。\\n#       现在流程：solver 先识别所有长直线门面，读出它们的颜色 2 -> 右；\\n#       然后对每个精灵，把这条线视作“可穿透门”，从门两端恢复边界射线，\\n#       内部填充穿门而出，继续向右扩散；障碍仍沿同方向制造阴影。\\n#     difference: |\\n#       如果还按原题把“缺失的一面”当作开口，则这里根本没有缺口；\\n#       如果只做单个 D13/1 精灵，也看不出 D12/0 的“统一全局方向重复出现”。\\n#   complexity_calibration:\\n#     - 保留原题的锯齿臂、两类射线斜率、阴影机制，所以仍属于同一视觉家族。\\n#     - 只增加一个低自由度的符号层：4 个固定方向色；同图内只激活其中 1 个，便于少样例归纳。\\n#     - 精灵数固定为 2，既能体现“多个且统一”，又不会把辐射区挤得过于混乱。\\n#   implicit_assumptions_review:\\n#     - 原代码假设 wall 是单色且唯一主组件；这里改为 closed_color 最大、open_color 为多段直线门面。\\n#     - 原代码依赖 degree-1 端点来找开口；这里墙体闭合，必须改为读取门面两端。\\n#     - 原代码默认墙完全不可穿过；这里 open_color 必须放入可通行集合，但输出保留原色。\\n#     - 原代码按单组件处理；这里要遍历多个 wall component，并给每个组件单独加外放射边界。\\n#     - 新增假设：所有门面都用同一个方向色，且每个门面是长度 >= 6 的单一直线段。\\n#       generator 通过固定门面构造、统一色表和障碍配色限制来保证这些前提成立。\\n#   placement_legality:\\n#     - 组件按与辐射垂直的轴分槽放置，保证输入时 bbox 不重叠。\\n#     - 同时要求门面投影区间留足空隙，降低多组件辐射区在输出中相互缠绕的概率。\\n#     - 障碍只放在背景格、远离墙体，并基于无障碍时的 nominal fill zone 采样。\\n#   observability_and_cleanliness:\\n#     - 人类会看到：同一种门面色在同图重复出现，两个精灵都朝同一方向出流。\\n#     - 方向色不复用于背景/种子/障碍，因此“颜色是语义标签”肉眼可见。\\n#     - 两个精灵分开摆放，门面是整齐直线，障碍仍是稀疏点状，层次不会打架。\\n\\nimport random\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nfrom scipy.ndimage import distance_transform_cdt\\n\\nfrom arc_utils import components_mask, get_bg, neighbors4, neighbors8\\n\\n\\nDIR_TO_COLOR = {\\n    (-1, 0): 1,  # blue -> up\\n    (0, 1): 2,   # red -> right\\n    (1, 0): 3,   # green -> down\\n    (0, -1): 4,  # yellow -> left\\n}\\nCOLOR_TO_DIR = {color: direction for direction, color in DIR_TO_COLOR.items()}\\nNON_DIRECTION_COLORS = [0, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9]\\n\\n\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Fill several closed funnels and let a shared door color dictate their common exit direction.\\n\\n    Input structure:\\n    - The background is the dominant color. Each sprite is a closed funnel: most wall pixels use one closed-wall color, while one straight wall face uses a direction-coded color.\\n    - There are multiple such sprites in one grid, and all coded faces share the same color, so every sprite uses the same outward direction. Small fill blobs sit inside the funnels; other sparse colors are obstacles.\\n\\n    Rule:\\n    - Decode the common outward direction from the door-face color, then treat each coded face as permeable while the rest of the wall stays solid.\\n    - Flood-fill from the interior seeds through each coded face, extend the fill outward within the two recovered boundary rays, and apply obstacle shadows along that shared direction.\\n\\n    Key insight: Geometry now tells you where each door segment is, but the door color tells you which global direction all sprites radiate toward; once that color is decoded, the same direction applies to every funnel in the grid.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.array(grid, copy=True)\\n    h, w = g.shape\\n\\n    vals = np.unique(g)\\n    bg = get_bg(g)\\n    non_bg = [int(v) for v in vals if int(v) != bg]\\n    assert non_bg, \\\"expected at least one non-background color\\\"\\n\\n    def sgn(x: int) -> int:\\n        return (x > 0) - (x < 0)\\n\\n    closed_color = max(non_bg, key=lambda c: int((g == c).sum()))\\n\\n    def straight_segments_for_color(color: int) -> list[set[tuple[int, int]]]:\\n        segments: list[set[tuple[int, int]]] = []\\n        for cells in components_mask(g == color, connectivity=4):\\n            pts = {(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in cells}\\n            if len(pts) < 6:\\n                continue\\n            rows = {r for r, _ in pts}\\n            cols = {c for _, c in pts}\\n            if len(rows) == 1:\\n                row = next(iter(rows))\\n                c0 = min(c for _, c in pts)\\n                c1 = max(c for _, c in pts)\\n                expected = {(row, cc) for cc in range(c0, c1 + 1)}\\n                endpoints = [(row, c0), (row, c1)]\\n            elif len(cols) == 1:\\n                col = next(iter(cols))\\n                r0 = min(r for r, _ in pts)\\n                r1 = max(r for r, _ in pts)\\n                expected = {(rr, col) for rr in range(r0, r1 + 1)}\\n                endpoints = [(r0, col), (r1, col)]\\n            else:\\n                continue\\n            if pts != expected:\\n                continue\\n            ok = True\\n            for ep in endpoints:\\n                touches_closed = any(\\n                    0 <= rr < h and 0 <= cc < w and g[rr, cc] == closed_color\\n                    for rr, cc in neighbors8(*ep)\\n                )\\n                if not touches_closed:\\n                    ok = False\\n                    break\\n            if ok:\\n                segments.append(pts)\\n        return segments\\n\\n    open_color = None\\n    open_segments: list[set[tuple[int, int]]] = []\\n    best_score = None\\n    for color in non_bg:\\n        if color == closed_color or color not in COLOR_TO_DIR:\\n            continue\\n        segments = straight_segments_for_color(color)\\n        if len(segments) < 2:\\n            continue\\n        score = (sum(len(seg) for seg in segments), len(segments))\\n        if best_score is None or score > best_score:\\n            best_score = score\\n            open_color = color\\n            open_segments = segments\\n\\n    assert open_color is not None, \\\"expected repeated straight door faces in a direction color\\\"\\n    rad = COLOR_TO_DIR[open_color]\\n\\n    wall_mask = (g == closed_color) | (g == open_color)\\n    wall_comps = [set((int(r), int(c)) for r, c in pts) for pts in components_mask(wall_mask, connectivity=8)]\\n    assert len(wall_comps) >= 2, \\\"expected multiple wall components\\\"\\n\\n    other_colors = [c for c in non_bg if c not in (closed_color, open_color)]\\n    assert other_colors, \\\"expected at least one non-wall color\\\"\\n    wall_points = [p for comp in wall_comps for p in comp]\\n\\n    def min_dist_to_wall(color: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\\n        pts = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(g == color)]\\n        best_d = 10**9\\n        for r, c in pts:\\n            for wr, wc in wall_points:\\n                d = abs(r - wr) + abs(c - wc)\\n                if d < best_d:\\n                    best_d = d\\n                    if best_d == 0:\\n                        return 0, len(pts)\\n        return best_d, len(pts)\\n\\n    fill_color = min(other_colors, key=lambda c: (min_dist_to_wall(c)[0], min_dist_to_wall(c)[1]))\\n    fill_pos = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in np.argwhere(g == fill_color)]\\n    if not fill_pos:\\n        return g\\n\\n    barrier = g == closed_color\\n\\n    def comp_neighbors(comp_mask: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\\n        out = []\\n        for rr, cc in neighbors8(r, c):\\n            if 0 <= rr < h and 0 <= cc < w and comp_mask[rr, cc]:\\n                out.append((rr, cc))\\n        return out\\n\\n    def add_ray(start: tuple[int, int], d: tuple[int, int]) -> None:\\n        rr, cc = start\\n        while True:\\n            rr += d[0]\\n            cc += d[1]\\n            if not (0 <= rr < h and 0 <= cc < w):\\n                break\\n            barrier[rr, cc] = True\\n\\n    def add_ray_12(start: tuple[int, int], d: tuple[int, int]) -> None:\\n        rr, cc = start\\n        step = 0\\n        while True:\\n            step += 1\\n            if step % 2 == 1:\\n                rr += d[0]\\n                cc += d[1]\\n            else:\\n                if rad[0] != 0:\\n                    rr += d[0]\\n                else:\\n                    cc += d[1]\\n            if not (0 <= rr < h and 0 <= cc < w):\\n                break\\n            barrier[rr, cc] = True\\n\\n    assigned_segments = 0\\n    for wall_comp in wall_comps:\\n        comp_open_segments = [seg for seg in open_segments if seg <= wall_comp]\\n        assert len(comp_open_segments) == 1, \\\"each wall component must contain exactly one coded face\\\"\\n        assigned_segments += 1\\n        open_face = comp_open_segments[0]\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_211346_seed1155420539_resume2_gpt54_xhigh/13_1.log:310:Erase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_211346_seed1155420539_resume2_gpt54_xhigh/13_1.log:318:- Within each object's own bounding box, set foreground pixels in the two leftmost columns to the background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_211346_seed1155420539_resume2_gpt54_xhigh/13_1.log:1167:    Erase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_211346_seed1155420539_resume2_gpt54_xhigh/13_1.log:1175:    - Within each object's own bounding box, set foreground pixels in the two leftmost columns to the background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/11/codegen_prompts/1.md:240:Erase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/11/codegen_prompts/1.md:248:- Within each object's own bounding box, set foreground pixels in the two leftmost columns to the background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/11/codegen_prompts/5.md:12:- `description`：将每个前景对象内部的颜色分布模式投影到该对象的边框上，使边框的每一侧反映其正对的内部颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/11/codegen_prompts/5.md:25:- `Key insight`：边框的颜色不是固定的，而是由其内部最近行/列的颜色分布决定——边框成为了内部内容的\"投影屏\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/7/codegen_prompts/5.md:12:- `description`：在包含\"发送器\"和\"接收器\"的网格中，每个发送器通过其颜色匹配的接收器，将自身的形状以镜像方式投影到接收器的另一侧。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/7/codegen_prompts/5.md:27:- `Key insight`：接收器标记既是颜色匹配键，也是空间定位锚点；发送器的形状经过镜像后\"穿越\"分隔线出现在右侧——颜色配对和镜像投影是两层独立的推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/1/codegen_prompts/6.md:12:- `description`：在棋盘格背景上，每个前景对象的边界凸出像素指向其应该\"投影\"到的网格边缘，投影在边缘处生成与对象同色的标记条，条的长度等于对象的像素数。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/1/codegen_prompts/6.md:26:- `Key insight`：突出像素既编码了投影方向，又是对象的一部分参与像素计数；边缘标记条的长度来自面积而非几何尺寸，这使得规则的两个维度（方向和长度）需要独立归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210621_gpt54_high_missing/9__codegen_prompts__3.log:43:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_21\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed56627177/9/prompt.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\\n\\n每个参考题描述包含：\\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\n\\n参考题目如下：\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"1\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"1d61978c\\\" lines=\\\"8-22\\\">\\n<description>\\nRecolor the two diagonal foreground-bar orientations, assigning teal to the larger orientation and red to the smaller one.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The grid has one dominant background color and one foreground color.\\n- Foreground pixels form one-cell-thick diagonal bars.\\n- Every foreground pixel belongs to exactly one diagonal orientation.\\n\\nRule\\n- Keep the background unchanged.\\n- Classify each foreground pixel by whether it has a diagonal neighbor on the NW/SE axis or the NE/SW axis.\\n- Recolor the orientation with more foreground pixels teal and the other orientation red.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- The output colors depend on the relative population of the two diagonal orientations, not on a fixed slash direction or position.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"2\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"2ba387bc\\\" lines=\\\"6-21\\\">\\n<description>\\nSort scattered 4×4 squares into two columns by type: frames left, solids right.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = most common color. Multiple 4×4 objects on bg.\\n- Frames: colored 1px border, bg-filled 2×2 interior.\\n- Solids: entirely filled with one non-bg color.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Classify each 4×4 object as frame or solid by its interior.\\n- Sort each group top-to-bottom by input row.\\n- Stack frames in left column (cols 0–3), solids in right (cols 4–7).\\n- Output is 8 wide; height = 4 × max(#frames, #solids), bg-padded.\\n\\nKey insight: Frame vs solid is determined solely by whether the 2×2 interior matches bg.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"3\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"52364a65\\\" lines=\\\"10-24\\\">\\n<description>\\nErase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- A grid has one dominant background color and several monochromatic 4-connected foreground objects.\\n- Each foreground object spans at least two columns in its bounding box.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Find each same-color 4-connected foreground object.\\n- Within each object's own bounding box, set foreground pixels in the two leftmost columns to the background color.\\n- Leave all other pixels unchanged.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- The deletion is measured from each object's local left edge, not from the grid edge or from a shared global column.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"4\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"8e5c0c38\\\" lines=\\\"9-21\\\">\\n<description>\\nClean each color layer by enforcing vertical mirror symmetry.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = background. Several non-bg colors, each forming a nearly-symmetric pattern about some vertical axis.\\n- Some pixels in each color are \\\"noise\\\" that breaks the symmetry.\\n\\nRule:\\n- For each non-bg color, find the vertical axis that best explains its pixel layout.\\n- Remove any pixel that lacks a same-color mirror counterpart across that axis.\\n\\nKey insight: Each color has its own independent symmetry axis; the task is per-color denoising, not whole-grid symmetry.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"5\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"e729b7be\\\" lines=\\\"8-20\\\">\\n<description>\\nComplete the scene by adding the point-reflected copy of the colored object across the central marker.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The grid has odd dimensions, a dominant background, and a center-row marker color appearing only at the left edge, center, and right edge.\\n- A single divider color fills the center column except for the center marker.\\n- All remaining foreground pixels form the object to copy, entirely on the left side of the divider.\\nRule\\n- Keep the input unchanged.\\n- For every object pixel, paint the pixel rotated 180 degrees around the center marker with the same color.\\nKey insight\\n- The center marker is the rotation center; the yellow-looking divider is not mirrored, it only separates the source from the empty target side.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"6\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"fc10701f\\\" lines=\\\"20-35\\\">\\n<description>\\nMove the orange rectangle onto the maroon rectangle and mark gated corridor crossings in red.\\n\\nInput structure\\n- The dominant background contains black obstacle segments.\\n- There is one solid orange rectangle and one solid maroon rectangle of the same size.\\n- The two rectangles share either their row span or their column span, so the move is straight and axis-aligned.\\n\\nRule\\n- Erase the original orange rectangle to the background.\\n- Replace the maroon rectangle with the orange rectangle.\\n- Between the two rectangles, paint red across the moving rectangle's width or height only at corridor cells flanked by black obstacle segments perpendicular to the movement.\\n\\nKey insight\\n- The black segments define gates in the straight corridor; only those gated openings, not every swept background cell, become red.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"7\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"6165ea8f\\\" lines=\\\"74-90\\\">\\n<description>\\nBuild a color-labeled shape-equivalence table from the objects listed on the right edge.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The background contains one main 4-connected object for each foreground color.\\n- The rightmost column has one singleton pixel of each foreground color, listed top-to-bottom.\\n- Those singleton pixels define the row and column order of the output table.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Normalize each main object to its tight mask and compare masks up to rotation or reflection.\\n- Draw 2x2 color labels across the top and down the left, separated by one background row/column.\\n- For each off-diagonal table cell, paint a 2x2 red block when the two labeled objects have the same shape under rotation/reflection, otherwise paint a 2x2 grey block.\\n- Leave diagonal cells and all separators as background.\\n\\nKey insight:\\n- Object positions and original orientations are distractors; the relation is dihedral shape equivalence, while the right-edge legend fixes the table order.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"8\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"97d7923e\\\" lines=\\\"81-94\\\">\\n<description>\\nRecolor vertical bars by legend-driven rank selection.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = background. Top-left: monochrome blocks touching row 0; each has color K and height k.\\n- Main grid: vertical bars capped top and bottom by a single color, with solid-color interiors.\\n\\nRule:\\n- For each legend entry (K, k), find vertical bars capped by K.\\n- Rank bars by interior length (longest = rank 1).\\n- Recolor the rank-k bar's interior to K.\\n\\nKey insight: Legend height is a rank index into length-sorted bars, not a literal size.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"9\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"4c416de3\\\" lines=\\\"99-118\\\">\\n<description>\\nReplicate a pre-drawn corner pattern to every other marker-bearing corner.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = most frequent color. Hollow 0-frames (possibly partial L-shapes); each\\n  frame-corner cell is either 0 or a painted (non-bg, non-0) color.\\n- >= 1 'source' corner: the pattern is already drawn (one color, both outward\\n  cells and an inward-diagonal trail).\\n- Other corners: a single colored pixel on the inward diagonal at the pattern's\\n  deepest (k,k) offset; the pixel's color is that corner's target color.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Extract the canonical (TL-oriented) pattern from any source.\\n- For each non-source corner whose marker cell is colored, paint the same\\n  pattern rotated to that corner's orientation, using the marker's color.\\n\\nKey insight: the pattern is symmetric about the corner's inward-diagonal axis\\n(canonical dr == dc), so it reflects cleanly across all four corner orientations.\\nPainting uses each target's OWN marker color, not the source color.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"10\\\" source=\\\"train\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"7e4d4f7c\\\" lines=\\\"9-24\\\">\\n<description>\\nCompress the L-shaped cue to three rows and add a pink copy of the top-row foreground mask.\\n\\nInput structure\\nThe grid has a dominant background color, a two-color top row, and all\\nforeground pixels below the top row lie in the first column as vertical markers.\\n\\nRule\\nKeep the input top row as output row 0 and the first marker row as output row 1.\\nOutput row 2 is background except at the top-row foreground columns, which are\\nrecolored pink.\\n\\nKey insight\\nThe lower repeated marker rows only identify the vertical cue; the generated\\nrow is a recolored mask of the horizontal cue in the top row.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"11\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"3e6067c3\\\" lines=\\\"7-20\\\">\\n<description>\\nConnect framed squares via colored bridges following a control-pixel sequence.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = background. Border color forms equal-sized framed squares with unique inner fill colors.\\n- Control row below squares: colored pixels read left-to-right encode visitation order.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Start at the square matching first control color c0.\\n- For each consecutive pair (ci, ci+1), find the ci+1-colored square aligned in the same row or column band, preferring nearest.\\n- Draw a bridge colored ci between the pair, spanning the gap with inner-square thickness.\\n\\nKey insight: Row/column-band alignment plus proximity resolves ambiguity when inner colors repeat.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"12\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"2d0172a1\\\" lines=\\\"209-224\\\">\\n<description>\\nConvert a rough nested line drawing into a clean canonical frame-and-dot diagram.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- The grid has one background color and one foreground color.\\n- Foreground 4-connected objects are rough closed frames or small filled blobs.\\n- Frames may contain other frames/blobs; blobs outside a frame remain outside it.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Detect the containment tree of foreground objects using holes of each frame object.\\n- Replace every blob with one foreground pixel.\\n- Replace every frame with a rectangular border padded two cells around its direct children.\\n- Place siblings by their original row/column overlap and order, with one empty cell between canonical objects.\\n\\nKey insight: The exact wobbly geometry is irrelevant; only enclosure plus relative sibling positions define the output.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"13\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"898e7135\\\" lines=\\\"7-20\\\">\\n<description>\\nInflate a frame's hole-layout and fill each hole with its matching piece.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg = most common color. Largest component is a monochrome frame enclosing bg holes.\\n- Outside pieces composed of k×k blocks; k = side of smallest solid square piece.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Extract connected hole regions inside the frame as slots.\\n- Match each piece to a slot by comparing block-level shapes under rotation/flip.\\n- Output the layout scaled by k, with pieces placed in slots; frame color as background.\\n\\nKey insight: Pieces are k×k-block-scaled versions of holes; downsampling reveals shape matches under all 8 orientations.\\n</description>\\n</reference_puzzle>\\n\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\"14\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"edb79dae\\\" lines=\\\"39-53\\\">\\n<description>\\nStamp recolored sprites into a framed region using placeholder positions and a color legend.\\n\\nInput structure:\\n- bg background, a rectangular single-color frame, colored placeholder cells inside the frame.\\n- Outside the frame: sprite shapes (one per placeholder color) and a small legend mapping each placeholder color to an output color.\\n\\nRule:\\n- Find the frame and its interior placeholders.\\n- For each placeholder color, locate the matching-color sprite outside the frame.\\n- Stamp each sprite at the placeholder's position inside the frame.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210621_gpt54_high_missing/9__codegen_prompts__3.log:45:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_22\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed56627177/9/des.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：根据每个封闭区域内部散落标记像素的颜色，从外部调色板中选取对应形状模板，将模板缩放后填入该封闭区域。\\n\\n- `Input structure`：\\n  - 背景为一种主色（如 black）。\\n  - 网格中有若干由同一颜色（如 blue）绘制的不规则封闭框，每个框的内部面积不同。\\n  - 每个封闭框内部散落着 1-3 个同色标记像素（颜色各不相同，如 red、green、yellow 等）。\\n  - 网格的底部或右侧有一排\\\"调色板区域\\\"：每种标记颜色对应一个小型形状模板（如 3x3 的 L 形、T 形、十字形等），模板由该标记颜色绘制在背景上。\\n\\n- `Rule`：\\n  - 对每个封闭框，统计其内部标记像素的数量 N。\\n  - 在该封闭框内部所有标记像素中，找到出现次数最多的颜色（保证唯一）。\\n  - 在调色板区域找到与该颜色匹配的形状模板。\\n  - 将模板整体缩放 N 倍（每个模板像素变成 NxN 的方块）。\\n  - 将缩放后的模板居中放置在封闭框内部（框的内部空间恰好能容纳缩放后的模板）。\\n  - 封闭框本身和调色板区域保持不变。\\n\\n- `Key insight`：标记像素同时承担两个角色——其颜色选择模板形状，其数量决定缩放倍率。解题者需要先发现\\\"颜色选模板\\\"的对应关系，再发现\\\"计数定缩放\\\"的第二层规则。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：将网格中散落的彩色碎片按遮挡关系还原为完整矩形，并按从上层到下层的顺序水平排列输出。\\n\\n- `Input structure`：\\n  - 背景为一种主色（如 black）。\\n  - 网格中有若干不同颜色的前景像素区域，它们是多个矩形层叠后的可见部分。\\n  - 每个矩形原本是纯色实心矩形，但由于相互遮挡，部分矩形只露出 L 形、条形或不规则碎片。\\n  - 每种前景颜色恰好对应一个矩形。\\n  - 至少有一个矩形完全可见（未被遮挡），其完整形状直接呈现。\\n\\n- `Rule`：\\n  - 识别每种前景颜色的所有像素，推断其原始矩形的完整边界（即包含该颜色所有像素的最小外接矩形）。\\n  - 确定遮挡关系：若颜色 A 的外接矩形范围内出现了颜色 B 的像素，则 B 在 A 之上。\\n  - 根据遮挡关系进行拓扑排序，从最上层到最下层排列。\\n  - 输出网格：将每个颜色的完整矩形（用其颜色填充）从左到右依次水平排列，矩形之间间隔一列背景色，顺序为从最上层（左）到最下层（右）。\\n  - 输出网格的高度等于所有矩形高度的最大值，不足的矩形在底部用背景色填充。\\n\\n- `Key insight`：可见碎片的形状本身不是答案——解题者需要反推每个矩形被遮挡前的完整尺寸，再通过\\\"谁覆盖了谁\\\"建立层叠顺序。两个推理层缺一不可：还原完整形状是第一层，确定层叠排序是第二层。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：在分隔线划分的子区域中，根据每个区域内\\\"种子像素\\\"的颜色找到对应的旋转模板，再根据种子像素相对于区域中心的象限位置确定旋转角度后填入。\\n\\n- `Input structure`：\\n  - 背景为一种主色（如 black）。\\n  - 网格被一种分隔色（如 grey）的完整行和完整列划分为大小相同的正方形子区域（如 5x5）。\\n  - 网格左上角的子区域包含若干\\\"模板定义\\\"：每个模板由一种非背景非分隔色绘制的小图案组成（如 red 的箭头形、green 的阶梯形），模板本身不具有四重旋转对称性。\\n  - 其余子区域中，每个子区域要么为空（纯背景），要么在区域内恰好有一个\\\"种子像素\\\"——一个非背景非分隔色的单像素点。\\n\\n- `Rule`：\\n  - 识别左上角区域中定义的各颜色模板及其原始朝向。\\n  - 对每个含种子像素的子区域：\\n    - 种子像素的颜色决定使用哪个模板。\\n    - 种子像素相对于该子区域中心点的位置决定旋转角度：左上象限 = 0 度（原始朝向）、右上象限 = 顺时针 90 度、右下象限 = 顺时针 180 度、左下象限 = 顺时针 270 度。\\n  - 将旋转后的模板居中绘制在该子区域内，使用种子像素的颜色。\\n  - 种子像素本身被模板覆盖。空子区域保持不变。\\n\\n- `Key insight`：种子像素编码了两层信息——颜色选择模板形状，空间位置（象限）选择旋转角度。解题者容易注意到颜色-模板的对应关系，但需要进一步发现位置-旋转的隐含编码才能完成推理。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：识别网格中由不同颜色绘制的有向路径箭头，沿箭头指向传递颜色，每个对象最终显示为其上游箭头指向它时所携带的颜色。\\n\\n- `Input structure`：\\n  - 背景为一种主色（如 black）。\\n  - 网格中有若干彩色对象，每个对象由两部分组成：一个 3x3 的实心正方形\\\"头部\\\"和一条从头部某一侧中央延伸出的长度为 2 的单像素宽\\\"尾巴\\\"。头部和尾巴同色。\\n  - 整个对象构成一个箭头形状：尾巴所在的方向是箭头的来源方向，头部对面的方向是箭头的指向方向。例如尾巴在左侧，则箭头指向右方。\\n  - 每个箭头的颜色各不相同。\\n  - 箭头的指向方向上（沿水平或垂直直线延伸）恰好会遇到另一个箭头的头部侧面。\\n\\n- `Rule`：\\n  - 识别每个箭头对象及其指向方向（头部对侧为尾巴所在方向，指向方向为尾巴的反方向）。\\n  - 建立指向关系链：箭头 A 指向箭头 B，意味着从 A 的头部沿指向方向直线前进最先碰到的对象是 B。\\n  - 找到链的起点（没有被任何箭头指向的箭头），其颜色保持不变。\\n  - 沿指向链依次传递：链中第 2 个箭头的输出颜色变为第 1 个箭头的颜色，第 3 个变为第 2 个的原始颜色，依此类推。\\n  - 每个箭头（头部 + 尾巴）整体被重新着色，形状和位置不变。\\n\\n- `Key insight`：解题者首先需要从不对称的形状中识别出箭头的指向方向（尾巴标识来源方向，而非指向方向），然后需要发现颜色沿指向链\\\"后移一位\\\"的传递规则。方向识别是第一层推理，颜色移位是第二层推理。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：将网格中每个彩色对象沿其自身对称轴方向投影到网格边界，投影长度等于该对象在垂直于对称轴方向上的像素跨度。\\n\\n- `Input structure`：\\n  - 背景为一种主色（如 black）。\\n  - 网格中有若干不同颜色的前景对象，每个对象是 4-连通的。\\n  - 每个对象恰好具有一条对称轴——要么是水平对称轴，要么是垂直对称轴（不会同时具有两条，也不会没有）。\\n  - 对象之间不接触，且与网格边界之间有足够的空白空间。\\n\\n- `Rule`：\\n  - 对每个前景对象，判断其对称轴方向（水平或垂直）。\\n  - 计算该对象在垂直于对称轴的方向上的像素跨度 S（例如对称轴为水平轴，则计算该对象的列跨度）。\\n  - 从该对象的外接矩形边缘出发，沿对称轴方向向最近的网格边界延伸，绘制一条长度为 S 的射线（用该对象的颜色绘制，宽度为 1 像素）。\\n  - 射线起点为对象外接矩形在射线方向上最近边界一侧的中心像素。\\n  - 原始对象保持不变。\\n\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要完成三步非平凡推理：（1）识别每个对象的对称轴类型（水平还是垂直），（2）发现射线方向与对称轴方向一致而非垂直，（3）发现射线长度等于对象在另一个方向上的跨度而非对称轴方向的跨度。对称轴同时编码了投影方向和测量维度的选择。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：根据网格边缘色带的颜色顺序，对网格内部的同心矩形嵌套图案进行颜色层级重排。\\n\\n- `Input structure`：\\n  - 背景为一种主色（如 black）。\\n  - 网格中央有一个由多种颜色组成的同心矩形嵌套图案：最外层是一种颜色的单像素宽矩形框，内部是另一种颜色的矩形框，依此类推，最内层可能是一个实心小矩形。每层颜色各不相同。\\n  - 网格的最上方一行（或最左方一列）有一排单像素色带，从左到右（或从上到下）依次排列若干颜色，这些颜色恰好是同心矩形中出现的所有颜色，但顺序与同心矩形中从外到内的顺序不同。\\n\\n- `Rule`：\\n  - 读取边缘色带中颜色的排列顺序，从左到右记为 C1, C2, C3, ...\\n  - 在原始同心矩形中，识别每层矩形框的颜色及其层级（从外到内）。\\n  - 重新构建同心矩形：最外层使用 C1 的颜色，第二层使用 C2 的颜色，依此类推。每层保持单像素宽矩形框的形状，嵌套结构与原始图案的层数和几何比例完全相同，仅颜色重新分配。\\n  - 边缘色带本身在输出中保持不变。\\n\\n- `Key insight`：同心矩形的层级结构是\\\"骨架\\\"，色带是\\\"重排指令\\\"。解题者需要先识别出同心矩形的层级顺序，再发现色带编码了新的颜色分配映射——色带的第 k 个颜色映射到第 k 层，而不是映射到某个特定颜色。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\\n<new_puzzle>\\n- `description`：在网格中找到被噪声像素部分污染的重复图案瓷砖，利用多份副本的交叉验证恢复无噪声的原始瓷砖，并用干净瓷砖替换所有副本。\\n\\n- `Input structure`：\\n  - 网格由一种小型矩形瓷砖（如 4x5）平铺而成，瓷砖之间无间隔，完美覆盖整个网格。\\n  - 原始瓷砖包含背景色和若干前景色像素组成的图案。\\n  - 每份瓷砖副本中，有 0-3 个像素被随机替换为一种特殊\\\"噪声色\\\"（如 maroon），该噪声色不出现在原始瓷砖图案中。\\n  - 不同副本中被污染的像素位置不同，但噪声颜色相同。\\n\\n- `Rule`：\\n  - 确定瓷砖的尺寸（通过观察网格的周期性重复模式）。\\n  - 将网格按瓷砖尺寸切分为多份副本。\\n  - 对于瓷砖中的每个像素位置，统计所有副本在该位置上出现的非噪声色颜色（即排除噪声色后的众数）。\\n  - 用恢复出的干净瓷砖替换网格中的所有副本，噪声像素被原始颜色替代。\\n\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先识别出平铺的周期性来确定瓷砖边界（第一层），然后发现噪声色是唯一在不同副本中出现在不同位置的颜色（第二层），最后通过交叉对比多份副本来投票恢复每个被污染像素的真实颜色（第三层）。\\n</new_puzzle>\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/9/codegen_prompts/3.md:89:- Full-width horizontal stripes of distinct non-bg colors, stacked vertically.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/9/codegen_prompts/3.md:102:  \"src\": \"horizontal stripes (full-width lines)\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210621_gpt54_high_missing/14__codegen_prompts__2.log:20:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/58490d8a.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"from __future__ import annotations\\nimport numpy as np\\nfrom arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, crop_bbox, get_bg, label_mask, paste, random_free_location\\nimport random\\nfrom functools import lru_cache\\nfrom itertools import combinations\\n\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Count colored objects and record tallies inside a legend box.\\n\\n    Input structure:\\n    - A black rectangular legend box with key-color pixels in its leftmost non-black column.\\n    - Outside the box, distinct objects of each key color are scattered across the grid.\\n\\n    Rule:\\n    - For each key color, count separate same-colored objects outside the legend box.\\n    - Output the legend box repainted: each key row gets one dot per object, spaced every other cell rightward from the key pixel.\\n\\n    Key insight: The legend is both the color index and the output canvas — object counts become dot sequences on the matching row.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\\n    H, W = g.shape\\n    _bg = int(get_bg(g))\\n\\n    black = 0\\n\\n    # STEP 1) Find the legend bbox: largest black CC whose bbox contains some non-black pixels.\\n    best = None  # (area, bbox)\\n    for coords in components_mask(g == int(black), connectivity=8):\\n        if coords.size == 0:\\n            continue\\n        b = bbox_coords(coords)\\n        sub = crop_bbox(g, b)\\n        if (sub != int(black)).any():\\n            area = int(coords.shape[0])\\n            cand = (area, tuple(map(int, b)))\\n            if best is None or cand[0] > best[0]:\\n                best = cand\\n\\n    assert not (best is None)\\n\\n    r0, c0, r1, c1 = map(int, best[1])\\n    box = crop_bbox(g, (r0, c0, r1, c1))\\n    bh, bw = map(int, box.shape)\\n\\n    # STEP 2) Inside the legend bbox, find the key column:\\n    # leftmost column with any non-black pixels (the \\\"key pixels\\\").\\n    key_col = None\\n    for cc in range(bw):\\n        if (box[:, int(cc)] != int(black)).any():\\n            key_col = int(cc)\\n            break\\n    if key_col is None:\\n        return np.zeros_like(box)\\n\\n    keys = [(int(rr), int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)])) for rr in range(bh) if int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)]) != int(black)]\\n    keys.sort(key=lambda t: int(t[0]))\\n\\n    outside = np.ones((H, W), dtype=bool)\\n    outside[int(r0) : int(r1) + 1, int(c0) : int(c1) + 1] = False\\n    out = np.zeros((bh, bw), dtype=int)\\n\\n    # STEP 3/4) Count CCs of each key color outside the legend, then draw 1 dot per CC.\\n    for rr, col in keys:\\n        mask = (g == int(col)) & outside\\n        _labc, nc = label_mask(mask, connectivity=8)\\n        for i in range(int(nc)):\\n            cc = int(key_col + 2 * i)\\n            if 0 <= cc < bw:\\n                out[int(rr), int(cc)] = int(col)\\n\\n    return out\\n\\n# --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\\n\\n# Palette and legend color choices.\\nCOLOR_POOL = tuple(range(1, 10))\\nBLACK = 0\\nDISTRACTOR_PROB = 0.5\\n\\n# Key rows and tally dimensions.\\nKEY_COUNT_RANGE = (2, 4)\\nTARGET_COUNT_RANGE = (1, 5)\\nKEY_ROW_FIRST = 1\\nKEY_ROW_STEP = 2\\nKEY_COLUMN = 1\\nTALLY_COL_STEP = 2\\nLEGEND_HEIGHT_TAIL = 1\\nLEGEND_WIDTH_TAIL = 1\\nLEGEND_SLACK_RANGE = (0, 3)\\n\\n# Canvas size and legend placement bounds.\\nGRID_HEIGHT_RANGE = (20, 25)\\nGRID_WIDTH_RANGE = (20, 25)\\nLEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN = 2\\n\\n# Sprite shape and placement constraints.\\nSPRITE_AREA_RANGE = (4, 7)\\nSPRITE_BBOXES = ((2, 2), (2, 3), (3, 2), (3, 3))\\nSPRITE_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\nSPRITE_PADDING = 1\\nSPRITE_PADDING_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\n\\n# Retry budget for rejection sampling.\\nGENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\\n\\n\\ndef _randint(bounds: tuple[int, int]) -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return an inclusive randint from a configured (low, high) pair.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return random.randint(bounds[0], bounds[1])\\n\\n\\n@lru_cache(maxsize=None)\\ndef _valid_masks(h: int, w: int, area: int) -> tuple[np.ndarray, ...]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return connected masks that span all four sides of the sprite bbox.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    masks = []\\n    for cells in combinations(range(h * w), area):\\n        mask = np.zeros((h, w), dtype=bool)\\n        for cell in cells:\\n            mask[cell // w, cell % w] = True\\n        spans_edges = mask[0, :].any() and mask[-1, :].any() and mask[:, 0].any() and mask[:, -1].any()\\n        if not spans_edges:\\n            continue\\n        _, n = label_mask(mask, connectivity=SPRITE_CONNECTIVITY)\\n        if n == 1:\\n            masks.append(mask)\\n    return tuple(masks)\\n\\n\\ndef _make_sprite(color: int, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Sample one connected same-color sprite drawn on the background color.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    area = _randint(SPRITE_AREA_RANGE)\\n    dims = []\\n    for h, w in SPRITE_BBOXES:\\n        if h * w >= area and _valid_masks(h, w, area):\\n            dims.append((h, w))\\n    h, w = random.choice(dims)\\n    mask = random.choice(_valid_masks(h, w, area))\\n    sprite = np.full((h, w), int(bg), dtype=int)\\n    sprite[mask] = int(color)\\n    return sprite\\n\\n\\ndef _sample_palette() -> tuple[int, list[int], int | None]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Choose background, key colors, and optional distractor color.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    colors = list(COLOR_POOL)\\n    bg = random.choice(colors)\\n\\n    k = _randint(KEY_COUNT_RANGE)\\n    remaining = [c for c in colors if c != bg]\\n    key_colors = random.sample(remaining,