：行列交叉投射影子是第一层推理——需要理解影子不是简单的方向投影，而是行列范围的笛卡尔积；影子重叠时按面积排序决定可见颜色是第二层推理——小面积优先是违反直觉的\"小在上\"规则，需要从样例中归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_123649_seed385645705_resume/6__7.py.jsonl:7:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'for f in /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/89565ca0.py /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/34cfa167.py /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/3e6067c3.py /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/bd283c4a.py /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/2d0172a1.py /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/58490d8a.py /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e3fe1151.py; do echo \\\"===== $f\\\"; sed -n '\\\"'/def main(/,/\\\"'^def /p'\\\"' \\\\\\\"\\\"'$f\\\" | sed '\\\"'\\\"'$d'\\\"'; sed -n '/def generate_input(/,\\\"'$p'\\\"' \\\\\\\"\\\"'$f\\\"; done'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/89565ca0.py\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Convert each colored partitioned frame into a horizontal bar whose length is its number of enclosed regions.\\n\\n    Input structure:\\n    - Black background with several axis-aligned colored line drawings.\\n    - The line drawings are damaged by scattered pixels of one non-background noise color and by overlaps with other drawings.\\n    - Each real drawing is a rectangular partitioned frame enclosing one or more background regions.\\n\\n    Rule:\\n    - For each non-background color, reconstruct its horizontal and vertical wall segments from dense row/column evidence.\\n    - Count the 4-connected background regions fully enclosed by those reconstructed walls.\\n    - The color with no enclosed region is the noise/pad color.\\n    - Sort drawing colors by enclosed-region count; equal counts are ordered by which reconstructed frame covers the other.\\n\\n    Key insight:\\n    - The scattered color is not an object; it only pads the histogram, while each true object's room count is stable after rectilinear wall reconstruction.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\n    bg = int(get_bg(g))\\n    assert bg == 0\\n\\n    counts: list[tuple[int, int, np.ndarray]] = []\\n    for color in colors_present(g, exclude={bg}):\\n        rooms = _room_count_for_color(g, int(color))\\n        walls = _walls_for_color(g, int(color))\\n        counts.append((int(color), int(rooms), walls))\\n\\n    drawings = [(color, rooms, walls) for color, rooms, walls in counts if rooms > 0]\\n    pad_colors = [color for color, rooms, _walls in counts if rooms == 0]\\n    assert drawings\\n    assert len(pad_colors) == 1\\n\\n    pad = int(pad_colors[0])\\n    ordered: list[tuple[int, int, np.ndarray]] = []\\n    for rooms in sorted({rooms for _color, rooms, _walls in drawings}):\\n        group = [item for item in drawings if item[1] == rooms]\\n        ordered.extend(_cover_order(g, group))\\n\\n    width = max(rooms for _color, rooms, _walls in ordered)\\n\\n    out = np.full((len(ordered), width), pad, dtype=int)\\n    for r, (color, rooms, _walls) in enumerate(ordered):\\n        out[r, :rooms] = int(color)\\n    return out\\n\\n# --------------- generator (claude-opus-4-6) ---------------\\n\\n# ---- CFG: Tunable generation parameters ----\\n_FRAME_COUNT_RANGE = (3, 5)           # number of colored frames per puzzle\\n_ROOM_COUNT_RANGE = (1, 6)            # rooms per frame\\n_TIE_PROBABILITY = 0.35              # chance of one tied room-count pair\\n_GRID_SIZE_BY_FRAMES = {             # (h_min, h_max, w_min, w_max, frame_max_h, frame_max_w)\\n    5: (25, 30, 25, 30, 16, 18),\\n    4: (22, 30, 22, 30, 18, 22),\\n    3: (20, 30, 20, 30, 22, 25),\\n}\\n_CELL_GAP_RANGE = (3, 13)            # min/max gap between grid lines within a frame\\n_NOISE_FRACTION_RANGE = (0.04, 0.09) # fraction of total cells as noise\\n_WALL_DAMAGE_FRACTION = 0.25         # max fraction of wall pixels replaced by noise\\n_EXTRA_OVERLAP_RANGE = (0, 3)        # non-tied overlap pairs to force\\n_OVERLAP_RETRY = 100                 # attempts to place overlapping frame\\n_GEN_RETRIES = 300                   # outer retry limit\\n\\n\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\n    for _ in range(_GEN_RETRIES):\\n        result = _gen_attempt()\\n        if result is not None:\\n            return result\\n    raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Failed to generate valid input after {_GEN_RETRIES} attempts\\\")\\n===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/34cfa167.py\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Complete a four-corner framed rectangle from one decorated anchor rectangle and its diagonal mate.\\n\\n    Input structure:\\n    - The background is the dominant color.\\n    - Two same-color solid rectangular anchors of the same size sit on opposite\\n      diagonal corners, with the first anchor above-left of the second.\\n    - The upper-left anchor has two one-cell-thick vertical control bars to its\\n      right and two one-cell-thick horizontal control bars below it.\\n\\n    Rule:\\n    - Copy the anchor rectangle into the two missing corners of the implied\\n      larger rectangle.\\n    - Repeat the right-side control bars horizontally between the left and right\\n      anchors, using their spacing as the period, and draw the outer top and\\n      bottom borders in the first right-control color.\\n    - Repeat the below-side control bars vertically between the top and bottom\\n      anchors, using the same period, and draw the outer left and right borders\\n      in the first below-control color.\\n\\n    Key insight: The small control bars are the first two ticks of two periodic\\n    frame patterns; the diagonal anchor supplies the opposite corner and the\\n    missing two anchor copies.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\n    bg = get_bg(g)\\n    source, dest, right_controls, below_controls = _find_structure(g, bg)\\n\\n    sr0, sc0, sr1, sc1 = source[\\\"bbox\\\"]\\n    dr0, dc0, dr1, dc1 = dest[\\\"bbox\\\"]\\n    anchor_color = int(source[\\\"color\\\"])\\n    assert int(dest[\\\"color\\\"]) == anchor_color, \\\"anchor colors must match\\\"\\n    assert bbox_h(source[\\\"bbox\\\"]) == bbox_h(dest[\\\"bbox\\\"]), \\\"anchor heights must match\\\"\\n    assert bbox_w(source[\\\"bbox\\\"]) == bbox_w(dest[\\\"bbox\\\"]), \\\"anchor widths must match\\\"\\n    assert sr0 > 0 and sc0 > 0, \\\"upper-left anchor must have space for outer frame\\\"\\n    assert dr1 + 1 < g.shape[0] and dc1 + 1 < g.shape[1], \\\"lower-right anchor must have space for outer frame\\\"\\n\\n    right_offsets = [int(comp[\\\"bbox\\\"][1] - sc1) for comp in right_controls]\\n    below_offsets = [int(comp[\\\"bbox\\\"][0] - sr1) for comp in below_controls]\\n    assert right_offsets == below_offsets and right_offsets[0] == 1, \\\"control offsets must match from the anchor edge\\\"\\n    step = int(right_offsets[1] - right_offsets[0])\\n    assert step > 0, \\\"control bars must be separated\\\"\\n    period = 2 * step\\n    assert (dc0 - 1 - sc1 - right_offsets[0]) % period == 0, \\\"right frame must close next to the destination anchor\\\"\\n    assert (dr0 - 1 - sr1 - below_offsets[0]) % period == 0, \\\"below frame must close next to the destination anchor\\\"\\n\\n    right_colors = [int(comp[\\\"color\\\"]) for comp in right_controls]\\n    below_colors = [int(comp[\\\"color\\\"]) for comp in below_controls]\\n    out = g.copy()\\n\\n    _paint_rect(out, bg, sr0, dc0, sr1, dc1, anchor_color)\\n    _paint_rect(out, bg, dr0, sc0, dr1, sc1, anchor_color)\\n\\n    first_c = int(sc1 + right_offsets[0])\\n    last_c = int(dc0 - 1)\\n    for c in range(first_c, last_c + 1):\\n        offset = int(c - sc1)\\n        if (offset - right_offsets[0]) % period == 0:\\n            color = right_colors[0]\\n        elif (offset - right_offsets[1]) % period == 0:\\n            color = right_colors[1]\\n        else:\\n            continue\\n        _paint_rect(out, bg, sr0, c, sr1, c, color)\\n        _paint_rect(out, bg, dr0, c, dr1, c, color)\\n\\n    _paint_rect(out, bg, sr0 - 1, first_c, sr0 - 1, last_c, right_colors[0])\\n    _paint_rect(out, bg, dr1 + 1, first_c, dr1 + 1, last_c, right_colors[0])\\n\\n    first_r = int(sr1 + below_offsets[0])\\n    last_r = int(dr0 - 1)\\n    left_c = int(sc0 - 1)\\n    right_c = int(dc1 + 1)\\n    for r in range(first_r, last_r + 1):\\n        _paint(out, bg, r, left_c, below_colors[0])\\n        _paint(out, bg, r, right_c, below_colors[0])\\n\\n        offset = int(r - sr1)\\n        if (offset - below_offsets[0]) % period == 0:\\n            _paint_rect(out, bg, r, left_c, r, sc1, below_colors[0])\\n            _paint_rect(out, bg, r, dc0, r, right_c, below_colors[0])\\n        elif (offset - below_offsets[1]) % period == 0:\\n            _paint_rect(out, bg, r, sc0, r, sc1, below_colors[1])\\n            _paint_rect(out, bg, r, dc0, r, dc1, below_colors[1])\\n\\n    return out\\n\\n# --------------- generator (att2, o5x) ---------------\\n\\n# Color sampling.\\nCOLOR_COUNT, NON_BG_COLOR_COUNT = 10, 4\\n\\n# Anchor/repetition geometry.\\nANCHOR_SIZE_RANGE = (1, 5)\\nREPEAT_COUNT_RANGE = (2, 5)\\nCONTROL_OFFSETS = (1, 3)\\nFRAME_PERIOD, DEST_ANCHOR_GAP, STRUCTURE_FIXED_PAD = 4, 2, 3\\n\\n# Canvas/margins.\\nCANVAS_MIN_SIZE, CANVAS_MAX_SIZE = 16, 30\\nMARGIN_CHOICES = range(4)\\nMIN_TOTAL_MARGIN, SOURCE_OUTER_MARGIN = 1, 1\\n\\n# Retry.\\nMAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\\n\\n\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\n    for _ in range(MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS):\\n        grid = _gen_attempt()\\n        if grid is not None:\\n            return grid\\n    raise RuntimeError(\\\"failed to generate valid input\\\")\\n===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/3e6067c3.py\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Connect framed squares via colored bridges following a control-pixel sequence.\\n\\n    Input structure:\\n    - bg = background. Border color forms equal-sized framed squares with unique inner fill colors.\\n    - Control row below squares: colored pixels read left-to-right encode visitation order.\\n\\n    Rule:\\n    - Start at the square matching first control color c0.\\n    - For each consecutive pair (ci, ci+1), find the ci+1-colored square aligned in the same row or column band, preferring nearest.\\n    - Draw a bridge colored ci between the pair, spanning the gap with inner-square thickness.\\n\\n    Key insight: Row/column-band alignment plus proximity resolves ambiguity when inner colors repeat.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\\n    H, W = g.shape\\n    bg = int(get_bg(g))\\n\\n    # border color = most common non-bg color\\n    cnt = Counter(map(int, g.flatten()))\\n    border = None\\n    for col, _k in cnt.most_common():\\n        if int(col) != int(bg):\\n            border = int(col)\\n            break\\n    assert not (border is None)\\n\\n    # detect framed squares as connected components of the border color\\n    lab, n = label_mask(g == int(border), connectivity=4)\\n    frames: list[dict] = []\\n    for cid in range(1, int(n) + 1):\\n        pts = np.argwhere(lab == int(cid))\\n        if int(pts.shape[0]) < 8:\\n            continue\\n        r0, c0 = pts.min(axis=0)\\n        r1, c1 = pts.max(axis=0)\\n        r0, c0, r1, c1 = map(int, (r0, c0, r1, c1))\\n        h = int(r1 - r0 + 1)\\n        w = int(c1 - c0 + 1)\\n        if h < 3 or w < 3:\\n            continue\\n\\n        t = None\\n        inner_col = None\\n        for tt in range(1, int(min(h, w) // 2) + 1):\\n            inner = g[int(r0 + tt) : int(r1 - tt) + 1, int(c0 + tt) : int(c1 - tt) + 1]\\n            if inner.size == 0:\\n                continue\\n            if bool((inner == int(border)).any()):\\n                continue\\n            u = set(map(int, inner.flatten()))\\n            if len(u) != 1:\\n                continue\\n\\n            ok = True\\n            if not bool((g[int(r0) : int(r0 + tt), int(c0) : int(c1) + 1] == int(border)).all()):\\n                ok = False\\n            if not bool((g[int(r1 - tt) + 1 : int(r1) + 1, int(c0) : int(c1) + 1] == int(border)).all()):\\n                ok = False\\n            if not bool((g[int(r0) : int(r1) + 1, int(c0) : int(c0 + tt)] == int(border)).all()):\\n                ok = False\\n            if not bool((g[int(r0) : int(r1) + 1, int(c1 - tt) + 1 : int(c1) + 1] == int(border)).all()):\\n                ok = False\\n            if not ok:\\n                continue\\n\\n            t = int(tt)\\n            inner_col = int(next(iter(u)))\\n            break\\n\\n        if t is None or inner_col is None:\\n            continue\\n\\n        frames.append(\\n            {\\n                \\\"bbox\\\": (int(r0), int(c0), int(r1), int(c1)),\\n                \\\"t\\\": int(t),\\n                \\\"inner\\\": int(inner_col),\\n                \\\"inner_bbox\\\": (int(r0 + t), int(c0 + t), int(r1 - t), int(c1 - t)),\\n            }\\n        )\\n\\n    assert not (not frames)\\n\\n    by: dict[int, list[dict]] = defaultdict(list)\\n    for f in frames:\\n        by[int(f[\\\"inner\\\"])].append(f)\\n\\n    max_frame_r = max(int(f[\\\"bbox\\\"][2]) for f in frames)\\n\\n    # control row = bottom-most row below the squares with >=2 non-bg pixels\\n    ctrl_r = None\\n    for r in range(int(H - 1), int(max_frame_r), -1):\\n        if int((g[int(r)] != int(bg)).sum()) >= 2:\\n            ctrl_r = int(r)\\n            break\\n    assert not (ctrl_r is None)\\n\\n    ctrl = [int(g[int(ctrl_r), int(c)]) for c in range(int(W)) if int(g[int(ctrl_r), int(c)]) != int(bg)]\\n    assert not (len(ctrl) < 2)\\n\\n    def center(f: dict) -> tuple[int, int]:\\n        r0, c0, r1, c1 = map(int, f[\\\"bbox\\\"])\\n        return int((r0 + r1) // 2), int((c0 + c1) // 2)\\n\\n    def aligned(f1: dict, f2: dict) -> tuple[bool, bool]:\\n        a = f1[\\\"inner_bbox\\\"]\\n        b = f2[\\\"inner_bbox\\\"]\\n        same_row = bool(int(a[0]) == int(b[0]) and int(a[2]) == int(b[2]))\\n        same_col = bool(int(a[1]) == int(b[1]) and int(a[3]) == int(b[3]))\\n        return same_row, same_col\\n\\n    # choose start frame\\n    start_color = int(ctrl[0])\\n    assert not (start_color not in by)\\n    start_cands = by[start_color]\\n    if len(start_cands) == 1:\\n        cur = start_cands[0]\\n    else:\\n        nxt_color = int(ctrl[1])\\n        nxt_cands = by.get(nxt_color, [])\\n        best = None\\n        bestf = None\\n        for f in start_cands:\\n            for g2 in (nxt_cands if nxt_cands else [f]):\\n                sr, sc = aligned(f, g2)\\n                al = 1 if (sr or sc) else 0\\n                (r1_, c1_) = center(f)\\n                (r2_, c2_) = center(g2)\\n                d = abs(int(r1_) - int(r2_)) + abs(int(c1_) - int(c2_))\\n                cand = (int(al), -int(d))\\n                if best is None or cand > best:\\n                    best = cand\\n                    bestf = f\\n        cur = bestf\\n\\n    out = g.copy()\\n\\n    def draw_bridge(fa: dict, fb: dict, color: int) -> None:\\n        (r0a, c0a, r1a, c1a) = map(int, fa[\\\"bbox\\\"])\\n        (r0b, c0b, r1b, c1b) = map(int, fb[\\\"bbox\\\"])\\n        ia = fa[\\\"inner_bbox\\\"]\\n        sr, sc = aligned(fa, fb)\\n        if sr:\\n            rr0, rr1 = int(ia[0]), int(ia[2])\\n            if int(c1a) < int(c0b):\\n                cc0, cc1 = int(c1a + 1), int(c0b - 1)\\n            else:\\n                cc0, cc1 = int(c1b + 1), int(c0a - 1)\\n            for r in range(int(rr0), int(rr1) + 1):\\n                for c in range(int(cc0), int(cc1) + 1):\\n                    if 0 <= r < H and 0 <= c < W:\\n                        out[int(r), int(c)] = int(color)\\n            return\\n        if sc:\\n            cc0, cc1 = int(ia[1]), int(ia[3])\\n            if int(r1a) < int(r0b):\\n                rr0, rr1 = int(r1a + 1), int(r0b - 1)\\n            else:\\n                rr0, rr1 = int(r1b + 1), int(r0a - 1)\\n            for r in range(int(rr0), int(rr1) + 1):\\n                for c in range(int(cc0), int(cc1) + 1):\\n                    if 0 <= r < H and 0 <= c < W:\\n                        out[int(r), int(c)] = int(color)\\n\\n    for i in range(int(len(ctrl)) - 1):\\n        a = int(ctrl[i])\\n        b = int(ctrl[i + 1])\\n        assert int(cur[\\\"inner\\\"]) == int(a)\\n        assert b in by, f\\\"control color {b} has no matching frame\\\"\\n        cands = by[b]\\n        best = None\\n        bestf = None\\n        for f in cands:\\n            sr, sc = aligned(cur, f)\\n            al = 1 if (sr or sc) else 0\\n            (r1_, c1_) = center(cur)\\n            (r2_, c2_) = center(f)\\n            d = abs(int(r1_) - int(r2_)) + abs(int(c1_) - int(c2_))\\n            cand = (int(al), -int(d))\\n            if best is None or cand > best:\\n                best = cand\\n                bestf = f\\n        nxt = bestf\\n        draw_bridge(cur, nxt, int(a))\\n        cur = nxt\\n\\n    return out\\n\\n\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\n    for _ in range(500):\\n        result = _gen_attempt()\\n        if result is not None:\\n            return result\\n    raise RuntimeError(\\\"Failed to generate valid input after 500 attempts\\\")\\n===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/bd283c4a.py\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pack all pixels into color-frequency runs along bottom-up columns.\\n\\n    Input structure\\n    The input is a rectangular grid whose colors are all foreground material;\\n    only the number of pixels of each color matters. In the observed task\\n    instances, every present color has a distinct pixel count.\\n\\n    Rule\\n    Count the pixels of each color and order the colors from most frequent to\\n    least frequent. Rewrite a same-size grid by placing each color's full count\\n    as one contiguous run while scanning columns from left to right and, within\\n    each column, from bottom to top.\\n\\n    Key insight\\n    The output preserves the multiset of colors but discards all original\\n    positions, turning the grid into a frequency-sorted column packing.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\n    assert g.ndim == 2\\n\\n    counts = Counter(map(int, g.ravel()))\\n    assert len(set(counts.values())) == len(counts), \\\"color counts must have a unique rank\\\"\\n\\n    colors = sorted(counts, key=lambda color: -counts[color])\\n    out = np.empty_like(g)\\n    height, width = g.shape\\n\\n    scan = ((r, c) for c in range(width) for r in range(height - 1, -1, -1))\\n    for color in colors:\\n        for _ in range(counts[color]):\\n            r, c = next(scan)\\n            out[r, c] = color\\n\\n    return out\\n\\n# --------------- generator (att1) ---------------\\n\\nGRID_SHAPE = (10, 10)\\nGRID_AREA = GRID_SHAPE[0] * GRID_SHAPE[1]\\n\\n# Palette: four distinct foreground colors, no background.\\nCOLOR_POOL = np.arange(1, 10)\\nN_COLORS = 4\\n\\n# Counts: largest, second, third are sampled; smallest is residual.\\nCOUNT_RANGES = ((40, 55), (25, 35), (10, 20))\\nRESIDUAL_COUNT_RANGE = (2, 10)\\nCOUNT_SAMPLE_RETRIES = 100\\nGENERATION_RETRIES = 300\\n\\n\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\n    for _ in range(GENERATION_RETRIES):\\n        result = _gen_attempt()\\n        if result is not None:\\n            try:\\n                out = main(result)\\n            except Exception:\\n                continue\\n            if out is not None:\\n                return result\\n    raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Failed to generate valid input after {GENERATION_RETRIES} attempts\\\")\\n===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/2d0172a1.py\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Convert a rough nested line drawing into a clean canonical frame-and-dot diagram.\\n\\n    Input structure:\\n    - The grid has one background color and one foreground color.\\n    - Foreground 4-connected objects are rough closed frames or small filled blobs.\\n    - Frames may contain other frames/blobs; blobs outside a frame remain outside it.\\n\\n    Rule:\\n    - Detect the containment tree of foreground objects using holes of each frame object.\\n    - Replace every blob with one foreground pixel.\\n    - Replace every frame with a rectangular border padded two cells around its direct children.\\n    - Place siblings by their original row/column overlap and order, with one empty cell between canonical objects.\\n\\n    Key insight: The exact wobbly geometry is irrelevant; only enclosure plus relative sibling positions define the output.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\n    bg = int(get_bg(g))\\n    fg_colors = sorted(set(map(int, g.flatten())) - {bg})\\n    assert len(fg_colors) == 1\\n    fg = int(fg_colors[0])\\n\\n    comps = find_components(g, bg=bg, connectivity=4, monochromatic=True, colors=[fg], return_format=\\\"dict\\\")\\n    assert comps\\n\\n    nodes: list[_Node] = []\\n    holes: list[list[np.ndarray]] = []\\n    for comp in comps:\\n        coords = np.asarray(comp[\\\"coords\\\"], dtype=int)\\n        node = _Node(\\n            coords=coords,\\n            bbox=tuple(map(int, comp[\\\"bbox\\\"])),\\n            center=coords.mean(axis=0),\\n        )\\n        node_holes = _component_holes(g.shape, coords)\\n        node.is_frame = bool(node_holes)\\n        nodes.append(node)\\n        holes.append(node_holes)\\n\\n    assert any(node.is_frame for node in nodes)\\n    for node_i, node in enumerate(nodes):\\n        containers = []\\n        for frame_i, frame in enumerate(nodes):\\n            if node_i == frame_i or not frame.is_frame:\\n                continue\\n            if any(np.all(hole[tuple(node.coords.T)]) for hole in holes[frame_i]):\\n                containers.append(frame)\\n        if containers:\\n            node.parent = min(containers, key=lambda item: int(item.coords.shape[0]))\\n            node.parent.children.append(node)\\n\\n    roots = [node for node in nodes if node.parent is None]\\n    mask = _layout_root(roots)\\n    out = np.full(mask.shape, bg, dtype=int)\\n    out[mask] = fg\\n    return out\\n\\n# --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\\n\\n# ── CFG: tunable generation parameters ──────────────────────────────────────\\n# Grid / canvas bounds\\nGRID_MIN = 16              # minimum grid dimension (rows or cols)\\nGRID_MAX = 25              # maximum grid dimension\\nMAX_EXTRA_PAD = 12         # max total padding beyond drawing extent\\nMAX_PAD_PER_SIDE = 6       # max padding on one side\\n\\n# Frame geometry\\nFRAME_H_RANGE = (7, 20)    # allowed frame bbox height\\nFRAME_W_RANGE = (7, 24)    # allowed frame bbox width\\nFRAME_CORNER_MAX = 5       # max corner wobble displacement\\nFRAME_MIN_EDGE = 2         # min straight-edge length between corners\\nFRAME_TURN_RATIO = (0.34, 0.43)  # acceptable turn-ratio range for wobbly loops\\nFRAME_RETRIES = 60         # retries per frame-mask generation\\n\\n# Blob geometry\\nBLOB_SIZE_RANGE = (4, 11)  # blob pixel count range\\nBLOB_BBOX_RANGE = (2, 5)   # blob bbox dimension range (exclusive upper)\\n\\n# Layout / arrangement\\nARRANGE_GAP_COMPACT = (2, 3)   # inter-sibling gap range (compact mode)\\nARRANGE_GAP_NORMAL = (2, 5)    # inter-sibling gap range (normal mode)\\nARRANGE_EXTRA_SPAN = (0, 4)    # extra span added to cross-axis in arrangement\\nFRAME_MARGIN_RANGE = (3, 5)    # margin around children inside a frame\\nCOMPACT_MARGIN = 3             # fixed margin in compact mode\\n\\n# Outside blob placement\\nOUTSIDE_GAP_RANGE = (2, 5)    # gap between frame and outside blob\\n\\n# Tree structure probabilities\\nDEPTH1_PROB = 0.35             # probability of depth-1 (blobs-only) tree\\nOUTSIDE_BLOB_PROB = 0.35       # probability of having an outside blob\\nDEPTH1_INSIDE_RANGE = (1, 3)   # blobs inside single frame (depth-1)\\nDEPT