置。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:58:  - 各区域的形状和大小不同，但都是由 blue 边界完全封闭的连通区域。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:59:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:60:- `Rule`：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:61:  - 对每个区域，从区域的 blue 边界向内逐层剥离（形态学腐蚀）：第一层是紧贴边界的所有内部黑色像素（即与 blue 像素四方向相邻的黑色像素），第二层是剥去第一层后紧贴新边界的像素，以此类推。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:62:  - 找到种子像素所在的层数 K（即种子距离区域边界的剥离层数）。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:63:  - 将从第 1 层到第 K 层的所有像素都填充为种子的颜色，形成从边界向内的 K 层同心轮廓带。第 K+1 层及更内部的像素保持黑色背景。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:64:  - 种子像素本身保持原色不变。blue 分隔线保持不变。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:65:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:66:- `Key insight`：种子到边界的\\\"层数\\\"通过逐层形态学腐蚀得到——每一层的形状严格跟随区域的不规则轮廓。解题者需要发现种子的位置决定了填充的深度，而填充的图案是区域边界的逐层内缩副本，形成类似等高线的效果。这不是简单的\\\"从种子向外扩散\\\"，而是\\\"从边界向内填充到种子所在深度\\\"。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:67:</new_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:68:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:69:<new_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:70:- `description`：将三面板中各自的对象按面板内对象的大小排名进行跨面板选择与合并，每个面板贡献排名与面板序号对应的那个对象。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:71:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:72:- `Input structure`：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:73:  - 网格被两条垂直的 grey 分隔线等分为三个面板（左、中、右）。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:74:  - 每个面板的背景为黑色，包含恰好三个单色四连通前景对象，颜色可以不同。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:75:  - 三个面板中的对象形状各异，但每个面板内三个对象的面积（像素数）互不相同。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:76:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:77:- `Rule`：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:78:  - 在每个面板内，将三个对象按面积从小到大排列，排名为 1（最小）、2（中等）、3（最大）。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:79:  - 从左面板取排名第 1（最小）的对象，从中面板取排名第 2（中等）的对象，从右面板取排名第 3（最大）的对象。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:80:  - 在一个新的单面板大小的黑色画布上，将这三个被选中的对象按其在各自面板内的原始相对位置放置。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:81:  - 如果放置位置有重叠，后放的对象（右面板的对象最后放置）覆盖先放的。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:82:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:83:- `Key insight`：面板序号（1、2、3）与面积排名（从小到大 1、2、3）形成对应关系——左面板选最小、中面板选中等、右面板选最大。解题者不仅需要发现跨面板选择的机制，还需要归纳出选择依据是面积排名与面板位置的匹配，而非简单的空间位置选择。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:84:</new_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:85:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:86:<new_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:87:- `description`：在由墙壁分割的房间网格中，根据每个房间内标记像素的颜色和数量，选择对应的填充图案模板来铺满该房间。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:88:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:89:- `Input structure`：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:90:  - 背景为黑色。网格中有 maroon 色的墙壁线条将空间分割为若干个不规则的封闭\\\"房间\\\"。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:91:  - 网格上方（墙壁结构之外）有一排图案模板区：每个模板是一个小矩形，内部用某种颜色绘制了一个重复纹理图案（如水平条纹、竖直条纹、棋盘格、对角线等），每个模板的颜色不同。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:92:  - 每个房间内部有 1 到 4 个同色标记像素（颜色与某个模板颜色相同），标记像素散布在房间的不同位置。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:93:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:94:- `Rule`：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:95:  - 标记像素的颜色决定使用哪个图案模板（颜色匹配）。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:96:  - 标记像素的数量决定图案的缩放比例：1 个标记 → 原始模板比例（1x），2 个标记 → 每个模板像素放大为 2x2，3 个标记 → 3x3，4 个标记 → 4x4。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:97:  - 用缩放后的图案平铺填满整个房间区域（从房间的左上角开始平铺，超出房间边界处裁剪）。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:98:  - 标记像素被图案覆盖。模板区在输出中被擦除。maroon 墙壁保持不变。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:99:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:100:- `Key insight`：标记颜色选择图案类型，标记数量控制缩放——这两个独立的属性编码在同一组标记像素中。解题者需要分两步归纳：先发现颜色是模板选择键，再发现数量是缩放因子，两者共同决定最终的填充效果。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:101:</new_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:102:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:103:<new_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:104:- `description`：根据每个前景对象的轮廓凸凹特征，在对象的凹陷处填入从颜色图例中匹配到的颜色。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:105:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:106:- `Input structure`：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:107:  - 背景为黑色。网格中有若干个形状不规则的单色（grey）四连通前景对象。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:108:  - 每个对象的轮廓上有若干处\\\"凹口\\\"——即对象边界向内凹陷形成的缺口，每个凹口的深度（向内凹入的像素层数）为 1 到 4 不等。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:109:  - 网格边缘有颜色图例：四个不同颜色的 1x1 像素从上到下排列，分别对应凹口深度 1、2、3、4。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:110:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:111:- `Rule`：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:112:  - 对每个 grey 对象，识别其轮廓上的所有凹口。凹口定义为：对象边界框内、不属于对象的连通黑色区域，且该区域仅从边界框的一侧与外部背景相连。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:113:  - 测量每个凹口的深度：从凹口开口处向内部延伸的最大像素层数。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:114:  - 用图例中对应深度的颜色填充该凹口区域。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:115:  - 对象本身的 grey 像素保持不变。图例在输出中保留。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:116:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:117:- `Key insight`：解题者需要先建立\\\"凹口\\\"的几何定义——区分真正的凹陷与对象的整体形状特征，然后将凹口深度这一视觉可测量属性映射到颜色图例。难点在于正确识别和测量凹口，而非简单地对对象整体属性进行分类。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed385645705/12/des.md:118:</new_puzzle>\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_123649_seed385645705_resume/6__4.py.jsonl:12:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '8,180p;265,380p' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/58490d8a.py && printf '\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n---FILE-END---\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n' && sed -n '81,470p' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/985ae207.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Count colored objects and record tallies inside a legend box.\\n\\n    Input structure:\\n    - A black rectangular legend box with key-color pixels in its leftmost non-black column.\\n    - Outside the box, distinct objects of each key color are scattered across the grid.\\n\\n    Rule:\\n    - For each key color, count separate same-colored objects outside the legend box.\\n    - Output the legend box repainted: each key row gets one dot per object, spaced every other cell rightward from the key pixel.\\n\\n    Key insight: The legend is both the color index and the output canvas — object counts become dot sequences on the matching row.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\\n    H, W = g.shape\\n    _bg = int(get_bg(g))\\n\\n    black = 0\\n\\n    # STEP 1) Find the legend bbox: largest black CC whose bbox contains some non-black pixels.\\n    best = None  # (area, bbox)\\n    for coords in components_mask(g == int(black), connectivity=8):\\n        if coords.size == 0:\\n            continue\\n        b = bbox_coords(coords)\\n        sub = crop_bbox(g, b)\\n        if (sub != int(black)).any():\\n            area = int(coords.shape[0])\\n            cand = (area, tuple(map(int, b)))\\n            if best is None or cand[0] > best[0]:\\n                best = cand\\n\\n    assert not (best is None)\\n\\n    r0, c0, r1, c1 = map(int, best[1])\\n    box = crop_bbox(g, (r0, c0, r1, c1))\\n    bh, bw = map(int, box.shape)\\n\\n    # STEP 2) Inside the legend bbox, find the key column:\\n    # leftmost column with any non-black pixels (the \\\"key pixels\\\").\\n    key_col = None\\n    for cc in range(bw):\\n        if (box[:, int(cc)] != int(black)).any():\\n            key_col = int(cc)\\n            break\\n    if key_col is None:\\n        return np.zeros_like(box)\\n\\n    keys = [(int(rr), int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)])) for rr in range(bh) if int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)]) != int(black)]\\n    keys.sort(key=lambda t: int(t[0]))\\n\\n    outside = np.ones((H, W), dtype=bool)\\n    outside[int(r0) : int(r1) + 1, int(c0) : int(c1) + 1] = False\\n    out = np.zeros((bh, bw), dtype=int)\\n\\n    # STEP 3/4) Count CCs of each key color outside the legend, then draw 1 dot per CC.\\n    for rr, col in keys:\\n        mask = (g == int(col)) & outside\\n        _labc, nc = label_mask(mask, connectivity=8)\\n        for i in range(int(nc)):\\n            cc = int(key_col + 2 * i)\\n            if 0 <= cc < bw:\\n                out[int(rr), int(cc)] = int(col)\\n\\n    return out\\n\\n# --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\\n\\n# Palette and legend color choices.\\nCOLOR_POOL = tuple(range(1, 10))\\nBLACK = 0\\nDISTRACTOR_PROB = 0.5\\n\\n# Key rows and tally dimensions.\\nKEY_COUNT_RANGE = (2, 4)\\nTARGET_COUNT_RANGE = (1, 5)\\nKEY_ROW_FIRST = 1\\nKEY_ROW_STEP = 2\\nKEY_COLUMN = 1\\nTALLY_COL_STEP = 2\\nLEGEND_HEIGHT_TAIL = 1\\nLEGEND_WIDTH_TAIL = 1\\nLEGEND_SLACK_RANGE = (0, 3)\\n\\n# Canvas size and legend placement bounds.\\nGRID_HEIGHT_RANGE = (20, 25)\\nGRID_WIDTH_RANGE = (20, 25)\\nLEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN = 2\\n\\n# Sprite shape and placement constraints.\\nSPRITE_AREA_RANGE = (4, 7)\\nSPRITE_BBOXES = ((2, 2), (2, 3), (3, 2), (3, 3))\\nSPRITE_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\nSPRITE_PADDING = 1\\nSPRITE_PADDING_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\n\\n# Retry budget for rejection sampling.\\nGENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\\n\\n\\ndef _randint(bounds: tuple[int, int]) -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return an inclusive randint from a configured (low, high) pair.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return random.randint(bounds[0], bounds[1])\\n\\n\\n@lru_cache(maxsize=None)\\ndef _valid_masks(h: int, w: int, area: int) -> tuple[np.ndarray, ...]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return connected masks that span all four sides of the sprite bbox.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    masks = []\\n    for cells in combinations(range(h * w), area):\\n        mask = np.zeros((h, w), dtype=bool)\\n        for cell in cells:\\n            mask[cell // w, cell % w] = True\\n        spans_edges = mask[0, :].any() and mask[-1, :].any() and mask[:, 0].any() and mask[:, -1].any()\\n        if not spans_edges:\\n            continue\\n        _, n = label_mask(mask, connectivity=SPRITE_CONNECTIVITY)\\n        if n == 1:\\n            masks.append(mask)\\n    return tuple(masks)\\n\\n\\ndef _make_sprite(color: int, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Sample one connected same-color sprite drawn on the background color.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    area = _randint(SPRITE_AREA_RANGE)\\n    dims = []\\n    for h, w in SPRITE_BBOXES:\\n        if h * w >= area and _valid_masks(h, w, area):\\n            dims.append((h, w))\\n    h, w = random.choice(dims)\\n    mask = random.choice(_valid_masks(h, w, area))\\n    sprite = np.full((h, w), int(bg), dtype=int)\\n    sprite[mask] = int(color)\\n    return sprite\\n\\n\\ndef _sample_palette() -> tuple[int, list[int], int | None]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Choose background, key colors, and optional distractor color.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    colors = list(COLOR_POOL)\\n    bg = random.choice(colors)\\n\\n    k = _randint(KEY_COUNT_RANGE)\\n    remaining = [c for c in colors if c != bg]\\n    key_colors = random.sample(remaining, k)\\n    remaining = [c for c in remaining if c not in key_colors]\\n    distractor_color = random.choice(remaining) if remaining and random.random() < DISTRACTOR_PROB else None\\n    return bg, key_colors, distractor_color\\n\\n\\ndef _sample_counts(k: int) -> list[int]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Sample the target outside-component count for each key color.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return [_randint(TARGET_COUNT_RANGE) for _ in range(k)]\\n\\n\\ndef _legend_shape(k: int, max_count: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return legend height and width for the key count and largest tally.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    bh = KEY_ROW_STEP * k + LEGEND_HEIGHT_TAIL\\n    bw = TALLY_COL_STEP * max_count + LEGEND_WIDTH_TAIL + _randint(LEGEND_SLACK_RANGE)\\n    return bh, bw\\n\\n\\ndef _key_row(i: int) -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Map a zero-based key index to its row inside the legend/output box.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return KEY_ROW_FIRST + KEY_ROW_STEP * i\\n\\n\\ndef _build_expected(key_colors: list[int], counts: list[int]) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Render the black output tally canvas implied by key colors and counts.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    max_count = max(counts)\\n    bh, bw = _legend_shape(len(key_colors), max_count)\\n\\n    expected = np.full((bh, bw), BLACK, dtype=int)\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\n    for _ in range(GENERATION_ATTEMPTS):\\n        grid = _gen_attempt()\\n        if grid is not None:\\n            return grid\\n    raise RuntimeError(\\\"failed to generate a valid 58490d8a input\\\")\\n\\n\\n---FILE-END---\\n\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Repeat each 3x3 control-center sprite toward the matching solid rectangle until a copy first overlaps that rectangle.\\n\\n    Input structure\\n    - The background is the dominant color.\\n    - Each sprite is a 3x3 foreground object whose eight border pixels have one color and whose center has a different control color.\\n    - For every control color, there is exactly one separate solid rectangular object of that color.\\n\\n    Rule\\n    - Match each sprite to the unique solid rectangle whose color equals the sprite center.\\n    - Copy the whole 3x3 sprite in the cardinal direction of that rectangle, stepping by three cells each time.\\n    - Stop after pasting the first copy whose 3x3 bbox overlaps the rectangle; copied pixels overwrite the rectangle there.\\n\\n    Key insight\\n    The center pixel is not the paint color: it is a destination key, while the entire 3x3 sprite is the motif tiled along the straight path.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\n    assert g.ndim == 2\\n    h, w = g.shape\\n    assert h >= 3 and w >= 3\\n\\n    bg = int(get_bg(g))\\n    sprites = _find_sprites(g, bg)\\n    assert sprites, \\\"expected at least one 3x3 control-center sprite\\\"\\n\\n    out = g.copy()\\n    for sprite_bbox, patch, center in sprites:\\n        targets = _solid_rectangles(g, bg, center)\\n        assert len(targets) == 1, \\\"each control color must have one solid rectangular target\\\"\\n        target_bbox = targets[0][\\\"bbox\\\"]\\n        assert not _intersects(sprite_bbox, target_bbox), \\\"sprite and target must start separate\\\"\\n\\n        dr, dc = _direction_to_target(sprite_bbox, target_bbox)\\n        r, c = sprite_bbox[0], sprite_bbox[1]\\n\\n        while True:\\n            current_bbox = (r, c, r + 2, c + 2)\\n            assert 0 <= r and r + 3 <= h and 0 <= c and c + 3 <= w\\n            paste(out, patch, r, c)\\n\\n            if _intersects(current_bbox, target_bbox):\\n                break\\n\\n            r += dr * 3\\n            c += dc * 3\\n\\n    return out\\n\\n# --------------- generator (att1) ---------------\\n# Canvas and colors.\\nBG_COLOR, COLOR_COUNT = 8, 10\\nGRID_MIN_SIZE, GRID_MAX_SIZE = 20, 25\\n\\n# Rectangles.\\nRECT_COUNT_MIN, RECT_COUNT_MAX = 2, 4\\nRECT_SIDE_MIN, RECT_SIDE_MAX = 2, 14\\nRECT_MARGIN, RECT_SPACING_PAD = 1, 5\\nRECT_PLACEMENT_ATTEMPTS = 50\\n\\n# Sprites and paths.\\nSPRITE_SIZE, SPRITE_TOTAL_MAX = 3, 5\\nSPRITE_GAPS = [1, 4, 7, 10]\\nDIRECTIONS = [(0, 1), (0, -1), (1, 0), (-1, 0)]\\n\\n# Retry limits.\\nGENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\\n\\n\\ndef _intersects_check(a, b):\\n    return not (a[2] < b[0] or b[2] < a[0] or a[3] < b[1] or b[3] < a[1])\\n\\n\\ndef _has_bg_border(grid, sr, sc, bg):\\n    H, W = grid.shape\\n    for r in range(sr, sr + SPRITE_SIZE):\\n        for c in range(sc, sc + SPRITE_SIZE):\\n            for dr, dc in [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]:\\n                nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\\n                if 0 <= nr < H and 0 <= nc < W:\\n                    if not (sr <= nr < sr + SPRITE_SIZE and sc <= nc < sc + SPRITE_SIZE):\\n                        if grid[nr, nc] != bg:\\n                            return False\\n    return True\\n\\n\\ndef _sample_palette(bg):\\n    all_colors = [c for c in range(COLOR_COUNT) if c != bg]\\n    random.shuffle(all_colors)\\n    num_rects = random.randint(RECT_COUNT_MIN, RECT_COUNT_MAX)\\n    body_color = all_colors[0]\\n    target_colors = all_colors[1:1 + num_rects]\\n    return body_color, target_colors\\n\\n\\ndef _rect_has_spacing(rect, rects, pad):\\n    r0, c0, r1, c1 = rect\\n    for rr0, rc0, rr1, rc1, _ in rects:\\n        if not (r1 + pad < rr0 or rr1 + pad < r0 or c1 + pad < rc0 or rc1 + pad < c0):\\n            return False\\n    return True\\n\\n\\ndef _place_rectangles(grid, target_colors):\\n    H, W = grid.shape\\n    rects = []\\n    for color in target_colors:\\n        for _ in range(RECT_PLACEMENT_ATTEMPTS):\\n            rh = random.randint(RECT_SIDE_MIN, min(RECT_SIDE_MAX, H - 4))\\n            rw = random.randint(RECT_SIDE_MIN, min(RECT_SIDE_MAX, W - 4))\\n            r0 = random.randint(RECT_MARGIN, H - rh - RECT_MARGIN)\\n            c0 = random.randint(RECT_MARGIN, W - rw - RECT_MARGIN)\\n            r1 = r0 + rh - 1\\n            c1 = c0 + rw - 1\\n            if _rect_has_spacing((r0, c0, r1, c1), rects, RECT_SPACING_PAD):\\n                rects.append((r0, c0, r1, c1, color))\\n                break\\n        else:\\n            return None\\n    for (r0, c0, r1, c1, color) in rects:\\n        grid[r0:r1 + 1, c0:c1 + 1] = color\\n    return rects\\n\\n\\ndef _assign_sprites(rects):\\n    num_rects = len(rects)\\n    sprite_assignments = []\\n    for i, (_, _, _, _, color) in enumerate(rects):\\n        sprite_assignments.append((i, color))\\n    max_extra = min(SPRITE_TOTAL_MAX - len(sprite_assignments), num_rects)\\n    if max_extra > 0:\\n        extra = random.randint(0, max_extra)\\n        for _ in range(extra):\\n            i = random.randint(0, num_rects - 1)\\n            sprite_assignments.append((i, rects[i][4]))\\n    if len(sprite_assignments) > SPRITE_TOTAL_MAX:\\n        sprite_assignments = sprite_assignments[:SPRITE_TOTAL_MAX]\\n    return sprite_assignments\\n\\n\\ndef _candidate_sprite_position(rect, direction, gap, H, W):\\n    r0, c0, r1, c1, _ = rect\\n    dr, dc = direction\\n    if dr == 0 and dc == 1:\\n        sc = c0 - gap - SPRITE_SIZE\\n        valid_rows = list(range(max(0, r0), min(H - SPRITE_SIZE, r1) + 1))\\n        if not valid_rows:\\n            return None\\n        sr = random.choice(valid_rows)\\n    elif dr == 0 and dc == -1:\\n        sc = c1 + gap + 1\\n        valid_rows = list(range(max(0, r0), min(H - SPRITE_SIZE, r1) + 1))\\n        if not valid_rows:\\n            return None\\n        sr = random.choice(valid_rows)\\n    elif dr == 1 and dc == 0:\\n        sr = r0 - gap - SPRITE_SIZE\\n        valid_cols = list(range(max(0, c0), min(W - SPRITE_SIZE, c1) + 1))\\n        if not valid_cols:\\n            return None\\n        sc = random.choice(valid_cols)\\n    else:\\n        sr = r1 + gap + 1\\n        valid_cols = list(range(max(0, c0), min(W - SPRITE_SIZE, c1) + 1))\\n        if not valid_cols:\\n            return None\\n        sc = random.choice(valid_cols)\\n    return sr, sc\\n\\n\\ndef _sprite_in_bounds(sr, sc, H, W):\\n    return 0 <= sr and sr + SPRITE_SIZE <= H and 0 <= sc and sc + SPRITE_SIZE <= W\\n\\n\\ndef _copy_positions_in_bounds(sr, sc, direction, copies, H, W):\\n    dr, dc = direction\\n    for step in range(1, copies + 1):\\n        nr = sr + dr * SPRITE_SIZE * step\\n        nc = sc + dc * SPRITE_SIZE * step\\n        if not _sprite_in_bounds(nr, nc, H, W):\\n            return False\\n    return True\\n\\n\\ndef _corridor_clear(grid, sr, sc, direction, copies, bg):\\n    dr, dc = direction\\n    for step in range(1, copies):\\n        nr = sr + dr * SPRITE_SIZE * step\\n        nc = sc + dc * SPRITE_SIZE * step\\n        if not np.all(grid[nr:nr + SPRITE_SIZE, nc:nc + SPRITE_SIZE] == bg):\\n            return False\\n    return True\\n\\n\\ndef _last_copy_is_valid(grid, sr, sc, direction, copies, rect, bg):\\n    r0, c0, r1, c1, _ = rect\\n    dr, dc = direction\\n    last_r = sr + dr * SPRITE_SIZE * copies\\n    last_c = sc + dc * SPRITE_SIZE * copies\\n    last_bbox = (last_r, last_c, last_r + SPRITE_SIZE - 1, last_c + SPRITE_SIZE - 1)\\n    if not _intersects_check(last_bbox, (r0, c0, r1, c1)):\\n        return False\\n    for rr in range(last_r, last_r + SPRITE_SIZE):\\n        for cc in range(last_c, last_c + SPRITE_SIZE):\\n            if not (r0 <= rr <= r1 and c0 <= cc <= c1) and grid[rr, cc] != bg:\\n                return False\\n    return True\\n\\n\\ndef _overlaps_placed_sprite(sr, sc, placed_sprites):\\n    for ps_r, ps_c in placed_sprites:\\n        if not (sr + SPRITE_SIZE < ps_r or ps_r + SPRITE_SIZE < sr or sc + SPRITE_SIZE < ps_c or ps_c + SPRITE_SIZE < sc):\\n            return True\\n    return False\\n\\n\\ndef _place_sprite(grid, sr, sc, body_color, center_color):\\n    patch = np.full((SPRITE_SIZE, SPRITE_SIZE), body_color, dtype=int)\\n    patch[SPRITE_SIZE // 2, SPRITE_SIZE // 2] = center_color\\n    grid[sr:sr + SPRITE_SIZE, sc:sc + SPRITE_SIZE] = patch\\n\\n\\ndef _try_place_assigned_sprite(grid, rect, center_color, body_color, placed_sprites, bg):\\n    H, W = grid.shape\\n    directions = DIRECTIONS.copy()\\n    random.shuffle(directions)\\n    for direction in directions:\\n        gaps = SPRITE_GAPS.copy()\\n        random.shuffle(gaps)\\n        for gap in gaps:\\n            copies = gap // SPRITE_SIZE + 1\\n            pos = _candidate_sprite_position(rect, direction, gap, H, W)\\n            if pos is None:\\n                continue\\n            sr, sc = pos\\n            if not _sprite_in_bounds(sr, sc, H, W):\\n                continue\\n            if not _copy_positions_in_bounds(sr, sc, direction, copies, H, W):\\n                continue\\n            if not np.all(grid[sr:sr + SPRITE_SIZE, sc:sc + SPRITE_SIZE] == bg):\\n                continue\\n            if not _has_bg_border(grid, sr, sc, bg):\\n                continue\\n            if not _corridor_clear(grid, sr, sc, direction, copies, bg):\\n                continue\\n            if not _last_copy_is_valid(grid, sr, sc, direction, copies, rect, bg):\\n                continue\\n            if _overlaps_placed_sprite(sr, sc, placed_sprites):\\n                continue\\n            _place_sprite(grid, sr, sc, body_color, center_color)\\n            placed_sprites.append((sr, sc))\\n            return True\\n    return False\\n\\n\\ndef _gen_attempt() -> np.ndarray | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Generate a single input grid for task 985ae207.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    H = random.randint(GRID_MIN_SIZE, GRID_MAX_SIZE)\\n    W = random.randint(GRID_MIN_SIZE, GRID_MAX_SIZE)\\n    bg = BG_COLOR\\n    grid = np.full((H, W), bg, dtype=int)\\n\\n    body_color, target_colors = _sample_palette(bg)\\n    rects = _place_rectangles(grid, target_colors)\\n    if rects is None:\\n        return None\\n\\n    sprite_assignments = _assign_sprites(rects)\\n    placed_sprites = []\\n    for rect_idx, center_color in sprite_assignments:\\n        if not _try_place_assigned_sprite(grid, rects[rect_idx], center_color, body_color, placed_sprites, bg):\\n            return None\\n\\n    try:\\n        main(grid)\\n    except Exception:\\n        return None\\n\\n    return grid\\n\\n\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\n    for _ in range(GENERATION_ATTEMPTS):\\n        result = _gen_attempt()\\n        if result is not None:\\n            return result\\n    raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Failed to generate valid input after {GENERATION_ATTEMPTS} attempts\\\")\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed227494705/11/codegen_prompts/6.md:206:Erase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed227494705/11/codegen_prompts/6.md:214:- Within each object's own bounding box, set foreground pixels in the two leftmost columns to the background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_123649_seed385645705_resume/6__5.py.jsonl:7:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'for f in /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/b1986d4b.py /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/17829a00.py /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/31f7f899.py /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/8abad3cf.py /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/aaecdb9a.py /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/58490d8a.py /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/2ba387bc.py /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/2601afb7.py; do echo \\\"FILE $f\\\"; sed -n '\\\"'/\\\"'^def main/,/''^def generate_input/p'\\\"' \\\\\\\"\\\"'$f\\\"; sed -n '\\\"'/\\\"'^def generate_input/,$p'\\\"' \\\\\\\"\\\"'$f\\\"; done'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"FILE /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/b1986d4b.py\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Render the filled-square object counts as compact nested stacks ordered by count rank.\\n\\n    Input structure\\n    A large noisy grid has a dominant background, scattered non-square noise, and\\n    filled monochrome square objects. Each square side length has exactly one\\n    object color, and side lengths form consecutive sizes.\\n\\n    Rule\\n    Ignore non-square components. If the lowest square in the scene is of the\\n    smallest side length, treat that one smallest square as a distractor and do\\n    not count it. For count rank k from left to right, create one block from all\\n    square sizes with at least k remaining objects; draw larger squares first and\\n    smaller squares over their upper-left corner, then append one background\\n    separator column.\\n\\n    Key insight\\n    The output is a count histogram of square side lengths, but each histogram\\n    slot is rendered as nested upper-left square masks using the side colors.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\n    assert g.ndim == 2, \\\"expected a 2D grid\\\"\\n\\n    bg = get_bg(g)\\n    objects = _square_objects(g, bg)\\n    assert objects, \\\"expected filled square objects\\\"\\n\\n    sides = sorted({obj[\\\"side\\\"] for obj in objects})\\n    assert sides == list(range(sides[0], sides[-1] + 1)), \\\"expected consecutive square side lengths\\\"\\n\\n    by_side = {side: [obj for obj in objects if obj[\\\"side\\\"] == side] for side in sides}\\n    colors = {}\\n    for side, side_objects in by_side.items():\\n        side_colors = {obj[\\\"color\\\"] for obj in side_objects}\\n        assert len(side_colors) == 1, \\\"each side length should have one color\\\"\\n        colors[side] = side_colors.pop()\\n\\n    smallest = sides[0]\\n    lowest_row = max(obj[\\\"bbox\\\"][2] for obj in objects)\\n    lowest_smallest = [obj for obj in by_side[smallest] if obj[\\\"bbox\\\"][2] == lowest_row]\\n    if lowest_smallest:\\n        assert len(lowest_smallest) == 1, \\\"expected at most one lowest smallest distractor\\\"\\n        drop_bbox = lowest_smallest[0][\\\"bbox\\\"]\\n        by_side[smallest] = [obj for obj in by_side[smallest] if obj[\\\"bbox\\\"] != drop_bbox]\\n\\n    counts = {side: len(side_objects) for side, side_objects in by_side.items()}\\n    assert all(count > 0 for count in counts.values()), \\\"each square size should remain represented\\\"\\n\\n    out_h = sides[-1] + 1\\n    groups = []\\n    for rank in range(max(counts.values())):\\n        present_sides = [side for side in sides if counts[side] > rank]\\n        assert present_sides, \\\"rank should contain at least one square size\\\"\\n\\n        group_w = max(present_sides)\\n        group = np.full((out_h, group_w), bg, dtype=int)\\n        for side in sorted(present_sides, reverse=True):\\n            group[:side, :side] = colors[side]\\n        groups.append(group)\\n\\n    out_w = sum(group.shape[1] + 1 for group in groups)\\n    out = np.full((out_h, out_w), bg, dtype=int)\\n    c = 0\\n    for group in groups:\\n        w = group.shape[1]\\n        out[:, c : c + w] = group\\n        c += w + 1\\n\\n    return out\\n\\n# --------------- generator (att1) ---------------\\n\\nSIDES = [2, 3, 4]\\nALL_COLORS = list(range(10))\\n\\n# Canvas and object bounds.\\nGRID_SIZE_RANGE = (25, 28)\\nCOUNT_RANGE = (2, 6)\\nSQUARE_GAP = 1\\n\\n# Noise and distractor controls.\\nDISTRACTOR_PROB = 0.5\\nNOISE_COUNT_RANGE = (40, 70)\\n\\n# Retry budget.\\nMAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\\n\\n\\ndef _choose_palette() -> tuple[int, dict[int, int], int]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Choose one background, three square colors, and one noise color.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    bg = random.choice(ALL_COLORS)\\n    non_bg = [c for c in ALL_COLORS if c != bg]\\n    random.shuffle(non_bg)\\n    square_colors = {side: non_bg[i] for i, side in enumerate(SIDES)}\\n    return bg, square_colors, non_bg[len(SIDES)]\\n\\n\\ndef _make_square_queue(\\n    counts: dict[int, int], square_colors: dict[int, int], has_distractor: bool\\n) -> tuple[list[tuple[int, int]], tuple[int, int] | None]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return regular squares plus the separately placed distractor candidate.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    squares = [(side, square_colors[side]) for side in SIDES for _ in range(counts[side])]\\n    if has_distractor:\\n        squares.append((SIDES[0], square_colors[SIDES[0]]))\\n\\n    random.shuffle(squares)\\n    if not has_distractor:\\n        return squares, None\\n    return squares[:-1], squares[-1]\\n\\n\\ndef _free_positions(occupied: np.ndarray, side: int, min_r: int = 0) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"List top-left positions whose padded square footprint is unoccupied.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    H, W = occupied.shape\\n    valid = []\\n    for r in range(min_r, H - side + 1):\\n        for c in range(0, W - side + 1):\\n            r0 = max(0, r - SQUARE_GAP)\\n            r1 = min(H, r + side + SQUARE_GAP)\\n            c0 = max(0, c - SQUARE_GAP)\\n            c1 = min(W, c + side + SQUARE_GAP)\\n            if not occupied[r0:r1, c0:c1].any():\\n                valid.append((r, c))\\n    return valid\\n\\n\\ndef _mark_occupied(occupied: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, side: int) -> None:\\n    H, W = occupied.shape\\n    r0 = max(0, r - SQUARE_GAP)\\n    r1 = min(H, r + side + SQUARE_GAP)\\n    c0 = max(0, c - SQUARE_GAP)\\n    c1 = min(W, c + side + SQUARE_GAP)\\n    occupied[r0:r1, c0:c1] = True\\n\\n\\ndef _place_square(\\n    grid: np.ndarray,\\n    occupied: np.ndarray,\\n    placed: list[tuple[int, int, int, int]],\\n    side: int,\\n    color: int,\\n    positions: list[tuple[int, int]] | None = None,\\n) -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Place one square at a random valid position and update grid state.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    valid = _free_positions(occupied, side) if positions is None else positions\\n    if not valid:\\n        return False\\n    r, c = random.choice(valid)\\n    grid[r:r + side, c:c + side] = color\\n    _mark_occupied(occupied, r, c, side)\\n    placed.append((r, c, side, color))\\n    return True\\n\\n\\ndef _place_squares(\\n    grid: np.ndarray,\\n    occupied: np.ndarray,\\n    regular_squares: list[tuple[int, int]],\\n    distractor_sq: tuple[int, int] | None,\\n) -> list[tuple[int, int, int, int]] | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Place all squares, requiring any distractor to sit below the others.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    placed = []\\n\\n    random.shuffle(regular_squares)\\n    for side, color in regular_squares:\\n        if not _place_square(grid, occupied, placed, side, color):\\n            return None\\n\\n    if distractor_sq is None:\\n        return placed\\n\\n    d_side, d_color = distractor_sq\\n    current_max_bottom = max(r + side - 1 for r, _, side, _ in placed) if placed else -1\\n    min_r = max(0, current_max_bottom - d_side + 2)\\n    valid = [\\n        (r, c)\\n        for r, c in _free_positions(occupied, d_side, min_r=min_r)\\n        if r + d_side - 1 > current_max_bottom\\n    ]\\n    if not _place_square(grid, occupied, placed, d_side, d_color, valid):\\n        return None\\n    return placed\\n\\n\\ndef _add_noise(grid: np.ndarray, bg: int, noise_color: int) -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Scatter noise onto background cells only.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    free_cells = list(zip(*np.where(grid == bg)))\\n    num_noise = random.randint(*NOISE_COUNT_RANGE)\\n    if len(free_cells) < num_noise:\\n        return False\\n    random.shuffle(free_cells)\\n    for r, c in free_cells[:num_noise]:\\n        grid[r, c] = noise_color\\n    return True\\n\\n\\ndef _would_trigger_unintended_distractor(placed: list[tuple[int, int, int, int]]) -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Detect no-distractor samples where the solver would drop a small square.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    lowest_row = max(r + side - 1 for r, _, side, _ in placed)\\n    return any(side == SIDES[0] and r + side - 1 == lowest_row for r, _, side, _ in placed)\\n\\n\\ndef _render_expected_output(\\n    bg: int, counts: dict[int, int], square_colors: dict[int, int]\\n) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Render the count-derived oracle output used to validate samples.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    out_h = SIDES[-1] + 1\\n    groups = []\\n    for rank in range(max(counts.values())):\\n        present_sides = [side for side in SIDES if counts[side] > rank]\\n        group = np.full((out_h, max(present_sides)), bg, dtype=int)\\n        for side in sorted(present_sides, reverse=True):\\n            group[:side, :side] = square_colors[side]\\n        groups.append(group)\\n\\n    out_w = sum(group.shape[1] + 1 for group in groups)\\n    out = np.full((out_h, out_w), bg, dtype=int)\\n    c = 0\\n    for group in groups:\\n        w = group.shape[1]\\n        out[:, c:c + w] = group\\n        c += w + 1\\n    return out\\n\\n\\ndef _gen_attempt() -> np.ndarray | None:\\n    bg, square_colors, noise_color = _choose_palette()\\n    counts = {side: random.randint(*COUNT_RANGE) for side in SIDES}\\n    has_distractor = random.random() < DISTRACTOR_PROB\\n    regular_squares, distractor_sq = _make_square_queue(counts, square_colors, has_distractor)\\n\\n    H = random.randint(*GRID_SIZE_RANGE)\\n    W = random.randint(*GRID_SIZE_RANGE)\\n    grid = np.full((H, W), bg, dtype=int)\\n    occupied = np.zeros((H, W), dtype=bool)\\n\\n    placed = _place_squares(grid, occupied, regular_squares, distractor_sq)\\n    if placed is None or not _add_noise(grid, bg, noise_color):\\n        return None\\n\\n    if not has_distractor and _would_trigger_unintended_distractor(placed):\\n        return None\\n\\n    expected_out = _render_expected_output(bg, counts, square_colors)\\n\\n    try:\\n        actual_out = main(grid)\\n    except Exception:\\n        return None\\n\\n    if not np.array_equal(actual_out, expected_out):\\n        return None\\n\\n    return grid\\n\\n\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\n    for _ in range(MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS):\\n        result = _gen_attempt()\\n        if result is not None:\\n            return result\\n    raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Failed to generate input after {MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS} attempts\\\")\\nFILE /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/17829a00.py\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Move each colored object vertically until it touches the matching top or bottom border bar.\\n\\n    Input structure:\\n    - The background is the dominant color.\\n    - The top row is a full-width bar in one foreground color and the bottom row is a full-width bar in another.\\n    - All other foreground pixels are 8-connected monochrome objects whose color matches one of those bars.\\n\\n    Rule:\\n    - Top-bar-colored objects move upward so their bbox top is row 1.\\n    - Bottom-bar-colored objects move downward so their bbox bottom is the row above the bottom bar.\\n    - A downward-moving one-column segment whose landing overlaps its source becomes the continuous vertical segment swept between them.\\n\\n    Key insight:\\n    The horizontal bars are destination anchors: color determines which border an object slides toward, while columns and object shape are otherwise preserved.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\n    assert g.ndim == 2\\n    h, w = g.shape\\n    assert h >= 3 and w >= 1\\n\\n    bg = int(get_bg(g))\\n    top_color = int(g[0, 0])\\n    bottom_color = int(g[h - 1, 0])\\n\\n    assert top_color != bg\\n    assert bottom_color != bg\\n    assert top_color != bottom_color\\n    assert bool(np.all(g[0, :] == top_color))\\n    assert bool(np.all(g[h - 1, :] == bottom_color))\\n    assert set(map(int, np.unique(g))) == {bg, top_color, bottom_color}\\n\\n    for c in range(w):\\n        top_rows = [r for r in range(1, h - 1) if int(g[r, c]) == top_color]\\n        bot_rows = [r for r in range(1, h - 1) if int(g[r, c]) == bottom_color]\\n        if top_rows and bot_rows:\\n            assert max(top_rows) < min(bot_rows), \\\"top-color objects must be above bottom-color objects in every column\\\"\\n\\n    out = np.full_like(g, bg)\\n    out[0, :] = top_color\\n    out[h - 1, :] = bottom_color\\n\\n    for color, target_side in ((top_color, \\\"top\\\"), (bottom_color, \\\"bottom\\\")):\\n        components = find_components(\\n            g,\\n            bg=bg,\\n            connectivity=8,\\n            monochromatic=True,\\n            colors=[color],\\n            return_format=\\\"dict\\\",\\n        )\\n        for comp in components:\\n            if _is_full_width_border(comp, h, w):\\n                continue\\n\\n            coords = np.asarray(comp[\\\"coords\\\"], dtype=int)\\n            r0, c0, r1, c1 = map(int, comp[\\\"bbox\\\"])\\n            assert 0 < r0 <= r1 < h - 1\\n\\n            if target_side == \\\"top\\\":\\n                dr = 1 - r0\\n                assert dr <= 0\\n                paint = coords + np.array([dr, 0], dtype=int)\\n            else:\\n                dr = (h - 2) - r1\\n                assert dr >= 0\\n                paint = coords + np.array([dr, 0], dtype=int)\\n                if dr > 0 and r0 + dr <= r1:\\n                    assert c0 == c1\\n                    rows = np.arange(r0, r1 + dr + 1, dtype=int)\\n                    paint = np.column_stack([rows, np.full(rows.shape, c0, dtype=int)])\\n\\n            assert bool(np.all((0 <= paint[:, 0]) & (paint[:, 0] < h)))\\n            assert bool(np.all((0 <= paint[:, 1]) & (paint[:, 1] < w)))\\n            assert bool(np.all(out[paint[:, 0], paint[:, 1]] == bg))\\n            out[paint[:, 0], paint[:, 1]] = color\\n\\n    return out\\n\\n# --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\\n\\nfrom scipy.ndimage import binary_dilation\\n\\n# -- Grid constants --\\nBG = 7\\nH = 16\\nW = 16\\n\\n# -- Sprite geometry --\\nSPRITE_AREA_MIN = 1\\nSPRITE_AREA_MAX = 6\\nSPRITE_H_MAX = 4       # bbox height upper bound (exclusive in range)\\nSPRITE_W_MAX = 5       # bbox width upper bound (exclusive in range)\\nSPRITE_DENSITY_MIN = 0.33  # min fill ratio inside bbox\\n\\n# -- Object counts per side --\\nOBJ_COUNT_MIN = 3      # per color\\nOBJ_COUNT_MAX = 5      # per color (inclusive)\\nOBJ_TOTAL_MAX = 9      # top_count + bottom_count\\n\\n# -- Swept segment (single-column overlap case) --\\nSWEPT_PROB = 0.15       # probability of including one swept-segment object\\nSWEPT_H_MIN = 2        # min input height for swept column\\nSWEPT_H_MAX = 4        # max input height (inclusive)\\nSWEPT_TOTAL_MAX = 5    # input_h + offset ceiling\\n\\n# -- Input derivation --\\nSLIDE_OFFSET_MAX = 10  # exclusive upper bound for slide offsets (range(1, N))\\n\\n# -- Retry budgets --\\nPLACE_RETRIES = 60     # sprite placement attempts per object\\nGEN_RETRIES = 300      # outer generation attempts\\n\\n\\ndef _corner_path(h: int, w: int) -> set[tuple[int, int]]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Generate a diagonal path from one corner of an (h,w) bbox to the opposite.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if h == 1 and w == 1:\\n        return {(0, 0)}\\n    r0 = random.choice([0, h - 1])\\n    c0 = random.choice([0, w - 1])\\n    r1 = h - 1 - r0\\n    c1 = w - 1 - c0\\n    steps = max(h, w)\\n    cells: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\\n    for k in range(steps):\\n        t = 0.0 if steps == 1 else k / (steps - 1)\\n        cells.add((int(round(r0 + (r1 - r0) * t)),\\n                    int(round(c0 + (c1 - c0) * t))))\\n    return cells\\n\\n\\ndef _random_sprite(color: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Create a small random 8-connected sprite with the given color on BG.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    area = random.randint(SPRITE_AREA_MIN, SPRITE_AREA_MAX)\\n    choices = [\\n        (sh, sw)\\n        for sh in range(1, SPRITE_H_MAX + 1)\\n        for sw in range(1, SPRITE_W_MAX + 1)\\n        if max(sh, sw) <= area <= sh * sw\\n        and area / (sh * sw) >= SPRITE_DENSITY_MIN\\n    ]\\n    sh, sw = random.choice(choices)\\n    cells = _corner_path(sh, sw)\\n    while len(cells) < area:\\n        frontier = []\\n        for r, c in cells:\\n            for dr in (-1, 0, 1):\\n                for dc in (-1, 0, 1):\\n                    if dr == 0 and dc == 0:\\n                        continue\\n                    rr, cc = r + dr, c + dc\\n                    if 0 <= rr < sh and 0 <= cc < sw and (rr, cc) not in cells:\\n                        frontier.append((rr, cc))\\n        cells.add(random.choice(frontier))\\n\\n    sprite = np.full((sh, sw), BG, dtype=int)\\n    rs, cs = zip(*cells)\\n    sprite[rs, cs] = color\\n    return sprite\\n\\n\\ndef _coords_from_patch(patch: np.ndarray, r0: int, c0: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return (N,2) absolute coords of non-BG pixels in patch placed at (r0,c0).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return np.argwhere(patch != BG) + np.array([r0, c0], dtype=int)\\n\\n\\ndef _is_bar(comp: dict) -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"True if a component dict represents a full-width border bar.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    r0, c0, r1, c1 = map(int, comp[\\\"bbox\\\"])\\n    return (\\n        int(comp[\\\"area\\\"]) == W\\n        and r0 == r1\\n        and c0 == 0\\n        and c1 == W - 1\\n        and r0 in {0, H - 1}\\n    )\\n\\n\\ndef _object_count(grid: np.ndarray, color: int) -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Count non-bar objects of the given color.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    comps = find_components(\\n        grid, bg=BG, connectivity=8, monochromatic=True,\\n        colors=[color], return_format=\\\"dict\\\",\\n    )\\n    return sum(1 for comp in comps if not _is_bar(comp))\\n\\n\\n_STRUCT8 = np.ones((3, 3), dtype=bool)\\n\\n\\ndef _touches_same(mask: np.ndarray, coords: np.ndarray) -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Check if any coord is 8-adjacent to an existing same-color pixel.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    probe = np.zeros((H, W), dtype=bool)\\n    probe[coords[:, 0], coords[:, 1]] = True\\n    dilated = binary_dilation(probe, structure=_STRUCT8)\\n    dilated[coords[:, 0], coords[:, 1]] = False  # exclude the coords themselves\\n    return bool((dilated & mask).any())\\n\\n\\ndef _place_output_object(out: np.ndarray, color: int, side: str) -> dict | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Try to place a random sprite on the output grid touching the bar on `side`.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    for _ in range(PLACE_RETRIES):\\n        patch = _random_sprite(color)\\n        ph, pw = map(int, patch.shape)\\n        r0 = 1 if side == \\\"top\\\" else H - 1 - ph\\n        cols = list(range(0, W - pw + 1))\\n        random.shuffle(cols)\\n        for c0 in cols:\\n            coords = _coords_from_patch(patch, r0, c0)\\n            if bool(np.all(out[coords[:, 0], coords[:, 1]] == BG)):\\n                paste(out, patch, r0, c0, transparent=BG)\\n                return {\\n                    \\\"color\\\": color, \\\"side\\\": side, \\\"coords\\\": coords,\\n                    \\\"height\\\": ph, \\\"width\\\": pw, \\\"special\\\": False,\\n                }\\n    return None\\n\\n\\ndef _place_swept_output_object(out: np.ndarray, color: int) -> dict | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Try to place a single-column swept-segment bottom object.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    choices = [\\n        (input_h, offset)\\n        for input_h in range(SWEPT_H_MIN, SWEPT_H_MAX + 1)\\n        for offset in range(1, input_h)\\n        if input_h + offset <= SWEPT_TOTAL_MAX\\n    ]\\n    random.shuffle(choices)\\n    cols = list(range(W))\\n    random.shuffle(cols)\\n    for input_h, offset in choices:\\n        out_h = input_h + offset\\n        patch = np.full((out_h, 1), color, dtype=int)\\n        r0 = H - 1 - out_h\\n        for c0 in cols:\\n            coords = _coords_from_patch(patch, r0, c0)\\n            if bool(np.all(out[coords[:, 0], coords[:, 1]] == BG)):\\n                paste(out, patch, r0, c0, transparent=BG)\\n                input_rows = np.arange(r0, r0 + input_h, dtype=int)\\n                input_coords = np.column_stack(\\n                    [input_rows, np.full(input_rows.shape, c0, dtype=int)]\\n                )\\n                return {\\n                    \\\"color\\\": color, \\\"side\\\": \\\"bottom\\\", \\\"coords\\\": coords,\\n                    \\\"input_coords\\\": input_coords,\\n                    \\\"height\\\": input_h, \\\"width\\\": 1, \\\"special\\\": True,\\n                }\\n    return None\\n\\n\\ndef _can_paint_input(\\n    occupied: np.ndarray, color_mask: np.ndarray, coords: np.ndarray\\n) -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Check that coords are unoccupied and not 8-adjacent to same-color pixels.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if not bool(np.all(occupied[coords[:, 0], coords[:, 1]] == 0)):\\n        return False\\n    return not _touches_same(color_mask, coords)\\n\\n\\ndef _check_column_order(\\n    coords: np.ndarray, color: int, top_color: int,\\n    top_max: np.ndarray, bot_min: np.ndarray,\\n) -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Verify that placing coords respects per-column top/bottom ordering.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    rs, cs = coords[:, 0], coords[:, 1]\\n    if color == top_color:\\n        return bool(np.all(rs < bot_min[cs]))\\n    return bool(np.all(rs > top_max[cs]))\\n\\n\\ndef _update_column_bounds(\\n    coords: np.ndarray, color: int, top_color: int,\\n    top_max: np.ndarray, bot_min: np.ndarray,\\n) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Update per-column top_max / bot_min after placing coords.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    for r, c in coords:\\n        r, c = int(r), int(c)\\n        if color == top_color:\\n            top_max[c] = max(top_max[c], r)\\n        else:\\n            bot_min[c] = min(bot_min[c], r)\\n\\n\\ndef _derive_input(\\n    objects: list[dict], top_color: int, bottom_color: int,\\n) -> np.ndarray | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Slide output objects away from their bars to produce a valid input grid.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    inp = np.full((H, W), BG, dtype=int)\\n    inp[0, :] = top_color\\n    inp[H - 1, :] = bottom_color\\n    occupied = inp != BG\\n    masks = {top_color: inp == top_color, bottom_color: inp == bottom_color}\\n\\n    top_max = np.full(W, 0, dtype=int)\\n    bot_min = np.full(W, H - 1, dtype=int)\\n\\n    ordered = objects[:]\\n    random.shuffle(ordered)\\n    for obj in ordered:\\n        color = int(obj[\\\"color\\\"])\\n        if obj[\\\"special\\\"]:\\n            coord_choices = [obj[\\\"input_coords\\\"]]\\n        elif obj[\\\"side\\\"] == \\\"top\\\":\\n            offsets = list(range(1, SLIDE_OFFSET_MAX))\\n            random.shuffle(offsets)\\n            coord_choices = [obj[\\\"coords\\\"] + np.array([off, 0], dtype=int) for off in offsets]\\n        else:\\n            min_offset = int(obj[\\\"height\\\"])\\n            offsets = list(range(min_offset, SLIDE_OFFSET_MAX))\\n            random.shuffle(offsets)\\n            coord_choices = [obj[\\\"coords\\\"] - np.array([off, 0], dtype=int) for off in offsets]\\n\\n        placed = False\\n        for coords in coord_choices:\\n            if not bool(np.all((1 <= coords[:, 0]) & (coords[:, 0] <= H - 2))):\\n                continue\\n            if not _check_column_order(coords, color, top_color, top_max, bot_min):\\n                continue\\n            if _can_paint_input(occupied, masks[color], coords):\\n                inp[coords[:, 0], coords[:, 1]] = color\\n                occupied[coords[:, 0], coords[:, 1]] = True\\n                masks[color][coords[:, 0], coords[:, 1]] = True\\n                _update_column_bounds(coords, color, top_color, top_max, bot_min)\\n                placed = True\\n                break\\n        if not placed:\\n            return None\\n\\n    return inp\\n\\n\\ndef _gen_attempt() -> np.ndarray | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Single attempt: build output grid, then derive a valid input.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    colors = [c for c in range(10) if c != BG]\\n    top_color, bottom_color = random.sample(colors, 2)\\n\\n    count_pairs = [\\n        (a, b)\\n        for a in range(OBJ_COUNT_MIN, OBJ_COUNT_MAX + 1)\\n        for b in range(OBJ_COUNT_MIN, OBJ_COUNT_MAX + 1)\\n        if a + b <= OBJ_TOTAL_MAX\\n    ]\\n    top_count, bottom_count = random.choice(count_pairs)\\n    include_swept = random.random() < SWEPT_PROB\\n\\n    out = np.full((H, W), BG, dtype=int)\\n    out[0, :] = top_color\\n    out[H - 1, :] = bottom_color\\n\\n    objects: list[dict] = []\\n    for _ in range(top_count):\\n        obj = _place_output_object(out, top_color, \\\"top\\\")\\n        if obj is None:\\n            return None\\n        objects.append(obj)\\n\\n    if include_swept:\\n        obj = _place_swept_output_object(out, bottom_color)\\n        if obj is None:\\n            return None\\n        objects.append(obj)\\n\\n    for _ in range(bottom_count - int(include_swept)):\\n        obj = _place_output_object(out, bottom_color, \\\"bottom\\\")\\n        if obj is None:\\n            return None\\n        objects.append(obj)\\n\\n    inp = _derive_input(objects, top_color, bottom_color)\\n    if inp is None:\\n        return None\\n    if _object_count(inp, top_color) != top_count:\\n        return None\\n    if _object_count(inp, bottom_color) != bottom_count:\\n        return None\\n    if not np.array_equal(main(inp), out):\\n        return None\\n    return inp\\n\\n\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\n    for _ in range(GEN_RETRIES):\\n        grid = _gen_attempt()\\n        if grid is not None:\\n            return grid\\n    raise RuntimeError(\\\"failed to generate a valid 17829a00 input\\\")\\nFILE /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/31f7f899.py\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Sort vertical bars by height and redistribute them across fixed colored slots.\\n\\n    Input structure:\\n    - bg background; a horizontal base line of a single color spans the full grid width.\\n    - Several monochrome vertical bars of distinct colors rise upward from the base line.\\n\\n    Rule:\\n    - Rank bar shapes by height (shortest to tallest).\\n    - Rank original x-positions (slots) left to right.\\n    - Place the i-th shortest shape into the i-th leftmost slot, recoloring it to that slot's original color.\\n    - The base line is preserved unchanged.\\n\\n    Key insight: Each slot keeps its x-position and color identity; only the bar silhouettes are redistributed among slots by height order.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\\n    H, W = g.shape\\n    bg = int(get_bg(g))\\n\\n    # Base row/color = (row,color) with maximal count on that row (excluding bg).\\n    best = None  # (count, row, color)\\n    for r in range(H):\\n        vals, counts = np.unique(g[r, :], return_counts=True)\\n        for v, cnt in zip(vals, counts):\\n            v = int(v)\\n            cnt = int(cnt)\\n            if v == bg:\\n                continue\\n            if best is None or cnt > best[0]:\\n                best = (cnt, int(r), int(v))\\n    assert not (best is None)\\n    _cnt, base_r, base_col = best\\n\\n    objects: list[dict[str, object]] = []\\n    for comp in find_components(g, bg=bg, connectivity=4, monochromatic=True, return_format=\\\"dict\\\"):\\n        col = int(comp[\\\"color\\\"])\\n        if col in {int(bg), int(base_col)}:\\n            continue\\n\\n        pts = comp[\\\"coords\\\"]\\n        b = comp[\\\"bbox\\\"]\\n        height = int(bbox_h(b))\\n\\n        base_cols = sorted(int(c) for r, c in pts if int(r) == int(base_r))\\n        if base_cols:\\n            anchor = int(base_cols[len(base_cols) // 2])\\n        else:\\n            cols_sorted = sorted(int(c) for _r, c in pts)\\n            anchor = int(cols_sorted[len(cols_sorted) // 2])\\n\\n        rel = [(int(r) - int(base_r), int(c) - int(anchor)) for r, c in pts]\\n        objects.append(\\n            {\\n                \\\"color\\\": int(col),\\n                \\\"anchor\\\": int(anchor),\\n                \\\"height\\\": int(height),\\n                \\\"size\\\": int(len(rel)),\\n                \\\"rel\\\": rel,\\n            }\\n        )\\n\\n    # Slots are determined by original x-positions; slot colors must be preserved.\\n    slots = sorted(objects, key=lambda o: (int(o[\\\"anchor\\\"]), int(o[\\\"color\\\"])))\\n    # Shapes are ordered by height (shortest -> tallest).\\n    shapes = sorted(objects, key=lambda o: (int(o[\\\"height\\\"]), int(o[\\\"size\\\"]), int(o[\\\"anchor\\\"]), int(o[\\\"color\\\"])))\\n\\n    out = np.full_like(g, bg)\\n    out[int(base_r), :] = int(base_col)\\n\\n    for slot, shape in zip(slots, shapes):\\n        slot_col = int(slot[\\\"color\\\"])\\n        slot_anchor = int(slot[\\\"anchor\\\"])\\n        for dr, dc in shape[\\\"rel\\\"]:\\n            rr = int(base_r) + int(dr)\\n            cc = int(slot_anchor) + int(dc)\\n            if 0 <= rr < H and 0 <= cc < W:\\n                out[rr, cc] = int(slot_col)\\n\\n    return out\\n\\n# --------------- generator (Codex#3) ---------------\\n\\ndef _rand_composition(total: int, parts: int) -> list[int]:\\n    return [int(x) for x in np.random.multinomial(int(total), np.full(int(parts), 1.0 / int(parts)))]\\n\\n\\ndef _slot_lefts(n: int, k: int, width: int) -> list[int]:\\n    used = int(k * width + (k - 1))\\n    extra = int(n - used)\\n    if extra < 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"bars do not fit\\\")\\n    gaps = _rand_composition(extra, k + 1)\\n    lefts: list[int] = []\\n    c = int(gaps[0])\\n    for i in range(k):\\n        lefts.append(int(c))\\n        c += int(width)\\n        if i < k - 1:\\n            c += 1 + int(gaps[i + 1])\\n    return lefts\\n\\n\\ndef _draw_scene(n: int, base_r: int, base_color: int, bg: int, lefts: list[int], width: int, colors: list[int], heights: list[int]) -> np.ndarray:\\n    grid = np.full((n, n), int(bg), dtype=int)\\n    grid[base_r, :] = int(base_color)\\n    for left, color, height in zip(lefts, colors, heights):\\n        patch = np.full((int(height), int(width)), int(color), dtype=int)\\n        paste(grid, patch, int(base_r - height // 2), int(left))\\n    return grid\\n\\n\\ndef _gen_attempt() -> np.ndarray | None:\\n    n = int(np.random.choice(np.arange(7, 18, 2)))\\n    base_r = n // 2\\n    bg = 8\\n    base_color = 6\\n\\n    height_choices = list(range(1, min(n, 11) + 1, 2))\\n    max_count = min(5, len(height_choices), (n + 1) // 2)\\n    if max_count < 3:\\n        return None\\n    k = int(np.random.randint(3, max_count + 1))\\n\\n    feasible_widths = [1]\\n    if n - 3 * k > 3 and n >= 4 * k - 1:\\n        feasible_widths.append(3)\\n    width = int(np.random.choice(feasible_widths))\\n\\n    lefts = _slot_lefts(n, k, width)\\n    colors = [int(c) for c in np.random.choice([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 9], size=k, replace=False)]\\n\\n    sorted_heights = sorted(int(h) for h in np.random.choice(height_choices, size=k, replace=False))\\n    out = _draw_scene(n, base_r, base_color, bg, lefts, width, colors, sorted_heights)\\n\\n    perm = np.random.permutation(k)\\n    if np.array_equal(perm, np.arange(k)):\\n        a, b = np.random.choice(k, size=2, replace=False)\\n        perm[a], perm[b] = perm[b], perm[a]\\n    in_heights = [int(sorted_heights[i]) for i in perm]\\n    inp = _draw_scene(n, base_r, base_color, bg, lefts, width, colors, in_heights)\\n\\n    if np.array_equal(inp, out):\\n        return None\\n    if not np.array_equal(main(inp), out):\\n        return None\\n    return inp\\n\\n\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\n    for _ in range(300):\\n        result = _gen_attempt()\\n        if result is not None:\\n            return result\\n    raise RuntimeError(\\\"generate_input failed after 300 attempts\\\")\\nFILE /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/8abad3cf.py\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Repack each non-background color group as a solid square ordered by increasing size.\\n\\n    Input structure\\n    The grid has one dominant background color, and each other color has a\\n    perfect-square pixel count. Those square side lengths are unique.\\n\\n    Rule\\n    Convert every non-background color into a filled square whose side length is\\n    the square root of its pixel count. Place the squares from left to right in\\n    increasing side length, bottom-aligned, with one background column between\\n    neighboring squares.\\n\\n    Key insight\\n    The original geometry of each color is discarded; only the color's total\\n    pixel count determines the size of its packed output square.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\n    bg = get_bg(g)\\n\\n    specs: list[tuple[int, int]] = []\\n    for color in colors_present(g, exclude={bg}):\\n        count = int(np.count_nonzero(g == color))\\n        side = math.isqrt(count)\\n        assert side * side == count\\n        specs.append((color, side))\\n\\n    assert specs\\n    sides = [side for _color, side in specs]\\n    assert len(set(sides)) == len(sides)\\n\\n    ordered = sorted(specs, key=lambda item: item[1])\\n    height = max(side for _color, side in ordered)\\n    width = sum(side for _color, side in ordered) + len(ordered) - 1\\n    out = np.full((height, width), bg, dtype=int)\\n\\n    col = 0\\n    for i, (color, side) in enumerate(ordered):\\n        out[height - side : height, col : col + side] = color\\n        col += side\\n        if i != len(ordered) - 1:\\n            col += 1\\n\\n    assert col == width\\n    return out\\n\\n# --------------- generator (att1) ---------------\\n\\n# Fixed task palette/background.\\nBG_COLOR = 7\\nALL_COLORS = range(10)\\n\\n# Color-group structure.\\nCOLOR_COUNTS = [2, 3]\\nSIDE_LENGTHS = range(1, 6)\\n\\n# Input canvas and density bounds.\\nROW_RANGE = range(5, 8)\\nCOL_RANGE = range(4, 11)\\nMIN_BG_FRACTION = 0.42\\nMAX_BG_FRACTION = 0.58\\n\\n# Retry budget.\\nMAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\\n\\n\\ndef _sample_groups() -> tuple[list[int], list[int]]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return colors and distinct square sides using the original sampling order.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    n_colors = random.choice(COLOR_COUNTS)\\n    sides = sorted(random.sample(SIDE_LENGTHS, n_colors))\\n    available_colors = [c for c in ALL_COLORS if c != BG_COLOR]\\n    colors = random.sample(available_colors, n_colors)\\n    return colors, sides\\n\\n\\ndef _valid_dimensions(total_pixels: int) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\\n    min_area = max(total_pixels + 1, int(np.ceil(total_pixels / MAX_BG_FRACTION)))\\n    max_area = int(np.floor(total_pixels / MIN_BG_FRACTION))\\n    if min_area > max_area:\\n        return []\\n\\n    return [\\n        (rows, cols)\\n        for rows in ROW_RANGE\\n        for cols in COL_RANGE\\n        if min_area <= rows * cols <= max_area\\n    ]\\n\\n\\ndef _scatter_pixels(rows: int, cols: int, colors: list[int], sides: list[int]) -> np.ndarray:\\n    grid = np.full((rows, cols), BG_COLOR, dtype=int)\\n    all_positions = [(r, c) for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols)]\\n    random.shuffle(all_positions)\\n\\n    idx = 0\\n    for color, side in zip(colors, sides):\\n        count = side * side\\n        for _ in range(count):\\n            r, c = all_positions[idx]\\n            grid[r, c] = color\\n            idx += 1\\n    return grid\\n\\n\\ndef _expected_output(colors: list[int], sides: list[int]) -> np.ndarray:\\n    ordered = sorted(zip(colors, sides), key=lambda x: x[1])\\n    height = max(sides)\\n    width = sum(sides) + len(sides) - 1\\n    expected = np.full((height, width), BG_COLOR, dtype=int)\\n    col = 0\\n    for i, (color, side) in enumerate(ordered):\\n        expected[height - side:height, col:col + side] = color\\n        col += side\\n        if i != len(ordered) - 1:\\n            col += 1\\n    return expected\\n\\n\\ndef _gen_attempt() -> np.ndarray | None:\\n    colors, sides = _sample_groups()\\n    total_pixels = sum(s * s for s in sides)\\n    valid_dims = _valid_dimensions(total_pixels)\\n    if not valid_dims:\\n        return None\\n\\n    rows, cols = random.choice(valid_dims)\\n    grid = _scatter_pixels(rows, cols, colors, sides)\\n\\n    try:\\n        output = main(grid)\\n    except (AssertionError, Exception):\\n        return None\\n\\n    if not np.array_equal(output, _expected_output(colors, sides)):\\n        return None\\n\\n    return grid\\n\\n\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\n    for _ in range(MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS):\\n        result = _gen_attempt()\\n        if result is not None:\\n            return result\\n    raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Failed to generate valid input after {MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS} attempts\\\")\\nFILE /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/aaecdb9a.py\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Convert scattered foreground objects into bottom-aligned count bars in a fixed five-color order.\\n\\n    Input structure\\n    The grid has a dominant background color and foreground objects in the task\\n    palette: grey, red, teal, maroon, and pink. Objects are monochromatic\\n    8-connected components; some palette colors may be absent.\\n\\n    Rule\\n    For each palette color in order grey, red, teal, maroon, pink, count its\\n    8-connected objects. Create a background grid with five columns and height\\n    equal to the largest count, then fill each column upward from the bottom\\n    with its palette color for that count.\\n\\n    Key insight\\n    The output does not preserve object shapes or positions; it is a histogram\\n    of per-color 8-connected object counts, using the learned palette order.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\n    assert g.ndim == 2\\n\\n    bg = get_bg(g)\\n    palette_set = set(PALETTE_ORDER)\\n    assert bg not in palette_set, \\\"background must not be a histogram color\\\"\\n    assert set(map(int, g.ravel())) <= palette_set | {bg}\\n\\n    object_counts = [len(components_mask(g == color, connectivity=8)) for color in PALETTE_ORDER]\\n    max_count = max(object_counts)\\n    assert max_count > 0, \\\"expected at least one foreground object\\\"\\n\\n    out = np.full((max_count, len(PALETTE_ORDER)), bg, dtype=int)\\n    for c, (color, count) in enumerate(zip(PALETTE_ORDER, object_counts)):\\n        if count:\\n            out[-count:, c] = color\\n    return out\\n\\n# --------------- generator (att1) ---------------\\n\\n# Canvas and palette.\\nGRID_SHAPE = (10, 10)\\nBACKGROUND_COLOR = Color.ORANGE\\nN_COLORS = len(PALETTE_ORDER)\\n\\n# Histogram count sampling.\\nNONZERO_COLOR_RANGE = (3, 6)\\nMAX_COUNT_RANGE = (2, 7)\\nTOTAL_OBJECT_RANGE = (4, 12)\\n\\n# Blob shape sampling.\\nN_BLOB_SHAPES = 6\\nLINE_LENGTH_RANGE = (2, 5)\\nSMALL_DIM_RANGE = (2, 4)\\nGROWN_BLOB_MIN_SIZE = 3\\nPLUS_SHAPE_SIZE = 3\\n\\n# Placement and retry limits.\\nSAME_COLOR_MIN_CHEBYSHEV = 2\\nBLOB_PLACE_TRIES = 100\\nGENERATION_TRIES = 300\\n\\n\\ndef _gen_attempt() -> np.ndarray | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Generate one candidate grid, returning None when placement or validation fails.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    rng = np.random.default_rng()\\n    counts = _sample_counts(rng)\\n    if counts is None:\\n        return None\\n\\n    grid = np.full(GRID_SHAPE, BACKGROUND_COLOR, dtype=int)\\n    if not _place_all_blobs(grid, counts, rng):\\n        return None\\n    if not _counts_match_grid(grid, counts):\\n        return None\\n    if not _solver_matches_expected(grid, counts):\\n        return None\\n    return grid\\n\\n\\ndef _sample_counts(rng) -> list[int] | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Sample per-color component counts matching the output histogram contract.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    n_nonzero = int(rng.integers(*NONZERO_COLOR_RANGE))\\n    max_count = int(rng.integers(*MAX_COUNT_RANGE))\\n\\n    counts = [0] * N_COLORS\\n    nonzero_indices = list(rng.choice(N_COLORS, size=n_nonzero, replace=False))\\n    max_idx = rng.choice(nonzero_indices)\\n    counts[max_idx] = max_count\\n\\n    remaining_budget = TOTAL_OBJECT_RANGE[1] - max_count\\n    for idx in [i for i in nonzero_indices if i != max_idx]:\\n        upper = min(max_count, remaining_budget)\\n        if upper < 1:\\n            counts[idx] = 1\\n            remaining_budget -= 1\\n        else:\\n            counts[idx] = int(rng.integers(1, upper + 1))\\n            remaining_budget -= counts[idx]\\n\\n    total = sum(counts)\\n    if total < TOTAL_OBJECT_RANGE[0] or total > TOTAL_OBJECT_RANGE[1]:\\n        return None\\n    return counts\\n\\n\\ndef _place_all_blobs(grid: np.ndarray, counts: list[int], rng) -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Place each color's requested number of same-color-separated blobs.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    for color_idx, count in enumerate(counts):\\n        if count == 0:\\n            continue\\n        if not _place_color_blobs(grid, PALETTE_ORDER[color_idx], count, rng):\\n            return False\\n    return True\\n\\n\\ndef _place_color_blobs(grid: np.ndarray, color: int, count: int, rng) -> bool:\\n    placed_blobs = []\\n    for _ in range(count):\\n        coords = _choose_placeable_blob(grid, placed_blobs, rng)\\n        if coords is None:\\n            return False\\n        _paint_coords(grid, coords, color)\\n        placed_blobs.append(coords)\\n    return True\\n\\n\\ndef _choose_placeable_blob(grid: np.ndarray, placed_blobs: list[set], rng) -> set | None:\\n    for _ in range(BLOB_PLACE_TRIES):\\n        blob = _random_blob(rng)\\n        bh, bw = blob.shape\\n        r0 = int(rng.integers(0, GRID_SHAPE[0] - bh + 1))\\n        c0 = int(rng.integers(0, GRID_SHAPE[1] - bw + 1))\\n        coords = _offset_blob_coords(blob, r0, c0)\\n        if _coords_are_free(grid, coords) and _chebyshev_ok(coords, placed_blobs):\\n            return coords\\n    return None\\n\\n\\ndef _offset_blob_coords(blob: np.ndarray, r0: int, c0: int) -> set:\\n    offsets = np.argwhere(blob)\\n    return set(map(tuple, offsets + np.array([r0, c0])))\\n\\n\\ndef _coords_are_free(grid: np.ndarray, coords: set) -> bool:\\n    return all(grid[r, c] == BACKGROUND_COLOR for r, c in coords)\\n\\n\\ndef _paint_coords(grid: np.ndarray, coords: set, color: int) -> None:\\n    rr, cc = np.array(list(coords)).T\\n    grid[rr, cc] = color\\n\\n\\ndef _counts_match_grid(grid: np.ndarray, counts: list[int]) -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Recompute 8-connected components to reject accidental same-color merges.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    for color, expected_count in zip(PALETTE_ORDER, counts):\\n        mask = grid == color\\n        if expected_count == 0:\\n            if mask.any():\\n                return False\\n        elif len(components_mask(mask, connectivity=8)) != expected_count:\\n            return False\\n    return True\\n\\n\\ndef _solver_matches_expected(grid: np.ndarray, counts: list[int]) -> bool:\\n    try:\\n        out = main(grid)\\n    except Exception:\\n        return False\\n    return np.array_equal(out, _expected_output(counts))\\n\\n\\ndef _expected_output(counts: list[int]) -> np.ndarray:\\n    out = np.full((max(counts), N_COLORS), BACKGROUND_COLOR, dtype=int)\\n    for c_idx, (color, count) in enumerate(zip(PALETTE_ORDER, counts)):\\n        if count:\\n            out[-count:, c_idx] = color\\n    return out\\n\\n\\ndef _random_blob(rng) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Generate a random small 8-connected blob mask.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    shape_type = rng.integers(0, N_BLOB_SHAPES)\\n\\n    if shape_type == 0:\\n        return np.array([[True]])\\n    elif shape_type == 1:\\n        length = int(rng.integers(*LINE_LENGTH_RANGE))\\n        return np.ones((1, length), dtype=bool)\\n    elif shape_type == 2:\\n        length = int(rng.integers(*LINE_LENGTH_RANGE))\\n        return np.ones((length, 1), dtype=bool)\\n    elif shape_type == 3:\\n        return _random_grown_blob(rng)\\n    elif shape_type == 4:\\n        return _plus_blob()\\n    else:\\n        h = int(rng.integers(*SMALL_DIM_RANGE))\\n        w = int(rng.integers(*SMALL_DIM_RANGE))\\n        return np.ones((h, w), dtype=bool)\\n\\n\\ndef _random_grown_blob(rng) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Grow a small mask by repeatedly adding an 8-neighbor of existing pixels.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    h = int(rng.integers(*SMALL_DIM_RANGE))\\n    w = int(rng.integers(*SMALL_DIM_RANGE))\\n    mask = np.zeros((h, w), dtype=bool)\\n    mask[0, 0] = True\\n    pixels = [(0, 0)]\\n    target_size = int(rng.integers(GROWN_BLOB_MIN_SIZE, h * w + 1))\\n    for _ in range(target_size - 1):\\n        candidates = _growth_candidates(mask, pixels)\\n        if not candidates:\\n            break\\n        pick = list(candidates)[int(rng.integers(0, len(candidates)))]\\n        mask[pick[0], pick[1]] = True\\n        pixels.append(pick)\\n    return mask\\n\\n\\ndef _growth_candidates(mask: np.ndarray, pixels: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> set:\\n    h, w = mask.shape\\n    candidates = set()\\n    for r, c in pixels:\\n        for dr in range(-1, 2):\\n            for dc in range(-1, 2):\\n                if dr == 0 and dc == 0:\\n                    continue\\n                nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\\n                if 0 <= nr < h and 0 <= nc < w and not mask[nr, nc]:\\n                    candidates.add((nr, nc))\\n    return candidates\\n\\n\\ndef _plus_blob() -> np.ndarray:\\n    mask = np.zeros((PLUS_SHAPE_SIZE, PLUS_SHAPE_SIZE), dtype=bool)\\n    center = PLUS_SHAPE_SIZE // 2\\n    mask[center, :] = True\\n    mask[:, center] = True\\n    return mask\\n\\n\\ndef _chebyshev_ok(new_coords: set, existing_blobs: list) -> bool:\\n    for blob in existing_blobs:\\n        for r1, c1 in new_coords:\\n            for r2, c2 in blob:\\n                if max(abs(r1 - r2), abs(c1 - c2)) < SAME_COLOR_MIN_CHEBYSHEV:\\n                    return False\\n    return True\\n\\n\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\n    for _ in range(GENERATION_TRIES):\\n        result = _gen_attempt()\\n        if result is not None:\\n            return result\\n    raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Failed to generate valid input after {GENERATION_TRIES} attempts\\\")\\nFILE /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/58490d8a.py\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Count colored objects and record tallies inside a legend box.\\n\\n    Input structure:\\n    - A black rectangular legend box with key-color pixels in its leftmost non-black column.\\n    - Outside the box, distinct objects of each key color are scattered across the grid.\\n\\n    Rule:\\n    - For each key color, count separate same-colored objects outside the legend box.\\n    - Output the legend box repainted: each key row gets one dot per object, spaced every other cell rightward from the key pixel.\\n\\n    Key insight: The legend is both the color index and the output canvas — object counts become dot sequences on the matching row.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\\n    H, W = g.shape\\n    _bg = int(get_bg(g))\\n\\n    black = 0\\n\\n    # STEP 1) Find the legend bbox: largest black CC whose bbox contains some non-black pixels.\\n    best = None  # (area, bbox)\\n    for coords in components_mask(g == int(black), connectivity=8):\\n        if coords.size == 0:\\n            continue\\n        b = bbox_coords(coords)\\n        sub = crop_bbox(g, b)\\n        if (sub != int(black)).any():\\n            area = int(coords.shape[0])\\n            cand = (area, tuple(map(int, b)))\\n            if best is None or cand[0] > best[0]:\\n                best = cand\\n\\n    assert not (best is None)\\n\\n    r0, c0, r1, c1 = map(int, best[1])\\n    box = crop_bbox(g, (r0, c0, r1, c1))\\n    bh, bw = map(int, box.shape)\\n\\n    # STEP 2) Inside the legend bbox, find the key column:\\n    # leftmost column with any non-black pixels (the \\\"key pixels\\\").\\n    key_col = None\\n    for cc in range(bw):\\n        if (box[:, int(cc)] != int(black)).any():\\n            key_col = int(cc)\\n            break\\n    if key_col is None:\\n        return np.zeros_like(box)\\n\\n    keys = [(int(rr), int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)])) for rr in range(bh) if int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)]) != int(black)]\\n    keys.sort(key=lambda t: int(t[0]))\\n\\n    outside = np.ones((H, W), dtype=bool)\\n    outside[int(r0) : int(r1) + 1, int(c0) : int(c1) + 1] = False\\n    out = np.zeros((bh, bw), dtype=int)\\n\\n    # STEP 3/4) Count CCs of each key color outside the legend, then draw 1 dot per CC.\\n    for rr, col in keys:\\n        mask = (g == int(col)) & outside\\n        _labc, nc = label_mask(mask, connectivity=8)\\n        for i in range(int(nc)):\\n            cc = int(key_col + 2 * i)\\n            if 0 <= cc < bw:\\n                out[int(rr), int(cc)] = int(col)\\n\\n    return out\\n\\n# --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\\n\\n# Palette and legend color choices.\\nCOLOR_POOL = tuple(range(1, 10))\\nBLACK = 0\\nDISTRACTOR_PROB = 0.5\\n\\n# Key rows and tally dimensions.\\nKEY_COUNT_RANGE = (2, 4)\\nTARGET_COUNT_RANGE = (1, 5)\\nKEY_ROW_FIRST = 1\\nKEY_ROW_STEP = 2\\nKEY_COLUMN = 1\\nTALLY_COL_STEP = 2\\nLEGEND_HEIGHT_TAIL = 1\\nLEGEND_WIDTH_TAIL = 1\\nLEGEND_SLACK_RANGE = (0, 3)\\n\\n# Canvas size and legend placement bounds.\\nGRID_HEIGHT_RANGE = (20, 25)\\nGRID_WIDTH_RANGE = (20, 25)\\nLEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN = 2\\n\\n# Sprite shape and placement constraints.\\nSPRITE_AREA_RANGE = (4, 7)\\nSPRITE_BBOXES = ((2, 2), (2, 3), (3, 2), (3, 3))\\nSPRITE_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\nSPRITE_PADDING = 1\\nSPRITE_PADDING_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\n\\n# Retry budget for rejection sampling.\\nGENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\\n\\n\\ndef _randint(bounds: tuple[int, int]) -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return an inclusive randint from a configured (low, high) pair.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return random.randint(bounds[0], bounds[1])\\n\\n\\n@lru_cache(maxsize=None)\\ndef _valid_masks(h: int, w: int, area: int) -> tuple[np.ndarray, ...]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return connected masks that span all four sides of the sprite bbox.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    masks = []\\n    for cells in combinations(range(h * w), area):\\n        mask = np.zeros((h, w), dtype=bool)\\n        for cell in cells:\\n            mask[cell // w, cell % w] = True\\n        spans_edges = mask[0, :].any() and mask[-1, :].any() and mask[:, 0].any() and mask[:, -1].any()\\n        if not spans_edges:\\n            continue\\n        _, n = label_mask(mask, connectivity=SPRITE_CONNECTIVITY)\\n        if n == 1:\\n            masks.append(mask)\\n    return tuple(masks)\\n\\n\\ndef _make_sprite(color: int, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Sample one connected same-color sprite drawn on the background color.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    area = _randint(SPRITE_AREA_RANGE)\\n    dims = []\\n    for h, w in SPRITE_BBOXES:\\n        if h * w >= area and _valid_masks(h, w, area):\\n            dims.append((h, w))\\n    h, w = random.choice(dims)\\n    mask = random.choice(_valid_masks(h, w, area))\\n    sprite = np.full((h, w), int(bg), dtype=int)\\n    sprite[mask] = int(color)\\n    return sprite\\n\\n\\ndef _sample_palette() -> tuple[int, list[int], int | None]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Choose background, key colors, and optional distractor color.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    colors = list(COLOR_POOL)\\n    bg = random.choice(colors)\\n\\n    k = _randint(KEY_COUNT_RANGE)\\n    remaining = [c for c in colors if c != bg]\\n    key_colors = random.sample(remaining, k)\\n    remaining = [c for c in remaining if c not in key_colors]\\n    distractor_color = random.choice(remaining) if remaining and random.random() < DISTRACTOR_PROB else None\\n    return bg, key_colors, distractor_color\\n\\n\\ndef _sample_counts(k: int) -> list[int]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Sample the target outside-component count for each key color.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return [_randint(TARGET_COUNT_RANGE) for _ in range(k)]\\n\\n\\ndef _legend_shape(k: int, max_count: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return legend height and width for the key count and largest tally.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    bh = KEY_ROW_STEP * k + LEGEND_HEIGHT_TAIL\\n    bw = TALLY_COL_STEP * max_count + LEGEND_WIDTH_TAIL + _randint(LEGEND_SLACK_RANGE)\\n    return bh, bw\\n\\n\\ndef _key_row(i: int) -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Map a zero-based key index to its row inside the legend/output box.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return KEY_ROW_FIRST + KEY_ROW_STEP * i\\n\\n\\ndef _build_expected(key_colors: list[int], counts: list[int]) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Render the black output tally canvas implied by key colors and counts.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    max_count = max(counts)\\n    bh, bw = _legend_shape(len(key_colors), max_count)\\n\\n    expected = np.full((bh, bw), BLACK, dtype=int)\\n    for i, (color, count) in enumerate(zip(key_colors, counts)):\\n        rr = _key_row(i)\\n        for j in range(count):\\n            expected[rr, KEY_COLUMN + TALLY_COL_STEP * j] = int(color)\\n    return expected\\n\\n\\ndef _build_legend(shape: tuple[int, int], key_colors: list[int]) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return a black legend patch with only the key-column pixels filled.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    legend = np.full(shape, BLACK, dtype=int)\\n    for i, color in enumerate(key_colors):\\n        legend[_key_row(i), KEY_COLUMN] = int(color)\\n    return legend\\n\\n\\ndef _new_grid_with_legend(bg: int, legend: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Sample a grid and paste the legend away from all canvas edges.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    bh, bw = map(int, legend.shape)\\n    H = _randint(GRID_HEIGHT_RANGE)\\n    W = _randint(GRID_WIDTH_RANGE)\\n    min_h = bh + 2 * LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN\\n    min_w = bw + 2 * LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN\\n    if H < min_h or W < min_w:\\n        return None\\n\\n    grid = np.full((H, W), int(bg), dtype=int)\\n    r0 = random.randint(LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN, H - bh - LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN)\\n    c0 = random.randint(LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN, W - bw - LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN)\\n    paste(grid, legend, r0, c0)\\n    return grid\\n\\n\\ndef _build_sprite_queue(\\n    key_colors: list[int],\\n    counts: list[int],\\n    distractor_color: int | None,\\n    bg: int,\\n) -> list[np.ndarray]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Create canonical key sprites, optional distractor sprite, and shuffle them.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    sprites = []\\n    for color, count in zip(key_colors, counts):\\n        sprite = _make_sprite(color, bg)\\n        for _ in range(count):\\n            sprites.append(sprite.copy())\\n    if distractor_color is not None:\\n        sprites.append(_make_sprite(distractor_color, bg))\\n    random.shuffle(sprites)\\n    return sprites\\n\\n\\ndef _place_sprites(grid: np.ndarray, sprites: list[np.ndarray], bg: int) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Paste sprites into random non-touching free locations in queue order.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    for sprite in sprites:\\n        sr, sc = random_free_location(\\n            grid,\\n            sprite,\\n            transparent=bg,\\n            padding=SPRITE_PADDING,\\n            padding_connectivity=SPRITE_PADDING_CONNECTIVITY,\\n        )\\n        paste(grid, sprite, sr, sc, transparent=bg)\\n\\n\\ndef _gen_attempt() -> np.ndarray | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Run one output-first generation attempt and reject solver mismatches.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    bg, key_colors, distractor_color = _sample_palette()\\n    counts = _sample_counts(len(key_colors))\\n    expected = _build_expected(key_colors, counts)\\n    legend = _build_legend(expected.shape, key_colors)\\n    grid = _new_grid_with_legend(bg, legend)\\n    if grid is None:\\n        return None\\n\\n    sprites = _build_sprite_queue(key_colors, counts, distractor_color, bg)\\n    try:\\n        _place_sprites(grid, sprites, bg)\\n    except ValueError:\\n        return None\\n\\n    if not np.array_equal(main(grid), expected):\\n        return None\\n    return grid\\n\\n\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\n    for _ in range(GENERATION_ATTEMPTS):\\n        grid = _gen_attempt()\\n        if grid is not None:\\n            return grid\\n    raise RuntimeError(\\\"failed to generate a valid 58490d8a input\\\")\\nFILE /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/2ba387bc.py\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Sort scattered 4×4 squares into two columns by type: frames left, solids right.\\n\\n    Input structure:\\n    - bg = most common color. Multiple 4×4 objects on bg.\\n    - Frames: colored 1px border, bg-filled 2×2 interior.\\n    - Solids: entirely filled with one non-bg color.\\n\\n    Rule:\\n    - Classify each 4×4 object as frame or solid by its interior.\\n    - Sort each group top-to-bottom by input row.\\n    - Stack frames in left column (cols 0–3), solids in right (cols 4–7).\\n    - Output is 8 wide; height = 4 × max(#frames, #solids), bg-padded.\\n\\n    Key insight: Frame vs solid is determined solely by whether the 2×2 interior matches bg.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\\n    bg = int(get_bg(g))\\n\\n    comps = find_components(g, bg=bg, connectivity=4, monochromatic=False, return_format=\\\"dict\\\")\\n    frames: list[tuple[int, int, np.ndarray]] = []\\n    solids: list[tuple[int, int, np.ndarray]] = []\\n\\n    for comp in comps:\\n        b = comp[\\\"bbox\\\"]\\n        if bbox_h(b) != 4 or bbox_w(b) != 4:\\n            continue\\n        r0, c0, _r1, _c1 = b\\n        sub = crop_bbox(g, b)\\n\\n        border = np.concatenate([sub[0, :], sub[-1, :], sub[1:-1, 0], sub[1:-1, -1]])\\n        bcols = set(map(int, border.flatten()))\\n\\n        if len(bcols) == 1 and bool((sub[1:3, 1:3] == int(bg)).all()):\\n            frames.append((int(r0), int(c0), sub))\\n        else:\\n            solids.append((int(r0), int(c0), sub))\\n\\n    frames.sort(key=lambda t: (int(t[0]), int(t[1])))\\n    solids.sort(key=lambda t: (int(t[0]), int(t[1])))\\n\\n    outH = 4 * max(int(len(frames)), int(len(solids)))\\n    outW = 8\\n    out = np.full((outH, outW), int(bg), dtype=int)\\n\\n    for i, (_r0, _c0, sub) in enumerate(frames):\\n        paste(out, sub, int(i * 4), 0)\\n    for i, (_r0, _c0, sub) in enumerate(solids):\\n        paste(out, sub, int(i * 4), 4)\\n\\n    return out\\n\\n\\ndef _make_frame(col: int, bg: int = 0) -> np.ndarray:\\n    a = np.full((4, 4), col, dtype=int)\\n    a[1:3, 1:3] = bg\\n    return a\\n\\ndef _make_solid(col: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n    return np.full((4, 4), col, dtype=int)\\n\\ndef _gen_attempt() -> np.ndarray | None:\\n    bg = 0\\n    H = int(np.random.randint(18, 30))\\n    W = int(np.random.randint(18, 30))\\n    g = np.full((H, W), bg, dtype=int)\\n    n_frames = int(np.random.randint(1, 5))\\n    n_solids = int(np.random.randint(1, 5))\\n    try:\\n        used_cols: set[int] = set()\\n        for _ in range(n_frames):\\n            col = int(np.random.randint(1, 10))\\n            while col in used_cols:\\n                col = int(np.random.randint(1, 10))\\n            used_cols.add(col)\\n            r0, c0 = random_free_location(g, _make_frame(col, bg), transparent=bg, border=1, padding=1, padding_connectivity=4)\\n            paste(g, _make_frame(col, bg), r0, c0, transparent=bg)\\n        for _ in range(n_solids):\\n            col = int(np.random.randint(1, 10))\\n            while col in used_cols:\\n                col = int(np.random.randint(1, 10))\\n            used_cols.add(col)\\n            r0, c0 = random_free_location(g, _make_solid(col), transparent=bg, border=1, padding=1, padding_connectivity=4)\\n            paste(g, _make_solid(col), r0, c0, transparent=bg)\\n        return g\\n    except Exception:\\n        return None\\n\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\n    for _ in range(300):\\n        result = _gen_attempt()\\n        if result is not None:\\n            return result\\n    raise RuntimeError(\\\"generate_input failed after 300 attempts\\\")\\n\\n\\nFILE /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/2601afb7.py\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Rotate each vertical bar's color one slot right and its height one slot left.\\n\\n    Input structure\\n    - A dominant background surrounds several monochrome one-cell-wide vertical bars.\\n    - Every bar is bottom-aligned and occupies a distinct column.\\n    - The ordered bar slots are read from left to right.\\n\\n    Rule\\n    - Keep the grid shape and the bar columns unchanged.\\n    - At slot i, use the color from the previous slot cyclically.\\n    - At slot i, use the height from the next slot cyclically.\\n\\n    Key insight\\n    - Color and height are independent cyclic attributes of the ordered bar slots:\\n      colors rotate right while heights rotate left.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\n    height = g.shape[0]\\n    bg = get_bg(g)\\n    bars = _extract_bars(g, bg)\\n\\n    out = np.full_like(g, bg)\\n    count = len(bars)\\n    for i, bar in enumerate(bars):\\n        color = bars[(i - 1) % count][\\\"color\\\"]\\n        bar_height = bars[(i + 1) % count][\\\"height\\\"]\\n        assert 1 <= bar_height <= height\\n        out[height - bar_height : height, bar[\\\"col\\\"]] = color\\n\\n    return out\\n\\n# --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\\n\\n_RNG = np.random.default_rng()\\n\\n# Canvas/bar bounds.\\nBAR_COUNT_MIN, BAR_COUNT_MAX_EXCLUSIVE = 3, 6\\nBACKGROUND_COLOR, MIN_BAR_HEIGHT = 7, 1\\nBAR_COL_OFFSET, BAR_COL_STRIDE = 1, 2\\n# Color and transform sampling.\\nCOLOR_POOL = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9]\\nOUTPUT_COLOR_SHIFT, OUTPUT_HEIGHT_SHIFT = 1, -1\\n# Retry limit.\\nMAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\\n\\n\\ndef _render_bars(n: int, colors: np.ndarray, heights: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    side = BAR_COL_STRIDE * n + BAR_COL_OFFSET\\n    grid = np.full((side, side), BACKGROUND_COLOR, dtype=int)\\n    for i, (color, bar_height) in enumerate(zip(colors, heights)):\\n        col = BAR_COL_STRIDE * i + BAR_COL_OFFSET\\n        grid[side - int(bar_height) : side, col] = int(color)\\n    return grid\\n\\n\\ndef _expected_output(n: int, colors: np.ndarray, heights: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n    out_colors = np.roll(colors, OUTPUT_COLOR_SHIFT)\\n    out_heights = np.roll(heights, OUTPUT_HEIGHT_SHIFT)\\n    return _render_bars(n, out_colors, out_heights)\\n\\n\\ndef _gen_attempt() -> np.ndarray | None:\\n    n = int(_RNG.integers(BAR_COUNT_MIN, BAR_COUNT_MAX_EXCLUSIVE))\\n    side = BAR_COL_STRIDE * n + BAR_COL_OFFSET\\n    colors = _RNG.choice(COLOR_POOL, size=n, replace=False)\\n    heights = _RNG.integers(MIN_BAR_HEIGHT, side, size=n)\\n    if len(set(map(int, heights))) == 1:\\n        idx = int(_RNG.integers(n))\\n        choices = [h for h in range(MIN_BAR_HEIGHT, side) if h != int(heights[idx])]\\n        heights[idx] = int(_RNG.choice(choices))\\n\\n    grid = _render_bars(n, colors, heights)\\n    if np.array_equal(main(grid), _expected_output(n, colors, heights)):\\n        return grid\\n    return None\\n\\n\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\n    for _ in range(MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS):\\n        grid = _gen_attempt()\\n        if grid is not None:\\n            return grid\\n    raise RuntimeError(\\\"failed to generate valid input\\\")\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/comb